/* Life-area readings: each placement read through the page it appears on, so Mars in the
   10th reads as love on the love page and as energy on the health page (see CLAUDE.md). */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.areas = {
  "love:mars": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "Desire hits you fast and you act on it before you have finished thinking. You are the one who makes the first move, boldly and without a second thought, reaching out or leaning in long before the other person has even had a chance to decide what they want. Sexual energy is direct, playful and a little competitive, and a partner who pushes back keeps you interested far longer than one who always agrees. At your best you make love feel brave and alive, and people remember how openly you wanted them. The shadow is impatience: when the spark dips you pick a fight just to feel the heat again, or leave before anything has had time to grow. Staying, it turns out, can be as bold as chasing.",
      "taurus": "You pursue slowly and steadily, and once you want someone you rarely give up. Attraction runs through the senses: a voice, a scent, a touch, and time together that quietly stretches on for hours. You remember a lover's small preferences and meet them before they have to ask. Sex matters to you as sustained, unhurried pleasure rather than conquest, and at your best you make a partner feel utterly safe in their body. In conflict you dig in and go silent, sometimes for days, and possessiveness creeps in when you sense a partner slipping away. What is meant to last tends to stay without being held so tightly.",
      "gemini": "Flirting is your foreplay. You chase with words: quick wit that makes them laugh, running jokes only the two of you understand, and messages you simply cannot wait to send. A mind that surprises you turns you on faster than looks alone, and you lose interest in someone who never asks a question back. Variety keeps desire alive, so new places, new conversations and a bit of play in the bedroom matter. At your best you make a partner feel endlessly interesting. Arguments become verbal sparring matches you are determined to win, and restlessness pulls your eye towards someone new when things feel routine. The best of your love life begins as a conversation neither of you wants to end.",
      "cancer": "Your desire is bound up with feeling safe, so you rarely pursue head on. Instead you look after someone, noticing their needs, checking they are all right and remembering every detail of their life, and wait for them to notice what all that care means. Intimacy deepens once trust exists, and sex becomes an expression of emotional closeness rather than a performance. Loved back, you are fiercely protective and tender, the lover who makes a partner feel held. When hurt, you sulk or needle rather than say it straight, and you can bring up something from three arguments ago in the middle of this one. Things go far better when you say what you want before resentment says it for you.",
      "leo": "Pursuit, for you, is grand, warm and unmistakable. You make grand gestures, give compliments generously and let someone know, for everyone to see, just how wonderful you find them. Being desired matters as much as desiring, so a partner who looks at you with open admiration lights you up for days. In bed you are playful, confident and generous. Pride is the weak spot: a careless remark about your appearance, or a partner's attention wandering elsewhere, can turn into a dramatic standoff, and you hate being the one who apologises first. With a partner who adores you back, you make love feel like a celebration, and the sweetest version of you loves wholeheartedly even when nobody is watching.",
      "virgo": "Attention to detail is how your desire shows. You notice what someone needs and quietly take care of it before they ask, because paying close attention is how you show you care. Pursuit is careful, even cautious, because you want to be sure before you spend your energy on anyone. Sexually you become more skilled and uninhibited with a trusted partner, and you take pride in getting things right. Arguments are where it sours, since criticism becomes your weapon: a small irritation stands in for the bigger grievance you have not named. Once you trust someone, you are devoted in a quietly practical way, and you soften a great deal when you accept that neither of you has to be perfect.",
      "libra": "Charm, courtesy and a sense of occasion are your tools of seduction, and you like romance to feel elegant and mutual. Often you wait to be chosen, or you steer things so skilfully that the other person believes the first move was their idea. Desire is stirred by beauty, good manners and a partner who meets you as an equal. When the match is right, you make someone feel perfectly paired and appreciated. Open conflict unsettles you, so anger comes out as coolness, a polite 'it's fine', or endless indecision about whether to stay. You can remain in something too long to avoid a scene. An honest row, cleanly resolved, often leaves your relationships stronger rather than uglier.",
      "scorpio": "Casual does not come easily to you. When you want someone you want all of them, and your pursuit is patient, magnetic and quietly intense: a long, steady look that says more than any words. Sex is a form of bonding and power exchange, and you are drawn to partners with depth, secrets or an edge of danger. You notice the tiny hesitation that gives away what someone would rather keep hidden. Once someone has earned your trust, you offer loyalty and passion that few people ever experience. The shadow is jealousy and control: you test loyalty, hold grudges for years, or turn cold and strategic when you feel betrayed. Closeness comes when you let yourself be known as fully as you want to know them.",
      "sagittarius": "Love is an adventure you chase, and you are drawn to people who bring something new, bold and unfamiliar into your life. Romance with you moves quickly towards shared plans and new horizons, and attraction often strikes when you least expect it. Honest, enthusiastic and often funny, you pursue openly and hate games. Freedom is essential, so a partner who tries to pin you down too quickly sets off your urge to bolt. In arguments you are bluntly tactless, saying the true thing in the worst possible way, then wondering why they are still upset. The partner who travels with you, literally and in spirit, gets the best of you: a love that feels expansive and hopeful, with the adventure happening inside the commitment rather than outside it.",
      "capricorn": "A serious relationship, to you, is a long-term project worth building properly, and you pursue it with purpose and patience. Competence and ambition attract you, and you are often drawn to someone older, established or visibly going somewhere. You approach romance with the same care you give your work, and quietly check whether this person fits the life you intend to have. Sexually you are more earthy and enduring than your reserved manner suggests. Committed, you are the dependable partner who delivers on every promise. The difficulty is emotional control: you treat vulnerability as weakness, retreat into work in the middle of an argument, and go stonily quiet rather than admit you are hurt. Softness, for you, is a strength still being learned.",
      "aquarius": "Attraction starts for you in the head and in friendship, and you often fall for someone you have known for months as a mate. You can realise you are in love halfway through a heated debate about ideas. You want a lover who is also an equal and an original, and conventional romantic scripts, the gestures everyone is expected to make, leave you cold. Experimentation and unusual arrangements interest you more than they would most people. The love you offer respects a partner's freedom completely. When things get emotionally heavy you detach, argue from principle rather than feeling, and seem distant just when a partner needs closeness. A partner who can talk about feelings as easily as ideas feels like home to you.",
      "pisces": "Longing moves in you like a tide, rising with mood, music and fantasy rather than plans. You pursue indirectly, drifting closer and hoping they read the signals, and you can dwell for days on a single moment that reminds you of them. Sex feels best when it is tender and merging, almost spiritual, and you respond acutely to a partner's feelings. Yours is a compassionate, imaginative love that makes someone feel completely understood. The shadow is passivity and escapism: you avoid confrontation, idealise people who are unavailable, and let resentment leak out sideways instead of saying what you want. Desire acted on in the real world, not only in the daydream, is where your love life starts."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "Your physical presence, energy and directness are a large part of your sex appeal, and you come on strong without even trying. People know within minutes whether you fancy them, because it shows in your eyes, your stance and how close you stand. You make the first move and show attraction openly, often through teasing or a bit of friendly competition. Nobody has to guess what you want from them, and that frankness is magnetic. The downside is a short fuse and a me-first reflex: fights flare quickly over small things, and you can steamroll a quieter partner before you notice they have gone silent. Slowing to the other person's pace is where your passion finds its staying power.",
      "2": "Desire for you is tied to touch, comfort and keeping what you have. You pursue someone the way you would acquire something precious: steadily, and with every intention of holding on. Gifts, good food and shared pleasures are your language of seduction, and you win hearts through comfort and generosity rather than grand words. You want sex to be unhurried and sensual. You give a partner a deep sense of physical security. Money becomes a flashpoint, with arguments over who paid for what, and jealousy flares when you feel what is yours is under threat. Cherishing someone and owning them are different things, and the difference matters in every relationship you have.",
      "3": "Talk is where your chase happens. You flirt through banter and debate, and a sharp exchange of words can arouse you more than any romantic setting. Romance often starts close to home, with someone who is already part of your everyday world. You polish your words carefully so that the joke lands perfectly. Your relationships stay lively and mentally electric for years. In fights you argue fast and sharply, and you can win the point while losing the mood by treating an emotional disagreement as a debate. The tender thing said plainly lands deeper than the clever one.",
      "4": "Passion shows most at home and in private, where you drop your public composure. You want to build a nest with a partner, and you are fiercely protective of the relationship and family you make together. Sexual intimacy is tied to emotional security and having your own space, so nowhere feels as intimate as the place you call home. You defend the people you love like a lion. The harder side is domestic friction: anger swallowed elsewhere comes out at home over something trivial, and old family patterns of shouting or stonewalling replay in your relationships. Many of your fiercest rows turn out to be about the past rather than the person in front of you.",
      "5": "Romance fires you up, and you pursue with flair, playfulness and loud enthusiasm. You love the chase, the dating, the flirtation and those first thrilling weeks when every message makes your heart race. Sex for you is a form of fun and self-expression, and confident, lively people who can play along attract you most. You are happy to make a fool of yourself for love, and you do it with total, unembarrassed delight. You bring joy and daring to love. The risk is chasing the high: when the drama fades you go looking for a new spark, or create conflict to keep the romance vivid. The play belongs in a long relationship as much as at its start, and you are capable of keeping it there.",
      "6": "Doing things is how you show desire: practical help, small acts of care and turning up when it counts. Love for you is practical and daily, and romance often starts at work or through a shared routine that brings you together again and again. You need a partner who pulls their weight. You are the reliable, hands-on lover who makes life easier. Irritation is your usual form of conflict: bickering over chores, or a sigh at how they insist on doing things their way. Passion fades when you turn a partner into a project to improve. Desire thrives when it is about pleasure, not only usefulness.",
      "7": "Partnership switches your energy on, and you are drawn to assertive, forceful or competitive people. You pursue relationships actively, even impulsively, and you want someone who challenges you rather than agreeing with everything. The same fire that attracts also clashes: arguments are frequent and heated, sometimes flaring over nothing and ending in a standoff. You tend to choose partners who act out the anger you do not fully own yourself. The partnerships you build are full of energy, loyalty and honest engagement. Fair fighting is the skill that turns conflict into a sharper bond instead of a slow wearing away.",
      "8": "Sexual chemistry decides whether a relationship works for you, and you want intensity, not politeness, behind closed doors. You are drawn to magnetic, secretive or powerful people, and you pursue with quiet determination until you break through their defences. You are the one who knows, from a single kiss, whether this will go anywhere. Once trust is won, you offer passion and loyalty of rare depth. Where it goes wrong is control: jealousy and suspicion take over when trust is shaky, and you can analyse a moment's silence for hours. Fights turn cutting because you know precisely where a partner is most vulnerable. The deepest nights come when you surrender without needing to win.",
      "9": "Distance and difference excite you. You are drawn to people from other cultures, countries or belief systems, and romance often sparks through a meeting of minds and a shared hunger for the wider world. Distance rarely puts you off, and you will go to great lengths for someone who widens your world. You pursue with enthusiasm and candour, and you need a partner who wants adventure too. Love with you becomes a shared journey of discovery. Conflict centres on principles, and you preach or insist you are right, turning a small disagreement into a moral debate. A partner's truth can sit alongside your own without either of you losing.",
      "10": "Ambition is attractive to you, and you are drawn to accomplished, driven people or those with standing in their field. Desire is stirred by respect: watching someone excel at what they do can make you fall for them on the spot. You want a partner you can be proud of in public, and romance often begins through work. Any relationship has to make room for your goals, and with the right match you and a partner become a formidable team. The friction comes when careers compete, with power struggles over whose plans come first, or a partner who feels second to your job. The relationship deserves the same best energy you give to your work.",
      "11": "Love often grows out of friendship for you, with someone from your wider circle or someone who shares your ideals. You pursue as a comrade first, and attraction often sneaks up on you while working side by side towards something you both care about. Shared ideals and a sense of fun matter as much as chemistry, and independence stays important even in commitment. You and a partner can feel like allies against the world. The catch is detachment or rebellion: you resist anything that looks like conventional coupledom, and friction arises when a partner feels less important than your social life. Sooner or later one person comes to matter more than the group, and that is where your love deepens.",
      "12": "Desire operates in secret for you. You are slow to show interest openly, and you can carry a crush for months, quietly watching and wondering, without ever acting on it. Sometimes you find yourself pulled into hidden or complicated affairs. Your sexuality has a dreamy, fantasy-rich side that you share only with someone you trust completely, and in that safety you bring a compassionate, almost spiritual quality to intimacy. Anger gets suppressed, so it leaks out as passive resistance or quiet withdrawal, and you are drawn to people who seem to need rescuing. Wanting brought into the open is wanting that can be met."
    }
  },
  "love:venus": {
    "house": {
      "1": "Love tends to find you through your own presence. People notice your looks, charm or style and are drawn to you far more often than you realise, and interest tends to come your way without you seeking it. You want a relationship that lets you be fully yourself and feel attractive. Being liked comes easily, which makes flirting feel natural rather than effortful, and you put people at ease the moment you smile. The risk is a need for constant affirmation, and you notice straight away when a partner stops commenting on how you look. You can mistake being admired for being known. The love that satisfies you most values who you are, not only how you appear.",
      "2": "Shared pleasures and steady, tangible gestures are how love reaches you. You want stability, loyalty and a partner who shows care in concrete ways, through comfort, generosity and time together that is never rushed. You remember the dates that matter, and your gifts are chosen with real thought. Your own affection comes through touch and generosity, and you make a relationship feel abundant and grounded. You value what lasts, so you are slow to let go even when you should. The trap is confusing material comfort with emotional security, and staying for the house or the routine. Knowing your own worth leads you to partners who match it.",
      "3": "Romance comes to you through conversation. Easy, everyday exchanges are where attraction sparks, and a witty, curious mind charms you instantly. The way someone uses words can win you over before anything else about them does. You want a partner you can talk to endlessly, who keeps things light and shares whatever they know will delight you. With a partner who talks back, a relationship feels like a lifelong conversation. Flirting is second nature, which makes you seem more available than you are, and your interest drifts once the talk dries up. Words lead you into love, and depth is what keeps you there.",
      "4": "Close to home is where love finds you, through family, old friends or someone who makes a room feel like a sanctuary. You want a partner to build a domestic life with, a shared home that welcomes and holds the people you love. You know you are falling for someone when you start picturing them as part of your family. Emotional safety is the heart of romance for you, and you can create a home that feels like a warm embrace. The weak spot is looking for a parent figure in a partner, or retreating into cosiness to avoid the risks intimacy asks. The home you want is one where both of you still have room to grow.",
      "5": "Love tends to find you when you are enjoying yourself and your playful, creative side is on show. You adore courtship and grand gestures, and you want a relationship full of play, affection and appreciation. You light up planning a romantic surprise, and you glow when someone does the same for you. Falling in love comes easily and feels wonderful, and you make a partner feel like the most delightful person alive. The difficulty is that you love the thrill of being in love more than the person, and ordinary life feels like a letdown after the honeymoon. Romance kept alive through years, not only weeks, is the prize.",
      "6": "Work, a shared routine or everyday service are the usual doorways to love for you, often with someone you see again and again. You want a partner who shows up in practical ways, and you express love by looking after daily needs. Small rituals of care matter enormously to you, and you remember exactly how the person you love likes things done. You are a caring, devoted partner whose love is visible in a hundred small acts. The danger is sliding into a caretaking role with too little romance, or being overly critical of a partner's flaws. Being looked after as generously as you look after others feels strange at first, and then wonderful.",
      "7": "Love finds you readily through introductions, social events and one-to-one encounters, and partnership sits at the centre of your life. You want a committed, harmonious relationship with someone refined, fair and good company. You rarely stay single for long, and you love bringing other people together too. Generous, gracious and devoted, you find your happiness in a long-term bond. What trips you up is dependence: you feel incomplete alone, compromise too much to keep the peace, or rush into commitment rather than face being on your own. Your happiest partnerships are chosen from wholeness, not from the fear of being single.",
      "8": "Intense, transformative encounters are how love arrives for you, rather than light flirtation. You want depth, sexual chemistry and total emotional honesty, and a relationship for you means merging lives, secrets and often finances. You can meet someone and feel, almost at once, that your life is about to change. Attraction can feel fated and consuming, and you offer a love of rare loyalty and depth. The cost is possessiveness, and being drawn into bonds that feel powerful precisely because they are dangerous. What you are seeking is an intimacy that transforms you without destroying you.",
      "9": "Far from your usual world is where love tends to find you, often with someone from a very different background or way of life. You want a partner who expands your mind and shares your appetite for adventure and meaning. Your best love stories tend to begin somewhere unlikely, with someone you would never have expected. Shared beliefs, big conversations and travel draw you closer, and your relationships feel like a joyful education. What can go wrong is idealising the exotic or the distant, then losing interest once the relationship becomes local, familiar and everyday. Finding wonder in someone you see every day is the quieter adventure.",
      "10": "Your career and public life are common meeting grounds for love, and partners often appear through work or professional networks. You want someone admired, accomplished or socially respected, and a relationship you can proudly present to the world. You notice how a partner carries themselves in public, and it matters to you more than you admit. Your charm helps your reputation, and you and a partner raise each other up. The pitfall is choosing partners for image or status, or letting the relationship become part of your public persona rather than a private refuge. A bond that feels as good behind closed doors as it looks in public is the one worth keeping.",
      "11": "Friendship is the doorway to love for you. Romance often begins within a social circle, a community or an online group, and you want a partner who is also your best friend. Many of your relationships grow slowly out of a long, easy friendship before either of you names it. Shared ideals, freedom and equality matter more than traditional romance, and you create partnerships that feel like true alliances. The downside is keeping things too casual or too friendly to risk rejection, or feeling torn between a partner and the wider group. Some of your best love stories start the moment a friendship tips into something more.",
      "12": "Hidden or unexpected places are where love finds you, through secret feelings, soulful connections and bonds that grow quietly out of sight. You want a love that feels soulful and selfless, and you give quietly and generously. You have kept a feeling to yourself for so long that the other person never knew. Your love has a compassionate, almost sacred quality. Trouble arrives through martyrdom or secrecy: you fall for unavailable people, stay loyal to someone who does not deserve it, or keep your true feelings hidden for years. A love that can be lived openly, in daylight, is what you are ultimately after."
    }
  },
  "love:house5": {
    "sun": "Romance is central to who you are, and you shine brightest when you are in love, courting or being courted. You bring warmth, generosity and a sense of occasion to dating: planning special nights, dressing up, making a partner feel like a star. You love the grand gesture, and you remember every meaningful detail of how a romance began. You want to be adored in return. You make love feel like a creative act. Your pride is bound up in your love life, so rejection stings hard, and you need more attention than a partner can always give. You love best when romance expresses who you are without turning into a performance for applause.",
    "moon": "Falling in love happens emotionally and quickly for you, and your mood rises and falls with the state of your romantic life. Dating feels best when it is warm, nurturing and a little playful, full of comfort, easy closeness and time that slips by unnoticed. You can tell someone is right when you could fall asleep beside them without a trace of awkwardness. The right person makes romance feel like coming home. The darker pull is neediness: you seek reassurance constantly in the early weeks, reading every delayed reply as a sign, or mistake comfort for being in love. Your feelings are wise guides, though not always the ones who should be driving.",
    "mercury": "Flirting, for you, is a game of words. You charm with wit, playful teasing and conversations that never seem to run dry, and a clever turn of phrase wins you over faster than any gift. You can spend ages crafting the perfect reply, and a playful exchange stays with you long after it ends. Dating works best when there is always something to talk about, and you make romance sparkle with humour and ideas. The hazard is keeping romance in your head: you flirt with many and commit to few, or intellectualise feelings rather than feeling them. The breakthrough comes when a great conversation becomes a lasting connection.",
    "venus": "Courtship is an art you excel at. You enjoy beauty, romance and all the small rituals of falling in love, and people find you easy to adore. Your flirting is graceful and warm rather than pushy, and you know how to make someone feel special with a single look. You are the one who dresses carefully for a first date and notices every detail of the setting. The harder side is indulgence: you chase pleasure for its own sake, fall for appearances, or drift from one enchanting romance to the next without letting any deepen. The richest pleasure is the kind that grows with time.",
    "mars": "Dating brings out your daring side. You are drawn to romance with movement, spontaneity and a bit of real risk in it. Flirting is direct and cheeky, and you tend to know within minutes whether the spark is there. You are usually the one who makes the first move, long before anyone else has worked up the nerve. The flip side is a low boredom threshold: you mistake adrenaline for love, lose interest once someone is won, or rush into bed before you know whether you even like the person. The passion worth having is the one that lasts beyond the chase.",
    "jupiter": "Luck tends to follow you in romance, and chances to fall in love come along often. You bring optimism, humour and big gestures to dating, and you are drawn to people who are larger than life, well travelled or from other cultures. Early romance quickly becomes an adventure with you, full of plans and grand ideas. You make love feel expansive, joyful and full of possibility. The danger is excess: overpromising, overindulging, or keeping options open because there always seems to be someone more exciting round the corner. One person, you eventually discover, can hold a whole world.",
    "saturn": "Caution colours your love life, and falling for someone never happens lightly. You can be shy about flirting, awkward on first dates or wary of looking foolish, so you hold back until you are sure. You often replay a conversation with someone you liked, wishing you had said more. Romance grows slowly for you and often gets better with age, and once you commit you take love seriously and loyally. The romance you offer is steady, honest and built to last. Where it goes wrong is joylessness: you treat dating like a test to pass and deny yourself pleasure out of fear of rejection. Fun is something you deserve, not something you have to earn.",
    "uranus": "Your romances arrive suddenly and rarely follow the usual script. You fall for unusual, unconventional people, often in unexpected places, and attraction can switch on and off like a light. You can feel electrified by someone within minutes, then find yourself strangely cold soon after. You want excitement, freedom and surprise in dating, and you bring originality and spark to love. The problem is instability: affairs start and end abruptly, and you back away the moment a romance begins to feel predictable or confining. The lover who suits you is the one who keeps surprising you for years.",
    "neptune": "The dream of love captivates you as much as the person. Romance for you is poetic, cinematic and full of longing, and you are drawn to artists, musicians or wounded souls. You can fall for someone almost at once and spend weeks imagining the life you could have together. Your flirtation is gentle, imaginative and a little elusive, and you bring tenderness and magic to love. The catch is illusion: you idealise someone who is not what they seem, ignore red flags, or keep loving a fantasy long after the real relationship has shown its limits. Flawed people, loved with open eyes, can be as beautiful as the dream.",
    "pluto": "Nothing about falling in love is casual for you; it is an all-consuming experience that changes you. Attraction is intense and magnetic, and you are drawn to people with depth, secrets or power. Once someone gets under your skin, they can fill your every waking thought. Your romances tend to be dramatic and transformative, and they reveal parts of you that nothing else could reach. The trap is obsession: you become fixated, jealous or controlling in the early stages, and you get drawn into affairs that are as destructive as they are thrilling. Passion can change you completely without consuming you.",
    "chiron": "Romance touches an old wound for you, often a sense of being unlovable, unattractive or not fun enough. You hesitate to flirt or show joy openly, or you over-perform charm to hide the insecurity. You can assume someone is only being polite when they are genuinely interested in you. Dating brings up your deepest self-doubts, and a single silence can feel like a verdict on your worth. Over time love becomes a place of healing, and you are unusually gentle with partners who also struggle to feel worthy of delight. You, too, deserve to be chosen and enjoyed.",
    "northNode": "Letting yourself fall in love, play and be seen is where your growth lies. You tend to hold back from romance by staying detached, rational or busy with group life, and you are more comfortable being everyone's friend than anyone's date. Your path asks you to take risks with your heart, flirt, date and enjoy pleasure without apology. Each time you choose delight over caution, life opens up in ways you did not expect. The pull back towards safe, impersonal connections is strong, and it shows in how quickly you change the subject when someone says they like you. Being openly, personally wanted is where the joy lies for you.",
    "lilith": "A wild, unapologetic streak runs through your romantic and erotic life. You refuse to play coy or follow the polite rules of dating, and you are drawn to forbidden, taboo or unconventional romances. You say plainly what you want from the very start, and you enjoy watching the other person take it in. Your flirting can be provocative and startling, and you bring an electric honesty to desire. The weak spot is feeling judged or rejected for your appetites, so you swing between suppressing your passion entirely and flaunting it as a form of rebellion. A partner worth keeping lets you be all of that without shrinking or performing."
  },
  "love:house7": {
    "sun": "Partnership is central to your sense of self, and you come alive most fully in a committed relationship. You choose partners who are confident, prominent or strong-willed, often people who reflect qualities you have not yet claimed in yourself. You catch yourself saying 'we' before you have even agreed you are a couple. Marriage or a lasting bond is a major life theme, and you and a partner bring out the best in each other. What trips you up is defining yourself through your partner, losing your own identity or letting them take the spotlight you need. The healthiest version of your marriage has two whole people in it, not one and a half.",
    "moon": "Home is what you look for in a partner. Committed relationships are where you find emotional security, and you are drawn to nurturing, sensitive or family-minded people. You notice every shift in a partner's mood, and you know from the way they shut the front door whether it was a bad day. You create a marriage that feels safe, warm and steadily supportive. The cost is dependence: your moods rise and fall with the relationship, and you either seek a parent in a partner or become the one who mothers everyone. The bond that lasts is one where both of you are cared for equally.",
    "mercury": "Good conversation is non-negotiable in the partners you choose, and a relationship without it feels empty to you. You want someone clever, communicative and mentally stimulating, often youthful in spirit or a sibling-like companion. The best moments of your relationship are the easy, running conversations where you think through life side by side. Agreements and talking things through are central to how you commit, and you build a partnership of true understanding. The pitfall is analysing the relationship endlessly or bickering over small words, and you can marry a mind while neglecting the heart. The partner for you hears what lies beneath your words.",
    "venus": "Commitment comes naturally to you, and marriage often brings ease, beauty and a sense of partnership as an art. You choose partners who are attractive, gracious and cultured, and you make a devoted, considerate spouse. People around you often see your relationships as effortlessly well matched. Shared taste, style and social life keep the bond sweet, and you build a relationship of mutual respect. Trouble arrives through avoiding conflict to keep things pretty: resentments go unspoken, and a relationship can look perfect from outside while feeling shallow within. Honesty deserves the same care you give to harmony.",
    "mars": "Fire is what you choose in a partner: independent, driven, sometimes combative people who will not meekly agree with you. Commitment for you is active; you want to do things together, compete, build and argue honestly. You are the couple who argues loudly over a board game and laughs about it an hour later. Marriage can feel like a partnership of two warriors, and together you push each other to be braver and stronger. What gets hard is a pattern of relationship battles, where fights over who leads become the main way you connect, and making up takes longer than it should. Shared fire works best aimed at common goals rather than at each other.",
    "jupiter": "Partnership tends to be lucky and expansive for you, and you choose generous, wise or worldly partners who broaden your horizons. Marriage often brings growth, travel or a rise in social standing. On meeting someone you care about, you are already imagining the adventures you will share in ten years. You are optimistic about commitment, and in love that suits you, your relationships are warm, generous and full of shared meaning. What can go wrong is overestimating a partner, marrying in haste out of enthusiasm, or expecting a relationship to supply meaning you need to find yourself. Faith in a partner works best alongside honesty about their limits.",
    "saturn": "Commitment is serious business to you. You often choose an older, mature or reliable partner, or you marry later after learning hard lessons about relationships. A bond for you is a long-term contract built on loyalty and responsibility, and you are the one who thinks through every promise carefully before making it. You are the partner people can build a whole life on. The darker pull is fear, of rejection, of being trapped or of choosing wrongly, and you can stay in a cold or dutiful marriage rather than risk the pain of leaving. Warmth and duty can live side by side in the same marriage.",
    "uranus": "Conventional marriage rarely fits you. You choose independent, unusual or eccentric partners, and you need plenty of space within commitment. You flinch at other people's expectations of where a relationship should be heading, not because you do not love your partner but because the script feels foreign. Relationships start suddenly and change dramatically, and you are open to non-traditional arrangements or long-distance bonds that surprise others. The ideal for you is a partnership of two free people. The snag is instability: sudden breakups, or a restlessness that makes lasting commitment hard. The right partner values freedom as much as you do and does not flinch at the unconventional.",
    "neptune": "A soulmate is what you long for, and you often choose partners through a haze of idealism. Artistic, spiritual or sensitive people attract you, and marriage for you is ideally a union of souls. You have probably defended a partner to your friends while quietly ignoring what those friends were trying to tell you. You are compassionate and self-sacrificing, and your love has a healing, spiritual quality. The harder side is disillusionment: you marry a fantasy, overlook deception or addiction in a partner, or fall into rescuing someone who drains you. Seeing a partner as they are and loving them anyway is the love you are built for.",
    "pluto": "Committed relationships are intense and transformative for you. You choose powerful, magnetic or controlling partners, and marriage changes you profoundly, sometimes through crisis. You want total commitment and complete honesty, and you notice the smallest evasion. You have known relationships where the same argument returns again and again until something fundamental shifts. Your partnerships lead you to extraordinary depth and self-knowledge. Where it goes wrong is power struggles: jealousy, manipulation or control dominate, and you can feel reborn through the end of a relationship as much as through its beginning. Power shared, rather than battled over, is what lets you rest.",
    "chiron": "Your deepest wound surfaces in committed partnership, often a fear of being abandoned, unworthy or unable to relate as an equal. You attract partners who need healing, or repeat painful patterns until you understand them. You have noticed that the same row seems to follow you from one relationship to the next. You can also be the partner who gives endlessly while secretly expecting to be left. Over time you develop remarkable empathy for a partner's struggles, and the relationships you work through become sources of healing for you both. You are worth staying for.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in partnership. You tend to rely on your own independence and self-sufficiency, and your instinct is to handle everything yourself, even when a partner is offering help. Your path asks you to share, compromise and commit to another person. Relationships teach you cooperation and trust, and each time you let someone in, your life becomes fuller. Old habits pull you towards going it alone, and you can make decisions about a shared future without consulting anyone. Learning to weigh a partner's needs alongside yours and to build something together brings the fulfilment you are looking for.",
    "lilith": "You refuse to disappear inside a relationship. Partnership for you involves power, independence and often a battle over who defines the rules, and you are drawn to strong-willed or unconventional partners. You bristle the moment someone assumes you will slip into a role you never agreed to play. Traditional roles in marriage feel stifling, and you create a bond of two sovereign people. The catch is attracting controlling partners or projecting your own rebellion onto them, so commitment becomes a fight for autonomy rather than a meeting of equals. Your wildness is not a problem to be tamed; it is part of what makes you worth marrying."
  },
  "love:house8": {
    "sun": "Intimacy is where you come fully alive. You want relationships with depth, and a bond that stays on the surface does not feel like love to you. Sex and emotional merging are central to your identity, and you draw out other people's secrets with ease: partners find themselves telling you things they have never told anyone. You offer a love that is profound and transforming. The trap is power: you hold back your own vulnerability while wanting total access to your partner's, and trust is slow to earn. Being seen as fully as you want to see is the test of your courage.",
    "moon": "Deep, private emotional closeness is what makes you feel secure. Sex for you is emotionally charged, a way of bonding and of being held, and you sense a partner's moods and secrets almost instantly. You can feel something is wrong from the smallest change in how they touch you. You need to know the relationship is solid underneath, and with that certainty you create an intimacy that feels like shelter. The weak spot is jealousy and fear of loss: you cling, brood over imagined betrayals, or withhold feelings as self-protection when you feel exposed. Closeness can survive your fears.",
    "mercury": "Knowing your partner completely, including what they do not say, matters enormously to you. Intimate conversations, pillow talk and uncovering secrets arouse you as much as touch, and you are drawn to probing, psychological discussion. You are the one asking about the old hurts and hidden stories that make them who they are. Words in the bedroom carry a charge, and you create intimacy through deep understanding. What trips you up is suspicion: you investigate, read between every line, or use sharp words to cut a partner where it hurts most. A little mystery left between you keeps the charge alive.",
    "venus": "Sensuality sits at the heart of how you love. You find beauty in what is hidden and taboo, and you are at your most loving in private, slow, intensely physical moments. You remember every sensation of the first time you trusted someone completely. Trust is the aphrodisiac: once someone earns it, you give generously and without reserve, and your love is devoted and profound. The cost is using affection or sex as leverage, or feeling jealous of a partner's past and their other attachments. What you want is a love that merges two lives completely without either person owning the other.",
    "mars": "Your sexual drive is strong, and you want intensity, stamina and a partner who can match your appetite. You pursue closeness with determination, and desire is often fuelled by a sense of the forbidden. Physical passion and emotional power are tightly linked for you, so a heated argument can end in bed. You bring courage and fire to intimacy, and you are unafraid of what others find too much. The pitfall is jealousy that turns into anger, and the urge to dominate or retaliate when trust is broken. Your strength is most beautiful when it protects vulnerability rather than conquering it.",
    "jupiter": "Closeness expands you. You are generous and open-minded in bed, curious about sexuality and willing to explore, and deep bonding can feel almost spiritual. Partners feel safe opening up to you because you do not judge, and you have heard confessions that surprised even the person making them. You make intimacy feel joyful, abundant and free of shame. Trouble arrives through excess: you overindulge in sexual adventure, trust too readily, or chase ever greater intensity rather than let a quiet closeness be enough. Depth, in the end, satisfies you more than breadth, and one trusted partner can open more doors than a dozen adventures.",
    "saturn": "Trust comes slowly to you, and letting someone see you naked, emotionally or physically, can feel frightening. You guard your vulnerability and hold back sexually until you feel completely secure. You know the ache of wanting to say something true to someone you love and being unable to. Once trust is established, your loyalty and depth are remarkable, and your intimacy is steady, committed and unguarded. The darker pull is inhibition or control: you withhold intimacy, feel shame around desire, or keep a partner at arm's length for fear of losing yourself. Closeness is something you allow, not something you manage.",
    "uranus": "Routine has no place in your intimate life. You are curious about unconventional sexuality and experimentation, and sudden, electric attractions come from nowhere. You need freedom even in the most intimate bond, and straight after a moment of closeness you can feel a sudden urge to pull away. Honesty, originality and openness are what you bring to intimacy. The harder side is detachment at moments of exposure: you switch off emotionally, pull back when things get close, or face sudden ruptures of trust that change a relationship overnight. Staying in the room when closeness feels most unsettling is your quiet act of bravery.",
    "neptune": "Merging is what you long for, an intimacy where boundaries dissolve. Sex for you can feel transcendent, dreamy and intensely emotional, and you sense a partner's inner world intuitively. You have felt a partner's sadness in your own body before they said a word. You are tender, responsive and capable of a rare spiritual closeness. Where it goes wrong is confusion and deception: you lose yourself in a partner, idealise a sexual connection, ignore betrayals, or become entangled in relationships built on secrecy. Knowing where you end and they begin keeps the magic from turning into loss.",
    "pluto": "For you, intimacy is a matter of life and death. You seek total, transformative bonds and sex that strips away every pretence, and half measures leave you cold. A single moment of real closeness can change how you see yourself. Your capacity for depth, loyalty and passion is profound, and in the strongest bonds you help a partner transform alongside you. The catch is obsession, jealousy and control: power struggles in the bedroom and beyond, suspicion of betrayal, and relationships that end in a complete, painful rebirth rather than a quiet parting. Surrender without domination is the intimacy you are seeking.",
    "chiron": "Vulnerability is where your deepest wound lies, often around trust, betrayal or feeling safe in your body with someone else. Sex and emotional merging can feel frightening or bound up with past hurt, and intimacy brings those wounds to the surface. You sometimes flinch at a tender touch, or crack a joke at the most exposed moment. Working through it gives you great sensitivity, and you become a partner who understands how much courage it takes to let someone close. A healing closeness, built at your own pace with someone patient enough to wait, is within your reach.",
    "northNode": "Letting someone in completely is where your growth lies. You tend to rely on self-sufficiency and your own resources, and you are more comfortable paying your own way and keeping your inner life private. Your path asks you to merge, trust and be transformed by deep intimacy. Sharing vulnerability, desire and power with a partner brings the fulfilment you need. The pull towards comfort and control is strong, and it shows when you go quiet the moment a conversation becomes too raw. Choosing depth over safety is what changes you, and hard-won trust brings a richness nothing else can.",
    "lilith": "Raw, powerful and unapologetic, your sexuality is drawn to the taboo and the intense. You refuse to hide your desires or to be tamed by a partner's expectations, and that frankness can both thrill and unsettle a lover. You can name exactly what you want without blushing, and you notice how it lands. A fierce honesty is what you bring to intimacy. Trust and power are the sore points: you fear being controlled or shamed for your desires, test a partner's loyalty, or use sexual power as armour against vulnerability. Your whole self deserves a partner with whom it is safe."
  },
  "career:saturn": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "Saturn in Aries makes independence at work something you have to earn rather than something handed to you. You want to lead, start things and act on your own judgement, yet you hold back until you are certain you will not look foolish. You can have a bold plan fully formed in your head, then hold it back for days until you are certain nobody will laugh at it. Early in a career this shows as impatience with slow promotion or a boss who second-guesses every call you make. Some years swing between hesitation and rash moves made out of frustration. Once preparation catches up with nerve, you become a leader whose courage people trust, and the work asks you to launch things on your own authority.",
      "taurus": "Your working life tends to be built slowly and solidly, one skill and one pay rise at a time. Saturn in Taurus gives you patience for craft, budgets and anything that needs steady tending. You weigh the security in any offer before its excitement, and you stay in a role long enough to be sure your success was not a fluke. The difficulty is a fear of financial insecurity that keeps you in a safe position long after it has stopped suiting you. Change at work feels expensive, even when it is overdue. Over the long run you build expertise and material security that nobody can take away, along with a hard-won trust in your own worth.",
      "gemini": "Communication is the skill you work hardest to master professionally. Saturn in Gemini can make you anxious about sounding uninformed in meetings, so you overprepare, read everything and check your facts twice. You rework a simple message several times before you send it, and you replay a clumsy answer long after everyone else has forgotten it. That diligence turns into recognised authority in writing, teaching, analysis or any role built on clear information. Worry can scatter you across too many small tasks, and you sometimes doubt an idea until someone more confident voices it first. Your career draws you towards becoming the trusted voice whose words carry weight precisely because they were earned.",
      "cancer": "Feelings at work are something you learn to manage carefully, sometimes too carefully. Saturn in Cancer often makes you the dependable one who looks after the team, remembers everyone's deadlines and quietly absorbs the stress of others. You quietly take on extra so that others can cope with what they are carrying at home, then say nothing about it. Being seen as vulnerable in front of bosses frightens you, so you keep a composed face even on bad days. Careers in care, property, family business or any role that protects people suit you. Your authority grows as warmth becomes part of your professional strength rather than something you hide.",
      "leo": "Recognition is the thing you most want at work and the thing you are most wary of claiming. Saturn in Leo gives you the discipline to become accomplished in a creative, leadership or public role, but it can also make you hold back from the spotlight for fear of being judged. You know the feeling of staying silent while someone else confidently voices the very idea you had been sitting on for weeks. You often watch less talented people take the credit while you wait to be invited. In time, you become a leader with substance, whose presence is built on skill. Your career asks you to stop waiting for permission and let your work carry your name.",
      "virgo": "Precision is your professional hallmark. Saturn in Virgo builds a working style that is thorough, methodical and precise to the decimal: you are the person who spots the flaw in the figures or the gap in the process. Perfectionism can slow your delivery, and you dread making even small mistakes in front of a manager. Criticism of your work can sting for days. Given time, you become an expert whose standards others rely on in health, analysis, editing, operations or technical work, and your career rewards quiet, patient competence.",
      "libra": "Partnerships, negotiation and fairness are where your career asks the most of you. Saturn in Libra tends to make you a careful collaborator who weighs every agreement and dislikes office politics. You read the contract twice, notice the clause that favours the other side and still find it hard to say so out loud. You can struggle to assert your own position when a colleague or client pushes back, and you often end up doing the diplomatic work nobody thanks you for. Roles in law, mediation, design, HR or client management reward your sense of balance. Over the years you earn authority as someone whose judgement is fair and whose word, and contracts, hold.",
      "scorpio": "Control and trust are central themes in how you handle work. Saturn in Scorpio gives you enormous staying power for demanding, high-stakes jobs: research, finance, crisis management, therapy, investigation. You rarely show your hand to a boss until you are sure of your ground, and you notice who in the meeting is holding back information. Being undermined or stripped of influence is your quiet dread, so you keep your own files and your own counsel. Secrecy creeps in, and a slight from a colleague can be remembered for years. You become the professional who handles what others cannot face, calmly and without fuss, and your influence is strongest when it is used cleanly.",
      "sagittarius": "Your ambition is tied to meaning, and you work hardest when the job connects to a belief or a bigger picture. Saturn in Sagittarius can make you doubt your qualifications, so you pursue degrees, certificates or years of study before feeling entitled to teach or lead. You are the one who signs up for another course rather than apply for the senior role you are already capable of. Academic, legal, publishing and international careers suit this structured pursuit of knowledge. Opinions can harden, and part of you fears your vision will not be taken seriously. Earned wisdom eventually makes you a respected authority, and teaching what you have tested becomes a natural next step.",
      "capricorn": "Saturn is at home in Capricorn, so ambition, structure and long-range planning are instinctive to you at work. Bosses tend to hand you the difficult project because they see you as a safe pair of hands, and you climb steadily through organisations by being the one who delivers. You have a five-year plan, even if you never show it to anyone, and you quietly track how far along it you are. The risk is measuring yourself only by title and output, working long hours out of fear rather than need. Time off can feel like lost ground. Your career usually gathers weight in your thirties and beyond, and you grow into an authority people are glad to follow.",
      "aquarius": "Your career asks you to find a structured way to be different. Saturn in Aquarius suits systems, technology, science, social causes and any organisation built around a collective aim, and you often become the one who designs the rules others follow. You can turn a team's messy way of working into a clean, logical system, then feel oddly left out of the easy social side of work. You can be uneasy about fitting in while also fearing that your unusual ideas will be dismissed. A cool detachment can make colleagues see you as aloof. Over time you turn original thinking into reliable, workable frameworks that outlast you, and that becomes your professional legacy.",
      "pisces": "Work that serves something beyond profit matters to you, yet boundaries at work are hard to hold. Saturn in Pisces brings discipline to creative, spiritual, healing or charitable careers, but it can also leave you anxious that your gifts are not practical enough to earn a living. You are there for anyone who is struggling, at any hour, then find it hard to ask to be paid properly for your own time. You overgive and underclaim credit for what you do. Vague roles with no clear structure leave you drifting. Giving imagination a solid structure is the long work here, and in time your sensitivity reads to others as a professional skill rather than a weakness."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "You tend to be seen at work as serious, competent and older than your years, even in your first job. Saturn in the 1st house means your professional presence is something you build deliberately: how you dress, speak and carry yourself in meetings. People often assume you have more experience than you do, and they turn to you for a judgement long before you feel ready to give one. Self-consciousness can make you slow to put yourself forward for promotion, and you hate being put on the spot. Colleagues sometimes read your reserve as coldness. You become the calm, reliable figure in the room when a project goes wrong, and your reputation grows steadily with every year.",
      "2": "Earning a living is something you take very seriously. Saturn in the 2nd house links your career closely to financial security, so you choose stable, salaried paths, save carefully and work hard for every rise. You keep a close eye on what you earn, and you know exactly what you are worth long before you find the nerve to ask for it out loud. The fear of not having enough can keep you in roles that pay well but bore you. Underpricing your own skills is a common pattern. Over time you build mastery in managing resources, and your value to an employer rests on proven, practical competence that grows more valuable with time.",
      "3": "Communication, paperwork and the daily flow of information run through your working life. Saturn in the 3rd house helps you master writing, teaching, sales, logistics or anything that requires clear messages and careful detail. You put things on record carefully when nobody else bothers, and later everyone relies on what you wrote down. You can be hesitant to speak up in meetings or worry that your ideas sound unpolished next to a quicker colleague. A nagging sense that you are less clever than the people around you can follow you for years. Persistence turns this into authority: people trust what you write and say because they know you have checked it thoroughly.",
      "4": "Career and home life pull against each other for you, and balancing them is part of the long climb. Saturn in the 4th house can mean building a career slowly from a modest or demanding family background, or working from home, in property or in a family business. You know the guilt of letting work spill into home life, and the pull of staying close by because family needs you, even when ambition points elsewhere. You often feel you carry the household's security on your shoulders. Slowly you build foundations so solid that ambition can rest on them. The rewards tend to arrive later in life, and they last.",
      "5": "Creativity at work is something you take seriously, perhaps too seriously at first. Saturn in the 5th house can make you hesitant to show your ideas or take creative risks for fear they will be judged. You tend to keep your best ideas to yourself, polishing them privately until they feel safe enough to show anyone. With practice you develop mastery in performance, design, teaching, working with children or any role that asks you to create. Every project can start to feel like an exam you might fail. Eventually work becomes a place where you let yourself enjoy what you make, and that enjoyment shows in the quality.",
      "6": "The daily job itself is where you prove yourself. Saturn in the 6th house makes you the colleague who handles the dull, essential tasks without complaint, keeps processes tidy and takes deadlines personally. You are often the last to stop at the end of a week, checking one more time so that nothing is left hanging unfinished. You shoulder too much and feel guilty stepping away from your desk. Managers learn they can depend on you completely, which can mean they pile on more. That diligence becomes true expertise, and this placement asks you to set limits on workload so that it builds you rather than wearing you down.",
      "7": "Business partnerships and client relationships are where your career gets tested. Saturn in the 7th house often draws you into formal collaborations, contracts and working relationships with older or more senior people. You take your commitments to clients very seriously, and you often end up carrying a shared project alone when a partner stops pulling their weight. Trusting a collaborator with your reputation does not come easily. Sometimes you choose safe, formal partnerships that end up restricting you. Consulting, law, agency work and any role built on long-term professional relationships suit you. Loyalty and reliability become your reputation, and clients stay with you for decades.",
      "8": "Your career often involves carrying responsibility for other people's money, secrets or crises. Saturn in the 8th house suits finance, insurance, research, psychology, investigation and any field where trust and discretion are essential. You are the one colleagues come to with the thing they cannot tell the boss, and you keep it. You are cautious about sharing power and wary of depending on a boss's goodwill or a shared business. A fear of losing control makes delegating feel dangerous. In time you become the steady professional others turn to when the stakes are highest, and your career asks you to hold power without gripping it.",
      "9": "Qualifications, study and belief shape your professional path. Saturn in the 9th house often leads to long training, higher education, law, academia, publishing or work abroad, and you tend to feel you must be properly credentialled before you can speak with authority. You often sit quietly while others hold forth, privately sure you know more than they do, and you say nothing at all. Doubts about your expertise can delay your first step into teaching or leading. Once you do arrive, your thinking can turn rigid. Even so, your knowledge carries weight, and colleagues seek out your considered opinion because they know it has been tested.",
      "10": "Saturn sits in its natural place here, at the top of the chart, making career one of the main arenas of your life. You aim high, respect hierarchy and understand that status takes years to build. When others move ahead faster, you quietly resolve to outlast them rather than compete on their terms. Bosses and authority figures loom large, sometimes as mentors and sometimes as obstacles. The fear of public failure can be intense, and a single visible mistake can haunt you for months. Success arrives later but lasts, and you often end up in a position of settled authority that nobody can question.",
      "11": "Your career grows through networks, professional bodies and long-term goals that take years to realise. Saturn in the 11th house can make you slow to join groups at work or leave you feeling like an outsider in a team, yet you often end up organising or leading them. You often start on the edge of a group, unsure of your place in it, and end up the one holding it together years later. You work towards one ambitious aim at a time. Some years you doubt your plans will ever come to fruition. Persistence and a few trusted allies prove you right, and the future you planned slowly takes shape.",
      "12": "Much of your best work happens behind the scenes. Saturn in the 12th house suits hospitals, charities, research, archives, prisons, creative solitude or any setting away from public view. You are the one who fixes the problem before anyone else knows there was one, and then feels faintly hurt that nobody noticed. You work hard without seeking credit, and you can harbour a hidden fear that your efforts count for nothing. Burnout from quiet overcommitment is a constant risk. Your mastery comes from disciplined inner work, and it earns deep respect from those who see it."
    }
  },
  "career:sun": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "You feel most yourself at work when you are starting something, leading a charge or competing to win. The Sun in Aries wants a role with pace, independence and a clear challenge: launching projects, entrepreneurship, sport, emergency work or anything where speed counts. You take ownership of a problem before others have finished discussing it, and you have a plan before anyone else has even started. Routine and slow committees drain you quickly. Impatience with process and slower colleagues can burn bridges. You are the spark that gets things moving, and your calling draws you towards being first.",
      "taurus": "Purpose at work comes from building something tangible and lasting. The Sun in Taurus wants a job with results you can see, touch or count: finance, food, design, property, craft or anything that creates value over time. You get quiet satisfaction from seeing something real and useful take shape through your own steady effort. You work best at a steady pace in a comfortable environment, and you resent being rushed into decisions. Stubbornness can leave you clinging to the old way when the market shifts. You are the reliable one who finishes what others abandon, and your calling is to build things of solid worth.",
      "gemini": "Variety, conversation and ideas are what make work feel alive to you. The Sun in Gemini thrives in roles with many moving parts: writing, media, teaching, sales, marketing, tech or anything that keeps information flowing. You keep many threads going at once and somehow remember the detail from each one. You want to learn something new every week, and you shine as the quick connector who can explain anything to anyone. Boredom is the bigger risk, and it can produce a career that looks scattered from the outside. You become the bridge between people and ideas, and the career that fits is one where versatility itself is the job.",
      "cancer": "Looking after people is what gives your work its sense of purpose. The Sun in Cancer shines in roles where you nurture, protect or provide: care, education, hospitality, property, HR, or running a small business that feels like a family. You remember what matters to the people around you, and you notice at once when someone feels left out. You work best when you feel emotionally safe with your team. Workplace criticism tends to land personally, and loyalty can keep you in a job long after the people there stopped returning it. You create workplaces where people feel they belong, and teams often stay together because of you.",
      "leo": "You want work that lets you be seen and that carries your personal stamp. The Sun in Leo shines in leadership, performance, creative direction, teaching or any role where your warmth and presence lift others. You come alive when all eyes are on you, and a single piece of sincere praise can keep you going for weeks. Anonymous back-office work tends to dim your energy. Needing the credit can make collaboration suffer, and an unnoticed contribution can leave you sulking for days. When it goes well, you inspire a team and make it proud of what it produces. Generous, visible leadership is where you belong.",
      "virgo": "Being useful is what makes work meaningful for you. The Sun in Virgo shines in roles that call for skill, analysis and care for detail: health, research, editing, data, operations, craft or any service where quality matters. You quietly fix the problem everyone else has been working around for months, and rarely mention that you did. You tend to undersell your abilities, perfecting small things while others with less competence claim the bigger roles. You are often the indispensable expert, and your calling asks you to let your skill be seen as well as used.",
      "libra": "Collaboration is where you come alive professionally. The Sun in Libra shines in roles that call for diplomacy, taste and fairness: law, mediation, design, client relations, the arts or any partnership business. You are the one who calms a tense meeting with a well-timed suggestion that lets both sides save face. You work best with a good colleague beside you and feel most yourself when bringing people to agreement or making something beautiful. Indecision and a reluctance to disappoint anyone can stall your career at crucial moments. You create the harmony that makes teams work, and the solutions you broker are both fair and elegant.",
      "scorpio": "Depth and intensity are what make work worth doing for you. The Sun in Scorpio shines in roles that involve investigation, transformation or high stakes: research, psychology, surgery, finance, crisis work or strategy. You read between the lines and see a problem coming long before anyone else has noticed it. You want to get to the bottom of things, and you commit completely once you care. Surface-level jobs bore you fast. Power struggles with bosses follow you, and so does a tendency to trust no one at work. You transform whatever you touch, and your calling asks you to go where others will not.",
      "sagittarius": "Work has to mean something and go somewhere for you to feel yourself in it. The Sun in Sagittarius shines in teaching, travel, publishing, law, philosophy, outdoor work or any role that widens horizons. You light up when work stretches beyond the familiar and gives you the chance to explain why something matters. You want freedom, room to grow and a vision worth believing in, and micromanagement stifles you. Overpromising is a habit, and you can move on before a project is finished because a bigger idea has appeared. You inspire people with your enthusiasm, and the knowledge you share travels far beyond the room.",
      "capricorn": "Achievement is close to the heart of who you are. The Sun in Capricorn shines in management, business, government, engineering or any structured field where results are measurable and progress can be tracked over years. You are the one who knows where you want to be in ten years and can list the steps to get there. Status can come to define your worth, and you can work so hard that the rest of life waits indefinitely. You grow into an authority built on results, and what you build is made to endure.",
      "aquarius": "Improving systems and thinking ahead of the crowd is when you feel most yourself at work. The Sun in Aquarius shines in technology, science, social enterprise, activism, innovation or any role serving a collective aim. You question out loud why things are still done the old way, and then you go ahead and build the better version yourself. You need freedom to experiment and resent rules that exist only for tradition. Colleagues value your originality, though your detachment and resistance to authority can make you hard to manage. You are an innovator, happiest when your work improves things for many people at once.",
      "pisces": "Imagination and compassion are what give your work meaning. The Sun in Pisces shines in the arts, music, film, healing, spirituality, charity or any role that serves people who are struggling. You pick up the mood of a workplace the moment you walk in, and you can tell which colleague is having a bad day before they say a word. Rigid, competitive environments drain you quickly. Without a clear direction you can drift, and others sometimes take advantage of your willingness to help. You bring vision and kindness to your work in a way that moves people. The work that fulfils you is the kind that gives your dreams a form."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "Your work is an extension of your personality, and people remember you as much as what you produce. The Sun in the 1st house suits careers where you are the face of the enterprise: self-employment, leadership, performance, personal brands or any role where initiative is rewarded. Wherever you work, people know who you are before long, even if you have said very little. You feel most yourself when you are visibly taking charge. Sharing credit is hard for you, and so is working unseen as one member of a team. Your presence opens doors, and work that carries your own name suits you best.",
      "2": "Earning well and building tangible value give your work its purpose. The Sun in the 2nd house makes you proud of your skills and keen to be paid what they are worth, and you often thrive in finance, sales, property, craft or business. There is a particular satisfaction for you in being paid what you are worth without having to argue for a cent of it. You feel most yourself when your efforts produce something solid and secure. Your sense of worth can become tangled up with your income, keeping you in a well-paid role that no longer inspires you. You build lasting value, and your skills become an asset over the years.",
      "3": "Words and ideas are where you shine professionally. The Sun in the 3rd house suits writing, journalism, teaching, sales, media, transport or any role that keeps you talking, moving and connecting people. You always seem to know the latest news, and you can make dry information lively enough that people want to hear it to the end. Work that confines you to one desk and one task tends to dull you. You can spread yourself thin, chasing the next conversation before finishing the last. A busy schedule of calls, messages and short projects brings out your sharpest thinking, and your calling is to connect people through information.",
      "4": "Home, roots and family sit close to the centre of your working purpose. The Sun in the 4th house often suits working from home, property, interiors, hospitality, family businesses or careers that create security for others. You are happiest when your working space feels like yours, and impersonal, soulless surroundings wear on you quickly. You need a private base before you can shine in public, and your career often comes into its own later in life. Family obligations or a need for safety can put a ceiling on your ambition. You build something lasting that shelters others, and that is your calling.",
      "5": "Creativity and self-expression are what make work feel like yours. The Sun in the 5th house shines in the arts, entertainment, teaching, working with children, sport or any job with an element of play. You bring a sense of occasion to even routine work, and people remember how you made it feel. You want to put your personality into what you make and enjoy the process of making it. Dull, joyless roles drain you quickly. You can take professional risks for the thrill, or lose motivation when the applause stops. Your enthusiasm is contagious, and your calling draws you towards work you love for its own sake.",
      "6": "You find your purpose in the daily practice of doing a job well. The Sun in the 6th house makes work a central part of your identity, and you shine in service, health, operations, craft or any role that improves how things function. You get a quiet glow from finishing what needs doing and from making things run better than they did before. You feel proud when colleagues rely on your skill. Defining yourself entirely by productivity leaves you lost and irritable on days when there is nothing useful to do. You become a true master of your craft, and your service speaks through the quality of what you do.",
      "7": "Partnership is where your professional self comes to life. The Sun in the 7th house suits consulting, law, agency work, counselling or any career built on one-to-one relationships with clients or a business partner. You think best in dialogue with someone else, and your sharpest ideas often arrive in the middle of a conversation. You feel most yourself when your skills serve another person's goals. Your own ambitions can slip out of sight, or you rely too heavily on a partner to open doors. You make every collaboration stronger, shining alongside others without disappearing into them.",
      "8": "Depth, stakes and a degree of mystery are what you look for in a job. The Sun in the 8th house shines in finance, investment, research, psychology, insurance, crisis work or anything involving other people's resources or secrets. You are the one who is oddly calm when the company is in trouble, and the one called in when something needs untangling. You feel most yourself transforming something that was broken or hidden. Power at work matters to you, sometimes more than you admit, and struggles over control with bosses or partners can recur. You turn crises into renewal, and your best work changes things at the root.",
      "9": "A career that expands your horizons is the one that feels like yours. The Sun in the 9th house shines in higher education, law, publishing, travel, religion, foreign trade or any role built on ideas and vision. You say yes to whatever widens your world at work, while others look for reasons to stay where they are. You feel most yourself when you are exploring or explaining the bigger picture. Work that is purely local or routine tends to feel too small. Restlessness follows you, along with a habit of preaching rather than listening. You open minds, and your calling is to share what you have learned.",
      "10": "Career sits at the very heart of your identity. The Sun in the 10th house puts you in the public eye and drives you towards leadership, visible achievement and a reputation you are proud of. When someone asks what you do, the answer feels like a statement about who you are. Bosses and authority figures matter hugely, whether as models or rivals. The shadow is feeling worthless between promotions, or when a title fails to reflect the person behind it. You become a respected figure in your field, and your calling asks you to lead in a way that honours what you care about.",
      "11": "Your purpose at work is bound up with groups, networks and future goals. The Sun in the 11th house shines in technology, social causes, community organising, professional associations or any team working towards a shared vision. Your best opportunities tend to arrive through the people you know and the people they know, often when you least expect it. You feel most yourself when you are part of something larger and progressive. The difficulty is losing your individual ambitions inside the group or drifting between causes. You rally people around a vision, and your calling draws you towards work that shapes the future.",
      "12": "Some of your most meaningful work happens out of the spotlight. The Sun in the 12th house shines in healing, research, the arts, spiritual work, charities, hospitals or institutions, and in any role where you serve quietly. You do your clearest thinking alone, when nobody is watching and nothing is expected of you. You feel most yourself following intuition rather than a job description. The difficulty is hiding your talents, avoiding recognition or giving so much behind the scenes that nobody knows what you contribute. Your work touches people's lives, even when your name is not on it."
    }
  },
  "career:house10": {
    "sun": "Being known for your work matters to you. With the Sun at the top of your chart, colleagues and the wider public tend to see you as a natural figurehead, and you are often promoted into roles that carry visibility and responsibility. People introduce you by your job title, and you feel a small lift when they do. You measure yourself against a parent or early role model more than you realise. The shadow is performing success for an audience rather than for yourself. You shine brightest when your reputation rests on work you believe in, and this placement draws you towards a role where your name stands for something.",
    "moon": "Your career is tied to your emotions and to the public mood. The Moon in the 10th house suits roles that involve caring for or connecting with people: hospitality, healthcare, education, retail, property or public-facing work. You can sense how a room or an audience is feeling and adjust your pitch without thinking about it. Your professional direction tends to shift in phases, and your reputation can rise and fall with how you feel. A cool word from a boss can unsettle your whole week. Public criticism goes straight to your heart. Over time the public comes to trust you, and people follow you because they feel looked after.",
    "mercury": "Communication is your professional calling card. Mercury in the 10th house suits careers in writing, media, teaching, sales, law, technology or anything where your ideas and words become your reputation. You are the one colleagues nominate to present the findings or write the difficult message to the client. You change direction several times or juggle more than one role at once, and your CV reads like several careers. You can overthink your image, or talk over bosses in the heat of a debate. You become a recognised voice in your field, the person others quote.",
    "venus": "Charm, diplomacy and taste help your career along. Venus in the 10th house suits the arts, design, fashion, beauty, hospitality, public relations or any role where likeability and aesthetic sense count. Bosses and clients tend to warm to you, and you are often the one sent to smooth things over when a relationship has soured. Work partnerships can overlap with personal ones, and important people often enter your life through your job. Popularity can become a crutch, and you shy away from the conflict that leadership sometimes requires. You build a reputation for grace under pressure, and doors open because people enjoy working with you.",
    "mars": "You pursue your career like a campaign. Mars in the 10th house drives you to compete, climb and prove yourself publicly, and you thrive in entrepreneurial, military, sporting, surgical or high-pressure roles. You know the flash of irritation when a manager says \"let's wait and see\", and you often push ahead anyway. You would rather run the show than take orders, which leads to clashes with bosses who do not move fast enough. Your reputation rests on getting things done. Burning out, or burning bridges on the way up, is the cost when you never ease off. You make a bold, decisive leader, and teams move faster when you are in charge.",
    "jupiter": "Opportunity tends to find you at work. Jupiter in the 10th house often brings a good reputation, generous mentors and a career that grows larger than you expected in law, education, publishing, business, travel or any field built on vision. You have probably been offered a role you did not apply for, because someone senior thought of you. You relate to authority with optimism and usually get on well with bosses. Overreaching is the trap: promising more than you can deliver, or coasting on early success. You become a respected, generous figure, and your career draws you towards leadership that lifts others.",
    "saturn": "Your public image is one of seriousness and reliability, and people tend to hand you responsibility before you ask for it. Saturn in the 10th house suits government, management, engineering, law or any established institution with a clear ladder. You are the one who is quietly asked to cover for the director when they are away, and you do it flawlessly. You often become the manager with high standards who holds everyone to account. Shortcuts backfire for you, so your reputation depends on integrity. The risk is turning into the rigid boss you once resented. Over the years you become an authority people trust completely.",
    "uranus": "Your career rarely follows a straight line. Uranus in the 10th house brings sudden changes of direction, unexpected job offers and a strong need for independence, so you thrive in technology, science, innovation, freelancing or any field that rewards originality. You have probably handed in your notice on impulse at least once, or reinvented your whole career almost overnight. Conventional hierarchies frustrate you, and you clash with bosses who insist on doing things the old way. The shadow is instability that makes employers wary. Your reputation is as the one who shakes things up, and you are usually right about where the field is heading.",
    "neptune": "Your sense of calling is strong but hard to pin down. Neptune in the 10th house draws you towards the arts, film, music, healing, spirituality, charity or any work that serves an ideal. When someone asks what you want to do with your career, you can describe the feeling perfectly but struggle to name the job. Others project their own dreams onto your public image, and your reputation can be glamorous or hazy. Career goals shift like fog, and you tend to idealise employers who later disappoint you. You inspire people through your work once a vision becomes a paid role.",
    "pluto": "Power and influence are central to your working life. Pluto in the 10th house drives you towards positions of control, often in business, politics, finance, psychology, research or any field that deals with crisis and transformation. You go through dramatic career reinventions rather than gentle changes, walking away from one identity to build another. You can read the power structure of a new workplace within days. Relations with authority are intense: you either fight a powerful boss or become one. The risk is obsession with status and control. Used well, that influence transforms organisations from the inside.",
    "chiron": "An old wound around recognition or success often sits underneath your career. Chiron in the 10th house can bring early setbacks, a critical parent or a sense of not being taken seriously by authority. Even after a promotion, you can feel as though someone is about to tap you on the shoulder and ask what you are doing there. You tend to doubt your right to lead. Over time you often find your calling in teaching, healing, mentoring or advocacy, helping others with the very professional struggles you have faced. Your reputation comes to rest on that hard-won understanding, and your career asks you to lead from experience.",
    "northNode": "Your life direction points squarely towards career and public contribution. The North Node in the 10th house asks you to step out of the comfort of home and private life and take on visible responsibility. You know the pull of turning down the promotion because it would mean more exposure, more meetings and less time in your safe routine. Family duties tend to call loudest in the same season ambition asks more of you. Hiding in private life is tempting when the world is asking for you. Growth comes when you accept a leadership role, build a reputation in your field and let the world see what you can do.",
    "lilith": "You have a complicated, rebellious relationship with authority and public image. Lilith in the 10th house resists being told how to behave at work, and you reject careers that require you to fit a polished mould. Rules about how you should look, sound or behave have always chafed, and you bristle at anyone who wants you to tone yourself down. You can face gossip, scrutiny or unfair judgement from people in power. Defiance can lead you to sabotage your own standing. Your strength emerges in unconventional or provocative work where you set the rules, and your reputation becomes that of the person who refused to conform."
  },
  "career:house6": {
    "sun": "Day to day, you want your job to reflect well on you. The Sun in the 6th house makes you a visible presence in the workplace: you set the standard for others and take real pride in work that runs smoothly because of you. You notice when someone changes how things are done without asking you first, and it bothers you more than it should. You work best with some autonomy over your own tasks. Ego clashes over how things should be done are common, and criticism of your work can feel like criticism of you. You lead by example, and your daily work becomes a source of self-respect.",
    "moon": "Your mood at work is shaped by the atmosphere around you. The Moon in the 6th house makes you sensitive to colleagues, and you often become the one people confide in or the one who keeps the team emotionally steady. You are the person who notices when the mood in the office shifts after a closed-door meeting. You need familiar routines and a workplace that feels safe, and changes in schedule unsettle you more than you show. Everyone's stress tends to land on you along with your own. You make any workplace feel more humane, and caring, catering and health roles often suit you.",
    "mercury": "Your working day runs on lists, emails and problem solving. Mercury in the 6th house gives you an efficient, analytical approach to tasks, and you are often the colleague who writes the procedures, spots the error or fixes the system. You have a to-do list for your to-do lists, and crossing an item off gives you a sharp hit of satisfaction. You enjoy technical or detailed work and like to keep your mind busy. Small worries can nag at you, and you can become overly critical of how others do their jobs. You make any operation run more smoothly and intelligently.",
    "venus": "A pleasant working environment matters to you more than you might admit. Venus in the 6th house makes you a well-liked colleague who smooths tensions and brings grace to routine tasks, and you work best in attractive surroundings with friendly people. You notice the small comforts that make a place pleasant, and you remember the little things that matter to each person you work with. Jobs in beauty, design, wellbeing, hospitality or the arts often suit you. Unpleasant tasks get quietly postponed, and office friendships or romances can complicate the work itself. You make daily work feel civilised and even enjoyable.",
    "mars": "You attack your workload with energy and speed. Mars in the 6th house makes you a hard, driven worker who wants to clear the task list and hates being slowed down by inefficient colleagues or pointless meetings. You are the one who sighs audibly when a meeting runs over, and who has finished the task while others are still discussing it. Physical, technical or fast-paced jobs suit you well. Irritability and friction with coworkers flare up, and you push yourself until you are running on empty. You get more done than anyone, given a clear target and some independence.",
    "jupiter": "Work tends to bring you opportunities and goodwill. Jupiter in the 6th house often means friendly colleagues, a generous workplace and a job that grows as you do, particularly in health, education, service or any role that helps people. You are the one who says yes to the extra project because it sounds interesting, then finds yourself juggling four of them. You approach daily tasks with optimism and a sense of purpose. You take on more than you can handle, and the detail slips because the bigger picture interests you more. You bring good humour and open-handed generosity to the working day.",
    "saturn": "Your daily job tends to come with heavy structure: strict schedules, demanding procedures or a boss who watches closely. Saturn in the 6th house often means periods of hard, unglamorous work early on, and you learn to build good working habits through them. You remember the job where every minute was logged, and part of you still works as though someone is checking. You prefer clear rules and dislike colleagues who cut corners. You can end up trapped in a routine that no longer grows you, or accept poor conditions for too long. In the end you become the most dependable, skilled worker in any team.",
    "uranus": "Routine and you do not get along easily. Uranus in the 6th house needs flexibility in the working day, so you thrive in freelancing, remote work, technology, shift patterns or roles with constant variety. You are quick to find a smarter way round a boring task, then just as quick to grow bored of the new way. Sudden job changes are common, sometimes by choice and sometimes not. You are the colleague who modernises how a team works, and your daily work asks for freedom within some basic structure.",
    "neptune": "Your daily work needs to feel meaningful, not just functional. Neptune in the 6th house draws you towards service, healing, the arts, charities or any job where compassion is part of the routine. You pick up on colleagues' moods and often help them behind the scenes, sometimes at the expense of your own tasks. You know the sinking feeling of finding a whole afternoon has vanished while your to-do list has not moved. The difficulty is vague job descriptions, disorganised schedules and giving too much to a workplace that does not give back. You bring kindness and imagination to ordinary work.",
    "pluto": "Your relationship with daily work is intense and all-consuming. Pluto in the 6th house makes you thorough, determined and capable of transforming a failing process or department from the ground up. You know exactly who holds the power in your office, and it is rarely the person with the title. You can become embroiled in control struggles with a manager or coworker. Research, investigation, crisis and restructuring roles suit you. Your working habits can turn obsessive, and delegating anything that matters feels almost impossible. You are the person who turns a broken team around and leaves it stronger than you found it.",
    "chiron": "Work is where old feelings of inadequacy tend to surface. Chiron in the 6th house can make you doubt your competence, overwork to compensate or struggle in jobs where you feel undervalued by colleagues. A single line of criticism in an appraisal can outweigh ten lines of praise. You have probably stayed late redoing work that was already good enough. Over time you often become an exceptionally skilled helper in health, therapy or service roles. You understand how others feel when they cannot cope with the daily grind, and your working life becomes a place of healing.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in the practical details of a daily job. The North Node in the 6th house asks you to commit to a routine, develop solid skills and serve others through steady, useful work. You know the temptation to drift into daydreams or plan an escape whenever the job feels mundane. Monday mornings can feel like a small act of courage. Part of you keeps waiting for a perfect calling instead of building a workable one. Progress comes through showing up consistently, getting organised and taking pride in doing ordinary tasks well. Slowly, you build a working life you respect.",
    "lilith": "You resist being treated as a cog in someone else's machine. Lilith in the 6th house rebels against petty rules, micromanagement and unfair workloads, and you tend to call out exploitation at work that others swallow. You are the one who asks, in front of everyone, why unpaid overtime is now expected. Colleagues can find you prickly or unpredictable. You work best when you set your own methods and hours. Resentment can push you to sabotage a job you need. You change working conditions for everyone, and a role that honours your independence brings out your best work."
  },
  "money:venus": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "You spend on impulse and on the thrill of the new: the first release, the fast upgrade, the thing you wanted the moment you saw it. The thrill is in the wanting, and you can feel oddly flat once the new thing is actually yours. You attract resources by going after them directly, pitching first, naming your price and asking plainly for what you want. You are refreshingly unashamed of wanting nice things, and you back yourself with money before anyone else does. The catch is a balance built from quick yeses that you forget as fast as you made them, and a boredom with anything you already own. Money, for you, is fuel: it exists to get you somewhere new, not to sit still.",
      "taurus": "Quality matters far more to you than quantity, and you would rather own one thing that lasts than several that do not. You like money you can see and hold, and a healthy savings balance gives you an almost physical sense of calm. You remember what you paid for the things you love years later, and you still reckon they were a bargain. Resources come to you steadily through patience, loyalty and a knack for spotting lasting value. The pitfall is that comfort spending rises when life feels shaky, and you can cling to possessions, and to underpriced arrangements, long after they have stopped serving you. Slow, solid wealth suits you best, the kind you can sink into like a good armchair.",
      "gemini": "Variety is where your money goes: small treats and new interests spread across many directions rather than one big purchase. Comparing options endlessly is part of the fun for you, and your spending is full of small payments you only half recognise. Resources tend to come through talk, networking, selling and side ideas, sometimes several at once. You are quick and funny in a negotiation, and casual conversation has turned into paid work more than once. The weak spot is scattered spending, where dozens of small payments and forgotten subscriptions add up unnoticed and you lose track of which account holds what. Two or three small incomes and the freedom to change your mind will always feel richer to you than one fixed salary.",
      "cancer": "Home, food and the people you love take most of your spending, and knowing there is plenty to go round feels like wealth to you. You stock up just in case, and anything that carries family meaning is worth far more to you than its price. You save instinctively for security, and a cushion of money in the bank calms you more than any luxury could. Resources often come through caring work, property, food or family connections. The trap is emotional spending, buying comfort for yourself or treats for others when you feel low, unappreciated or worried about someone. Underneath it all, every dollar you save is a roof over someone you love, and that includes you.",
      "leo": "You like money to look good and feel generous, and nothing pleases you more than spending in a way that makes someone's face light up. Quietly treating everyone before they notice, then enjoying their protests afterwards, is very much your style. You attract resources by being visible, warm and confident about what you are worth, and people often pay willingly for your style and presence. You make money feel like a celebration, and people remember your generosity long after the moment has passed. The downside is paying for the image: picking up every bill, buying the showpiece, or funding a lifestyle designed to impress when the account quietly needed a rest. The money that pleases you most is earned by being unmistakably yourself and spent on things that match your taste.",
      "virgo": "You value what is useful, well made and fairly priced, and you tend to read the reviews before buying almost anything. Pleasure comes from a tidy budget, a good bargain and an item that does its job perfectly for years. Your budget is carefully planned, yet you still feel faintly guilty about choosing the better version of anything. Resources come through competence and reliable service rather than salesmanship, and clients return because your work is excellent. The harder side is undercharging, doing meticulous work for modest fees, and feeling a small twist of guilt every time you spend on pure enjoyment even when you can afford it. Your best purchases are the sensible ones that also, quietly, make you happy.",
      "libra": "Beauty and balance guide your spending, and you are drawn to what is elegant, harmonious and best enjoyed with someone else. Choosing between two nearly identical options can take you an age, and a second opinion is often what finally settles it. Resources come easily through charm, diplomacy and collaboration, and you are a gifted negotiator when you keep your nerve. People trust you to split a bill or a deal fairly, and everyone walks away feeling well treated. Where it goes wrong is a habit of spending to keep the peace or splitting costs evenly when the arrangement is not fair to you. Your finances look their healthiest when there are two names on the plan and your own side of the scales carries equal weight.",
      "scorpio": "Depth matters more to you than display, and you prefer a few powerful possessions to a pile of pretty ones. When someone asks what you earn, you smile and change the subject, yet you know your own balance to the penny. Resources tend to come through strategy, research, negotiation and other people's backing, and you sense very quickly who has money and who is bluffing. You are loyal and shrewd, and nobody out-waits you in a deal. The price is all or nothing behaviour: long stretches of strict control broken by an intense, secret splurge, or using money to hold power in a close relationship. Over a lifetime your finances tend to be rebuilt more than once, each time stronger and more private than before.",
      "sagittarius": "Your money goes on experiences that widen your world: learning, exploring and anything that takes you somewhere new. Your happiest purchases are the ones that open a door or teach you something, never anything sitting in a cupboard. You attract resources through optimism, teaching, publishing and contacts abroad or online, and your enthusiasm makes people want to invest in you. You are generous and open-handed, and money has a funny habit of finding its way back to you. The flip side is generosity and excitement running ahead of the numbers, booking the trip first and working out how to pay for it later. A life rich in experience sitting next to a rather thin savings account is the classic picture of this placement.",
      "capricorn": "Lasting quality is what you value most, along with possessions that quietly signal achievement and will still be worth something in years to come. Watching your savings build month by month gives you a small, private satisfaction that few people ever see. Resources come through discipline, patience and a reputation for being reliable, and senior people tend to trust you with responsibility and pay. You build security carefully, and your taste only gets better with age. What trips you up is treating pleasure as something that must be earned first, denying yourself small comforts while the balance grows well beyond what you need. Your wealth tends to grow with age, and so, eventually, does your willingness to enjoy it.",
      "aquarius": "Independence and originality are what you value, and you spend on technology, causes and things nobody else in your circle owns. Living simply suits you fine if it frees money for what you care about, and status labels bore you. Resources come through networks, communities and new ideas, often from unexpected directions. You are fair-minded and inventive with money, and you often spot an opportunity years before your friends do. The snag is detachment from money itself: forgetting bills, undervaluing comfort, or giving to the collective while your own needs wait. Money matters to you mainly as a way to stay free and to fund the people and ideas you believe in.",
      "pisces": "Music, beauty, escape and other people's needs soak up your spending, and money slips through your fingers more easily than you notice. Giving on impulse comes naturally, and so does discovering forgotten payments long after they should have stopped. Resources arrive through creative, healing or caring work, and at times through quiet good fortune that feels almost like grace. Your generosity is instinctive, and you treat money as something to be shared rather than guarded. The danger is vagueness: avoiding statements, ignoring the balance and hoping it will somehow work out, or being charmed by people who take more than they give. Kindness is your currency, and it lasts longest when it has a clear edge to it."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "You attract money partly through personal charm and appearance, and people are often drawn to hire you, pay you or help you out. A fair share of your budget goes on how you look and present yourself, from haircuts to clothes to skincare, and this can pay back in your working life. Looking your best when it counts is an expense you rarely skip, and it usually turns out to be money well spent. Your warmth is an asset, and it opens financial doors that qualifications alone would not. The trouble is spending on your image in order to feel worthy, as if the right purchase could prove your value. Nothing you could buy adds as much to your value as the ease you carry into a room.",
      "2": "Venus sits at home in the house of earning, which gives you a natural feel for money and a fond eye for good possessions. Income tends to come through pleasant, creative or beauty-related work, and pay rises often arrive without a fight because people enjoy paying you. You notice the quality and feel of something long before you ever glance at the price tag. You have a relaxed confidence about money, and oddly enough that ease seems to attract more of it. The shadow is complacency: spending freely because money has always seemed to return, or letting your standards drift upwards with every raise. Earning, owning and enjoying are all tangled together for you, and life feels good when the three stay in step.",
      "3": "Money comes to you through words, messages and local connections: writing, selling, teaching, or a pleasant knack for getting a good deal through conversation. A friendly chat often ends with you getting a better deal, and the saving rarely stays saved for long. Siblings, cousins or neighbours can be part of your financial story, through shared purchases, small loans or tips about work. You can talk your way into better rates and make friends of every supplier. The difficulty is spending a little on everything that catches your interest and ending the month unsure where it all went. Small sums matter more than they seem, and one good conversation can easily turn into your best-paid week.",
      "4": "A beautiful home matters more to you than almost anything else money can buy, and much of your spending goes on furniture, décor, good food and hosting. Property and family resources can bring you comfort, including inherited objects or practical help from parents. Making your space beautiful feels like a treat, and you would happily go without elsewhere to get it exactly right. The home you create tends to grow in value while holding the people you love. The risk is pouring money into the home as emotional reassurance, or relying on family support longer than suits your independence. Property and a settled base sit at the centre of your wealth, and your own front door is where you feel richest.",
      "5": "Pleasure is a major budget line for you: fun, romance, the people you love and whatever sparks your creativity. You can earn through art, entertainment, performance or anything that feels like play, and work you enjoy tends to pay better for you than work you tolerate. You love spending on the people you care about and treating them lavishly. Money in your hands can be joyful rather than grim. The danger is gambling, speculation or chasing a good time, where the thrill of the spend outweighs any sense of the numbers. Fun is part of your income as well as your spending, and you are happiest when there is enough left over for the next good time.",
      "6": "Steady, pleasant work and good relationships with colleagues and clients bring money your way. You spend happily on tools, wellbeing and anything that makes your daily routine smoother, calmer and more pleasant to live with day after day. Keeping neatly on top of everything you owe gives you a quiet glow of pleasure. Your work is so reliable and gracious that people are glad to pay for it. The catch is valuing your service too modestly, doing lovely work for rates that do not reflect its quality, or staying in a cosy job long after it has stopped paying fairly. Useful, beautiful work is your natural way of earning, and it pays best once your prices catch up with its quality.",
      "7": "Partnership shapes your finances strongly: money often improves through marriage, business partners or good long-term clients. You tend to share costs and make big purchases together, and a generous partner can noticeably raise your standard of living. You feel noticeably richer once life is shared with someone and the costs are carried together. Negotiating contracts comes naturally, because you sense what the other side wants and find the agreeable middle. The partnerships you build are usually fair and profitable, with both of you coming out ahead. The pitfall is letting someone else set your spending level, or tying your sense of worth to what a partner earns and provides. However generous the other person turns out to be, your own financial footing still matters in every arrangement.",
      "8": "Other people's money tends to favour you: a partner's income, gifts, inheritance, or favourable terms on loans and investments. You are good at attracting backing, and a surprising amount of your comfort comes from money that did not start as your own. Quiet help from the people close to you, arriving just when it is needed, turns up more often than you like to admit. Your spending can be private and intensely felt, and you rarely discuss the details. People trust you with joint money, and it tends to grow while you are looking after it. The weak spot is dependence, becoming comfortable on another person's money and losing sight of what you earn and control yourself. Merged money suits you, provided the balance stays honest and nobody ends up owning the other.",
      "9": "Travel, study, publishing and anything that broadens your outlook take a large share of your money, and a trip abroad feels like money well spent rather than an indulgence. Income can come through teaching, foreign contacts, tourism, law or work in higher education. Going without elsewhere so you can learn, explore and broaden your world strikes you as an obvious choice. You value freedom and meaning more than ownership, and new experiences please you far more than new possessions. Your curiosity can become a portable, international way of earning. The trap is funding the next adventure or qualification before the last one has paid for itself. Knowledge and distance tend to pay you back, often from places you never planned to visit.",
      "10": "Money follows your reputation: you attract income by being liked and respected in your field, and public roles tend to pay well for you. You value the signs of quiet success, and you like what you own to reflect how far you have come. Working in beauty, design, diplomacy, hospitality or the arts can be profitable, and senior people often help your career along. Your charm and good taste at work raise your earnings steadily. The downside is spending to keep up appearances at a level your career has not yet reached. Over the years the polish and the substance catch up with each other, and so does your salary.",
      "11": "Friends and networks bring you money, through introductions, group ventures or a well-connected social circle. You spend on memberships, social events, gifts for friends and causes you believe in, and you enjoy funding shared goals. Quietly covering more than your share for the sake of the group is a very familiar move. Your long-term financial wishes often come true through other people rather than solo effort. Around you, friends end up swapping skills, work and favours, and money moves generously in every direction. The harder side is spending to belong: matching friends' lifestyles, joining in on shared costs you cannot afford, or lending money to people you find it hard to refuse. The friends worth keeping value you more than your wallet, and they are usually the ones who bring the best opportunities.",
      "12": "You tend to keep your spending and your pleasures private, and there can be hidden costs, secret treats or very discreet generosity. Money comes through behind-the-scenes, creative or caring work, sometimes through charities, hospitals, retreats or institutions. Your kindest giving usually goes unsigned, and there is often a money matter you have quietly put off looking at. Giving quietly feels better to you than being thanked in public. You are a gentle, invisible benefactor, and help often reaches you in return when you least expect it. Where it goes wrong is financial blind spots: bills left unread, small costs forgotten, and a hazy relationship with the numbers. Your own bank statements need the gentleness you show everyone else."
    }
  },
  "money:jupiter": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "Your financial luck comes from acting first: starting the business, applying before the advert closes, backing yourself while others are still hesitating. Opportunity grows whenever you take the lead and trust your instincts on new ventures. Your ventures tend to begin in a rush of excitement, decided in a moment and announced before any doubt can set in. You are happiest being first into a market, and some of your best money comes from ideas nobody else dared to try. The price is impatience with slow growth, jumping in and out of investments, or overspending on impulse because the next chance always feels bigger than the last. Your fortunes are self-made, and the good ones come from ideas you stuck with past the exciting first month.",
      "taurus": "Growth for you is slow, solid and tangible: property, savings, land, and assets that increase over decades. You have a knack for recognising lasting value and buying well, and what you choose tends to hold its worth for years. Something bought wisely long ago and quietly climbing in value is the kind of win that suits you best. Luck tends to reward patience rather than bold moves. The wealth you build is comfortable and dependable, and it pays for a generous, pleasurable life. The flip side is indulgence, a lifestyle that expands faster than your income, or a stubborn refusal to sell when the time has come. Abundance for you is something you can touch, solid and lasting, and built from years of patience.",
      "gemini": "Several streams of income suit you better than one, and luck often arrives through conversations, contacts and timely information. You spot opportunities in trading, writing, media, teaching or anything built on ideas, and you hear about openings before most people do. You hear about an opening, pitch for it the same day and have the work done before others have made up their minds. You are a natural connector who turns gossip, news and contacts into profit. What trips you up is spreading yourself too thinly, running too many small ventures at once, and spending on the latest scheme before the previous one has earned anything. The gains only add up once you finish enough of what you start.",
      "cancer": "Financial luck is tied to home, family and security: property, family businesses, inheritances, food or care services can all be generous to you. You tend to save instinctively and feel richest when the people you love are well provided for. Your generosity is protective and warm, and it goes wherever it keeps someone safe. Over time you can build a family fortune, large or small, that shelters people for generations. The snag is overspending on family, or holding on to cash so tightly out of fear that it never gets the chance to grow. In the end it is growth, not just saving, that makes you feel safe.",
      "leo": "Luck comes when you are visible and confident, whether through performance, leadership, creative projects or a business built around your personality. You spend big and give big, and people often reward that warmth with loyalty, custom and opportunity. Treating everyone and waving away every offer to share the cost gives you real delight. Believing in your own worth tends to raise your income directly. You share success easily, and people around you aim higher because you do. The danger is extravagance: grand gestures, luxury purchases and a lifestyle designed to impress, funded by the assumption that more money is always on its way. The generosity people love in you works best when it comes out of surplus rather than pride.",
      "virgo": "Your prosperity grows through skill, detail and useful service. Small improvements, careful budgets and a reputation for excellent work compound nicely over time, and health, admin, editing or practical trades can be surprisingly profitable. Spotting the small saving everyone else missed, and letting it add up month after month, is a typical win. You are generous with help, advice and time as much as with cash. Your best money comes from being the person who fixes what others cannot. The trouble is worrying about money even when you have plenty, and letting perfectionism stop you from reaching for the larger opportunity when it comes. Careful work like yours deserves a bigger stage and a bigger fee than you usually ask for.",
      "libra": "Money expands through partnerships, contracts and people who simply like you. Good deals, fair negotiations and joint ventures bring your luck, and a spouse, business partner or loyal client often opens important doors. Often you get the better price simply by being lovely to deal with. You enjoy spending on beauty, style and pleasures shared with the people you love. You are a gifted dealmaker, and your arrangements usually leave everyone better off. The shadow is overspending to keep relationships pleasant, and leaning on a partner's money or judgement instead of developing your own financial confidence. Your own interests deserve the same generous attention you give everyone else's at the negotiating table.",
      "scorpio": "Depth and strategy are the source of your financial luck: investments, research, shared finances, insurance, and other people's resources. You can turn around a failing situation, or benefit from money that passes through a crisis, such as buying low when everyone else is panicking. Growth is often hidden until it is substantial, because you keep your plans to yourself. While everyone else is still guessing, you already know exactly where the money sits and who controls it. You are shrewd and resilient, and you understand where the power in any deal sits. The difficulty is extremes: betting heavily on a single outcome, or letting money become a tool for control in close relationships. Money in your hands carries influence, and people notice whether you use it cleanly.",
      "sagittarius": "Faith in the future is your biggest financial asset, and opportunities tend to arrive through travel, education, publishing or connections abroad. You are open-handed, and money often returns to you in unexpected ways, through contacts far from home or chances that seem to come out of nowhere. Big-picture thinking suits your income more than detailed bookkeeping. Saying yes to a distant opportunity on instinct alone is the kind of leap that has paid off for you before. People catch your enthusiasm, and backers buy into your vision as much as your figures. The risk is overconfidence: expensive trips, overpromised plans and a habit of assuming that good fortune will always cover the gap. The vision wins you the deal, and a plan on paper is what makes the money stay.",
      "capricorn": "Jupiter works slowly but reliably here: wealth grows through discipline, long-term planning and a steady rise in position. You are good at building assets that last, such as a pension, property or a respected business with your name on it. Watching what you owe shrink and what you own grow, year after year, gives you a deep, private pleasure. Luck often comes later in life, and once it arrives it tends to stay. In time you become the trusted, well-paid professional who has earned every step. The cost is excessive caution, turning down good opportunities because the risk feels too high, or measuring your worth only by what you have achieved. A little ease and generosity along the way costs you less than you fear, and the fortune keeps growing regardless.",
      "aquarius": "Networks, technology and ideas ahead of their time bring your luck. Money can grow through online ventures, group projects, innovation or unusual income sources that others overlook, such as a niche digital product or a cooperative. You are generous towards causes and communities, and you like wealth that benefits more than one person. Your ideas tend to pay off because you saw the trend first. People around you are often sceptical when you first share an idea, and later you are proved right. The catch is erratic finances, sudden windfalls followed by sudden losses, and backing a brilliant concept without checking whether it has a workable plan. Brilliant ideas become money in the bank once they are given a bit of ordinary structure.",
      "pisces": "Your luck with money often feels mysterious: help arrives when it is most needed, and opportunities come through intuition, creativity or compassionate work. You are lavishly generous and find it very hard to refuse anyone in need. Giving quietly to someone who is struggling, only to find unexpected money coming back to you soon after, is a pattern you know well. Spiritual, artistic, musical or healing ventures can be surprisingly profitable. You trust money to flow, you give without fear, and it tends to come back. The pitfall is vague boundaries: lending without records, trusting the wrong schemes, and letting money drift away unnoticed while you look elsewhere. Practical numbers are the one thing faith cannot replace, and keeping half an eye on them lets the good fortune keep flowing."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "Opportunity comes to you personally: people offer you chances because you seem capable, cheerful and trustworthy. Your own presence and initiative are your main financial assets, and self-employment or a public-facing role can suit you well. First impressions often lead directly to income. Casual conversations have a way of turning into offers you were not expecting, simply because people like what they see in you. Your optimism is contagious, and clients and employers want to back you. The weak spot is overspending on yourself and your lifestyle, trusting that natural luck will always cover whatever you spend. Your big personality is your best financial asset, and it works hardest with a sound budget standing behind it.",
      "2": "Jupiter in the house of earning gives a strong capacity to make money, and income tends to expand over the course of your life. You attract resources easily, often through several talents at once, and you enjoy spending on comfort and quality. More than once something you simply enjoyed doing has turned into a second income. Your sense of self-worth is generally healthy, which helps you ask for fair pay. Wealth feels like a natural part of your life, and you share it easily. The trap is that easy money leaves easily too, and a steadily rising lifestyle can swallow every pay rise before any of it is saved. The abundance is there, though it only becomes lasting wealth when part of it is left alone to grow.",
      "3": "Income opportunities arrive through communication: writing, sales, teaching, media or local business. Luck often comes through a timely conversation, or through someone close by who knows someone looking for your skills. Many small ventures can add up to substantial growth, and you are good at spotting a quick deal. You are a lively, persuasive trader of ideas and information. The downside is spending freely on whatever catches your curiosity, and scattering your earning energy across too many side projects. Following one good lead all the way through pays far more than chasing every one.",
      "4": "Luck is strongest around property and family resources: bricks and mortar, a home-based business, or support and inheritance from relatives. Your wealth tends to increase in the second half of life, and a larger or better home is often a clear marker of your success. You are generous with hospitality and like a full table. Family tends to gather around you, and you always offer more than anyone expects. You build a secure base that supports your whole family financially and emotionally. The harder side is overspending on the house itself, with renovations, extensions and furnishings that grow faster than the budget. Land and home are where your wealth takes root, and it helps when the foundations are as sound as the décor.",
      "5": "Money can grow through creativity, entertainment, children's services or ventures that feel like play. You are often lucky with speculation, and a flair for enjoying life attracts generous people and profitable opportunities. You spend lavishly on pleasure, on play and on the people you love most. A stroke of luck is, for you, a reason to celebrate with everyone around you. Your talents and your sheer enjoyment of life can turn into income. Where it goes wrong is gambling and risky investments, where a few lucky wins convince you that the odds are always on your side. A calculated bet and a thrill feel identical in the moment, and your luck holds longer when you can tell them apart.",
      "6": "Work itself is your main source of opportunity: a good job, generous employers, and steady growth through reliable service. Health, wellness, admin or practical trades can be profitable for you, and colleagues often pass good work your way. Daily habits are where your wealth builds, one well-managed task and one sensible routine at a time. Quietly fixing what everyone else only complains about tends to be followed, soon after, by a promotion. You end up valued and well paid because everything runs better when you are around. The price is overcommitting, taking on more work than you can sustain, or spending on wellness products and services beyond what you use. The energy that earns your money is itself your most valuable resource.",
      "7": "Other people are often the route to your financial growth: a prosperous partner, generous clients, or a strong business partnership. Contracts and negotiations tend to go your way, and legal or advisory work can be lucrative. Your income often jumps the year you sign with the right agent, client or business partner, and you walk out of negotiations with better terms than anyone expected. Marriage or a committed partnership can significantly raise your standard of living. You attract backers and partners who multiply what you can achieve alone. The flip side is relying on others to provide, or overspending as a couple because together you feel invincible. Partners whose judgement matches their generosity are the ones who make you rich.",
      "8": "Luck flows through shared money: a partner's income, investments, inheritance, insurance or backing from others. You can do very well in finance, banking, tax or managing other people's assets. Backing that others struggle to secure tends to come through for you, and help from shared resources arrives at the right moment. Loans tend to be granted, and debts are sometimes cleared in ways you did not expect. You grow joint resources wisely and often end up helping others with theirs. What trips you up is overleveraging: borrowing too much because credit comes easily, or depending on money that is not yours. Every loan is also a promise, and the growth lasts when those promises are kept as carefully as the gains are counted.",
      "9": "Distant places bring you opportunity: foreign clients, travel, higher education, publishing or law. Your beliefs and optimism attract good fortune, and taking a chance on a distant opportunity often pays off handsomely. Work from far away, or a chance to share what you know, tends to arrive just when you need it. Knowledge is your most profitable asset, and qualifications tend to raise your income. Over time you can build an international way of earning that feels meaningful as well as lucrative. The snag is spending heavily on travel and study, and trusting a big vision so completely that the practical details of payment are ignored. The lessons you bring home from far away are what end up paying the bills.",
      "10": "Career is your main route to wealth: promotions, public recognition and a strong reputation raise your income steadily. Authority figures tend to help you, and senior or visible roles suit you well. Someone senior tends to put your name forward at the right time, and your earnings rise in noticeable steps. Success is noticeable and generally well rewarded, sometimes with titles and perks as well as pay. You tend to end up in charge, and you are the kind of boss who shares the bonus. The danger is overreaching, taking on status and its costs before the income supports them, or tying your self-worth entirely to your job title and salary. Reputation is the engine of your prosperity, and it runs best on solid ground.",
      "11": "Friends, networks and groups are your source of luck, and the right contact often brings the right financial opportunity. You can profit through organisations, technology, community ventures or crowdfunding. Much of your best-paid work began with an introduction from someone in your circle. Your long-term financial hopes tend to be realised most readily when you share them with others. The trouble is spending too much on social life, and lending money or backing friends' schemes out of loyalty rather than judgement. When the group succeeds, you tend to succeed right along with it.",
      "12": "Financial protection tends to arrive without fanfare: unexpected help in hard moments, or resources that appear just when you need them most. Work behind the scenes, in charities, hospitals, institutions or spiritual settings, can be rewarding in every sense. When money runs short, a refund or an unexpected payment tends to appear soon after. You are generous in secret and rarely want credit. You trust that you will be provided for, and that trust seems to be answered. The shadow is losing track of money, giving too much away, or ignoring financial reality because you assume things will always work out. Faith looks after you, and a glance at the numbers now and then makes its job a good deal easier."
    }
  },
  "money:house2": {
    "sun": "Earning is central to your identity: your sense of who you are is closely tied to what you produce, own and can provide. You want to build your own income and be proud of it, and financial independence matters to you more than to most people. Every step up in what you earn feels like a personal victory, and you remember each milestone exactly. You have a strong, healthy confidence in your value and the drive to back it up with results. The difficulty is measuring yourself by your bank balance, feeling diminished when money is short and overly pleased with yourself when it is plentiful. Underneath the salary and the savings sits a sense of worth that does not rise and fall with them.",
    "moon": "Your income and your emotions move together: money feels secure when you feel secure, and anxious when life is unsettled. You tend to keep a savings cushion as emotional protection, and an empty account can feel like an empty larder. Earnings can fluctuate like tides, with busy and quiet months, and work in food, care, hospitality or the home suits you. You are an instinctive provider who always makes sure there is enough. On quiet weeks you check your balance more often, as if looking at it could make it rise. The risk is comfort spending, and holding on to belongings for sentimental reasons long after they have any use. A full cupboard and a little money set aside will always be your idea of peace.",
    "mercury": "You earn through your mind and your mouth: writing, selling, teaching, negotiating, coding, or any work built on information. You think about money often, and you like to track, compare prices and plan purchases in detail. Hunting down the best deal, and passing it on to the people you care about, is second nature. Several income streams tend to suit you better than one fixed salary. You are a sharp, practical thinker who can explain a budget, write a winning proposal and spot a better deal in seconds. The cost is overthinking financial decisions until the chance has gone, or talking yourself into purchases with clever justifications. Your knowledge is an asset, and people pay well for the way you explain things.",
    "venus": "Money tends to come to you pleasantly, through charm, creativity or work connected to beauty, art, food or comfort. You enjoy owning lovely things and spend readily on quality, preferring one good piece to several cheap ones. Waiting to afford the thing you truly love feels far better to you than settling for something lesser today. Your self-worth is usually steady, and you do not easily undervalue what you offer. You attract resources with an easy grace and enjoy them without guilt. The catch is a comfortable relationship with spending that slides into indulgence, buying beautiful things because they make you feel loved or valued. Pleasure and earning feed each other in your life, as long as the things you buy are ones you treasure.",
    "mars": "You go after money energetically, working hard and earning through initiative, competition, sport, trades or physical effort. You want control over your own income and hate waiting for payment or permission. Your spending is quick and decisive: once you want something, you buy it. Fighting for money you are owed fires you up in a way that surprises people. You are a determined earner who fights for fair pay and wins it. The pitfall is impulse purchases, arguments about money, and a tendency to take financial risks when you feel impatient or angry. All that fire builds wealth fast when it goes into earning, and burns through it just as fast when it goes into spending.",
    "jupiter": "Your earning potential is large and tends to grow over time, often through generosity, teaching, advising or big ideas. Money comes relatively easily to you, and you share it freely with friends and family. When someone close is short of money, you are usually the first to help without being asked. You have a healthy confidence in your own value and rarely feel poor for long. You are open-handed and prosperous, and your optimism attracts more opportunity. The weak spot is overspending in the belief that more is always coming, and a comfortable lifestyle that absorbs every increase in income. The abundance only turns into wealth once some of it stays put.",
    "saturn": "Money comes through effort, patience and time, and early financial struggle often builds discipline in you. You take earning seriously, tend to save carefully, and rarely buy anything on a whim. You keep a close, steady watch on what you have, and you know where you stand without checking. Security grows steadily, often more in later life than in youth. You are the reliable builder of lasting wealth, with a pension, savings and assets that nobody can take from you. The trap is fear of scarcity: undercharging, feeling that you never have enough, or refusing yourself small pleasures even when your accounts say otherwise. Your worth was solid long before the savings were.",
    "uranus": "Unconventional income is typical for you, and it can change overnight: freelance work, technology, inventions, or several short-lived ventures in succession. Windfalls and unexpected expenses both arrive without warning, and your financial year rarely looks like the last one. What pays your way one year can be something you had never even heard of the year before. Freedom matters more to you than a steady wage, and a boss controlling your earnings feels unbearable. You find original ways to make money that others would never have considered. The downside is instability, with erratic spending and a restless urge to change how you earn just as things settle. A safety net underneath is what lets the experiments keep going.",
    "neptune": "A hazy quality surrounds your money: income can come through creative, spiritual, musical or healing work, but it is often hard to predict or measure. You tend to be generous and idealistic about possessions, and material things rarely feel as important as meaning. Budgeting can seem dull or confusing, so you sometimes avoid it. Money matters can go ignored for weeks while you give your time freely to something or someone that moves you. Some of your best earnings come from imagination and compassion, and people admire how little money rules you. The harder side is vagueness: underestimating costs, overlooking statements, or being drawn into schemes that promise easy money. Clear finances are what give the dreamy, creative work room to breathe.",
    "pluto": "Your relationship with money is intense and transformative. You can build financial power through research, strategy or investment, and there are often periods when you lose and rebuild almost everything. Possessions carry deep emotional weight, and you hold on tightly or let go completely. Once you decide to clear a debt, you pay it off with a ferocity that surprises everyone, including you. You have remarkable resilience and an instinct for turning scarcity into strength. Where it goes wrong is control: using money to feel powerful, or fearing loss so strongly that it drives obsessive saving or reckless risk. Power over money is yours to build, and how honestly you use it shapes the whole story.",
    "chiron": "Money and self-worth carry an old wound: perhaps early scarcity, or a sense that what you offered was never quite valued enough. You tend to undercharge, feel uneasy about earning well, or swing between overspending and strict denial. Receiving payment or gifts can feel strangely uncomfortable. Your voice drops a little when you say what you want, and you settle for less before anyone has asked you to. Once you work through it, you become wise about value, both your own and other people's. Even then the old pattern returns at times, accepting less or apologising for what you ask. You often end up urging others, firmly, to ask for what they are really worth.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in building your own resources and self-worth. Learning to earn, save and value what you have is part of your life's direction, even if standing on your own financial feet feels unfamiliar at first. Paying for something entirely with money you earned yourself brings a surprisingly deep satisfaction. Relying on other people's money, or on shared arrangements you never examine, is a habit you are meant to outgrow. Steady, practical income that is yours alone brings a calm nothing else quite matches. The flip side is slipping back into old patterns of dependence or intensity around shared money. Money that is entirely yours feels like arriving home.",
    "lilith": "You have a rebellious relationship with money and possessions: you resist being told how to earn, what to own or what you are worth. Other people's judgements about your income or spending can provoke fierce reactions. Sometimes you reject material values outright, and at other times you embrace luxury defiantly. You define wealth entirely on your own terms and refuse to be bought. What trips you up is shame or secrecy about money, and hidden anger when others try to control your finances. Claiming what you are worth, out loud and without apology, is the whole point here."
  },
  "money:house8": {
    "sun": "Shared money is a central theme for you: partners' finances, investments, inheritances and joint accounts shape your life strongly. You are good at managing other people's resources and can thrive in finance, insurance, tax or estate work. People bring you their most confusing money questions, and you make sense of them quickly and calmly. Trust and control around money matter enormously to you. People hand you the keys to shared money because you handle it straight. The snag is power struggles over shared assets, or identifying too closely with what you control rather than what you earn yourself. Your reputation rests on handling other people's money with the integrity you expect from them.",
    "moon": "Your emotional security is tied to shared resources: a partner's income, family money, or the safety net of a joint account. You feel strongly about financial trust and can be badly hurt when money is kept secret from you. Inheritance and family finances carry strong emotional weight, and settling an estate can stir up old feelings. With the right partner, money becomes a source of safety for you both rather than a battleground. The danger is emotional dependence on other people's money, or anxiety about debt that spikes whenever you feel insecure. The deepest security you find is the kind that would survive even if the joint account did not.",
    "mercury": "You think strategically about shared money: investments, taxes, contracts and financial research are your home ground. You enjoy understanding how money moves beneath the surface, from interest rates to the terms buried in an agreement. Before signing anything that ties up money, you read every line and question whatever does not quite add up. Negotiating loans, settlements or divisions of property suits your sharp, probing mind. You are the person everyone trusts to read the small print and find the hidden cost. The trouble is suspicion, overanalysing a partner's spending, or keeping financial information to yourself as a quiet form of control. All that insight works best out in the open, where a partner can see the same numbers you can.",
    "venus": "Shared resources tend to favour you: generous partners, gifts, inheritance, or favourable terms on a mortgage or loan. You attract financial support easily and often benefit from joint ventures and pooled money. Help from someone close arriving at exactly the right moment is a familiar story in your life. Sharing finances with someone you love can feel pleasurable and bonding. Joint ventures and pooled savings tend to leave you both better off. The shadow is getting comfortable in dependence, letting a partner cover costs in a way that slowly shifts the balance of power between you. Fairness in both directions is what keeps the arrangement sweet.",
    "mars": "You fight for your share of joint resources and can be forceful in negotiations over debts, settlements, divorces or inheritances. You are energetic about investing and comfortable with financial risk, sometimes more than your partners are. Money conflicts in close relationships can become heated and fast. Your pulse rises the moment you sense someone making money decisions that affect you without asking first. You are a courageous and effective advocate for fair division, and you do not let anyone take advantage. The difficulty is aggressive borrowing, impulsive investments, or battles over shared property that cost more than they win. The fights worth having are about fairness, not about winning.",
    "jupiter": "Other people's money tends to expand your life: a prosperous partner, a generous inheritance, or investments that grow well over time. Credit comes easily to you, and financial backing often arrives the week a project needs it. Lenders and backers tend to say yes to you, and money you set aside has a habit of quietly growing while you look elsewhere. You can do well managing assets for others, as an adviser, banker or trustee. You multiply shared wealth wisely, and those who trust you with money are glad they did. The risk is overconfidence with debt, borrowing too freely because you trust that good fortune will continue. What is owed matters as much as what is gained, and your luck holds when you treat it that way.",
    "saturn": "Debts, taxes, loans and joint obligations feel heavy and serious to you, and they demand careful attention. You tend to be cautious about merging money and slow to trust a partner with your resources. Even after years together you like to keep something of your own, and any shared financial commitment feels like a very serious step. Inheritances can arrive late or with conditions attached. You are a meticulous manager of joint finances who pays off debt and keeps everything in order. The cost is fear of dependence, refusing help or holding financial control so tightly that closeness suffers. Trust builds slowly for you, like savings, and it becomes just as solid.",
    "uranus": "Joint finances bring surprises: sudden windfalls, unexpected inheritances, or abrupt changes in a partner's income. You value independence even inside shared arrangements and often resist a traditional joint account. Shared money can swing without warning, rising suddenly one month and shifting just as abruptly the next. Investments in technology or unusual areas can pay off well, sometimes spectacularly. Your money arrangements with a partner are often unusual but workable, with room for both of you to stay free. The catch is instability, with debts or shared resources changing without warning, and a tendency to pull away from financial commitments at short notice. A little shared stability underneath means the surprises stay surprises instead of turning into crises.",
    "neptune": "Clarity is hard to come by in shared money: unclear agreements, hidden debts, or a partner's finances that are never fully visible. You tend to be trusting and generous with joint resources, sometimes to a fault. You tend to give and lend on trust, and the details of who owes what can quietly fade from view. Your intuition about investments can be surprisingly good when you follow it with care. Your compassion is practical, and you are often the one who helps a friend out of a financial hole. The pitfall is deception or self-deception, signing papers without reading them or supporting someone financially without clear limits. Seeing the figures clearly is one of the most loving things you can do with shared money.",
    "pluto": "Power and money are closely intertwined for you in shared finances. You can build significant wealth through investment, strategy, or managing other people's resources, and you understand financial power instinctively. In every relationship you enter, you know who controls the money, often before a word about it has been said. Inheritances, debts or a partner's fortunes can transform your life completely. Untangling your finances from someone else's can feel like a death and a rebirth at once. The weak spot is control battles, financial manipulation, or all-or-nothing risks with joint money that leave little room for trust. Financial power is always in the room with you, and integrity is what stops it turning on you.",
    "chiron": "An old hurt lives in your experience of shared money: perhaps debt that shaped your childhood, a painful inheritance, or a betrayal of financial trust. You tend to feel vulnerable when depending on others' resources, and loans or joint accounts can stir up anxiety. The thought of relying on someone else for money makes your stomach tighten, even when they have already offered. Once that pain turns into wisdom, you become skilled at helping others through debt or shared finances. The trap is repeating the old wound, choosing arrangements where you give too much or trust too little. Honest conversations about money, once so hard, can become one of your quiet strengths.",
    "northNode": "Learning to share resources and trust others with money is where your growth lies. Letting someone else carry part of the cost, or pooling what you have, can feel strangely exposing at first. Joint finances, investments and financial partnerships are part of your life's direction, even if you have always preferred complete self-reliance. Merging money with a partner, taking on a sensible mortgage, or accepting financial backing for a project can mark turning points. Slowly you discover that what you build together can outgrow anything you would manage alone. The downside is clinging to the comfort of doing everything yourself. Opening your resources to someone else is the unfamiliar step that changes everything.",
    "lilith": "You resist financial control from others and feel strongly about keeping your own money separate, even within committed relationships. Shared finances can bring power struggles, secrets or taboos, such as undisclosed debts or unspoken resentment about who pays for what. Having money that is truly your own feels essential, and the idea of asking permission to spend sends a jolt through you. You refuse to be financially dominated and insist on fairness in every arrangement. The harder side is secrecy, hidden accounts, or using money as a weapon in close bonds. Dragging hidden money matters into daylight is where your power comes back."
  },
  "home:moon": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "Emotionally you react fast, and home feels safest when you can say what you feel the moment you feel it. Your temper flares, something sharp gets said, and a few minutes later you are warm and caring again as if nothing happened. Early on you probably learned to look after yourself, and being fussed over or tucked in too tightly still makes you itch to leave the room. When a family member needs defending, you are first to the door, fierce and completely loyal. Slower, heavier moods test you, though, and someone who needs days to talk something through can leave you restless and impatient. What home asks of you is to let a feeling breathe a little longer before you act on it.",
      "taurus": "Emotional security for you is physical: comfort you can feel, familiar things around you, simple pleasures and a home that stays much the same from year to year. When something in your space changes without warning, you notice at once, and it nags at you for days. Family love, in your world, means a hot meal, a warm hand on the shoulder and simply being there, rather than long speeches. People feel fed and held in your home, and they tend to stay longer than they planned. Change is the hard part, since a house move or a new person in the household can unsettle you for months. You are drawn to build a home that lasts and to become the steady ground others lean on.",
      "gemini": "You feel at home where there is conversation, a steady flow of news and ideas, and always something going on. Staying in touch with the people you love keeps you steady, and a home that goes silent for too long starts to feel wrong. Emotional safety comes from talking a feeling through, often while doing three other things. Your childhood home may have been busy, changeable or divided, which made you quick to adapt. In your family you are usually the one carrying the news and lightening a heavy mood with a story. Hurt, though, tends to get explained, analysed and filed away rather than felt. Ease comes when the easy talk goes all the way down to the heart.",
      "cancer": "Family sits at the centre of your emotional life, and home is where you go to recover from everything else. You remember what matters to each person you love, keep the keepsakes others forget and can sense from the smallest signal when someone close is struggling. Mothering is instinctive for you, and it reaches everyone who comes close, not only family. Guests relax the moment they walk through your door, often without knowing why. Old family hurts linger for years, and when home feels threatened you retreat into your shell and go quietly cold. Building the nest you always wanted matters to you, and so does letting others care for you in return.",
      "leo": "You need to feel cherished at home, the one whose presence lights up the house and whose efforts do not go unnoticed. You put your heart into making family moments special, then wait, a little too hopefully, for someone to notice how lovely it all is. As a child you likely thrived on praise and felt it keenly whenever attention moved to someone else. Your warmth and generosity make every family gathering feel like a celebration. When a relative takes you for granted, though, the hurt comes out as a dignified sulk rather than an honest word. Deep down you want to be loved at home for who you are, not only for everything you give.",
      "virgo": "Feeling safe at home, for you, means order: things in their place and a routine everyone can rely on. You spot what needs doing before anyone else notices, and you like to leave everything ready so that each day starts right. Care for your family comes through practical things, the small acts of help that keep everyone well and running smoothly. You may have grown up as the helpful child who saw what needed doing and did it without being asked. Worry, however, tends to leak out as criticism, and relatives feel judged when you are only anxious about them. Home life softens when a little mess is allowed to be enough.",
      "libra": "A peaceful, attractive home is essential to your emotional balance, and raised voices or visual clutter unsettle you more than most. When tension rises at home, you step in to help each side feel heard, then work quietly to soften the mood. Chores, attention and affection need to feel fairly shared for you to relax. Living alone rarely suits you for long, as you feel most secure sharing a home with someone. Everyone in your household tends to feel considered and gracefully looked after. Keeping the peace at any price is the trap, since smoothed over tension builds into resentment. Harmony at home, for you, grows from the truth being spoken there.",
      "scorpio": "Your emotional bonds with family run deep and private, and you need a home where you can close the door and be completely unguarded. You sense what goes unsaid in your family, understood far more as a child than anyone told you, and keep it all to yourself. Trust inside the household is everything, and a betrayal by a relative is carried for a very long time. Childhood may have held intense feelings or a strong, complicated tie to one parent. In a crisis, family members turn to you because you do not flinch. Feeling exposed, however, makes you possessive or suspicious. What you long for is a bond where someone sees all of you and stays.",
      "sagittarius": "Wide open space matters to your emotional wellbeing, and a house that feels like a cage makes you miserable within days. When family tension builds, your instinct is to escape somewhere new, and part of you is always ready to go. Family life suits you when it is warm, funny and open to guests, travel and new ideas. You may have moved often, grown up between cultures or left home early to see the world. Children raised around you tend to grow up curious and optimistic. Heavy emotional scenes, though, make you reach for the door or a joke. Staying present with feelings that do not resolve quickly is where your home life deepens.",
      "capricorn": "Security, for you, is built rather than given, and you feel safe once your finances are in order and the household stands on solid ground. You keep track of everything that matters, and you quietly make sure everyone's obligations are covered. Your family may have expected maturity from you early, so you learned to keep feelings contained and get on with things. Love, in your hands, looks like responsibility: planning, providing and turning up when it counts. Relatives can mistake your composure for coldness when in fact you feel a great deal and say little. Warmth grows in you with age. Letting yourself be looked after, not only doing the looking after, is part of feeling at home.",
      "aquarius": "Space within family life is essential to you: a place of your own and relatives who accept that you are a little different. Traditional family occasions can feel like a performance to you, and you often feel more at home among people you have chosen. Home works best as an unconventional base where people drop by and nobody enforces tradition for its own sake. Your upbringing may have felt emotionally cool or unusual in structure. Family members are free to be themselves around you, and you never judge a choice that breaks the mould. Needy displays of emotion, however, send you retreating into your head. Closeness that still leaves room to breathe is what makes you feel safe.",
      "pisces": "Home is your refuge from a world that feels too loud, and you need somewhere soft, quiet and a little dreamy to recover. Coming home, you know at once that something is wrong, long before anyone says a word. You absorb the moods of everyone in the household, and a parent's or partner's sadness can sit in your own chest all evening. Mothering flows from you as compassion and seemingly endless patience, and nobody has to pretend in your home. Boundaries are the hard part, as you take on family problems as your own and lose track of what you need. A sanctuary that protects your sensitivity, rather than draining it, is what your emotional life keeps reaching for."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "Your feelings show on your face, and the family always knows within seconds when something is wrong. When you are having a bad day, the whole atmosphere at home shifts with you. Home needs to be a place where you can be as you are, moods and all, without explaining yourself. A strong mother or early carer shaped how you see yourself, and people often say you have their expressions. You carry a sense of home with you, making any new place feel familiar within hours. Household tension, though, lands very personally, as if every tense moment were about you. Knowing your own emotional needs and meeting them without apology is central to your security.",
      "2": "Emotional safety is tied closely to money and possessions for you, and knowing you have enough put by calms you more than reassurance ever could. The things that carry memories stay with you through every change, because they hold part of your history. Your mother or early home probably taught you strong habits around spending or saving, and you still hear that voice whenever you spend. Home under your care feels comfortable, well provided for and plentiful. Things are also how you soothe feelings, so an anxious spell often ends with something new bought for comfort. Trusting your own worth as much as your bank balance is what makes you feel secure.",
      "3": "Siblings, cousins and neighbours play a big part in your sense of belonging. You know the familiar faces around you, keep up with everyone's news and stay in easy, regular contact with the people you grew up with. A lively neighbourhood with familiar faces and short daily trips makes you feel settled, while silence in the household worries you. You may have moved schools or areas as a child, which left you adaptable but sometimes unsure where home is. Relatives rely on you to keep everyone talking and to pass on the news. Needing constant contact to feel secure can leave you restless. Everyday, local rootedness is what steadies your quick mind.",
      "4": "Home and family are the core of your emotional life, and you need a private base more than almost anything else. The places of your childhood still pull at you, and the thought of losing them brings a real pang. Your attachment to your roots, and to your mother or main carer, runs very deep. Wherever you land, making a space feel like home is the first thing you do. The home you make becomes a haven that everyone you love returns to. Retreating so fully into family that the outside world starts to feel threatening is the risk. A home that nourishes you and sends you back out stronger is what you are building.",
      "5": "A playful, creative household full of children, pets or fun is where you feel most at home. You can turn an ordinary, empty day into something fun, and play comes to you as naturally as breathing. Family time means shared pleasures rather than duty, and a house without laughter drains you quickly. Being a parent, or a loving presence to younger relatives, meets a deep emotional need. Joy and warmth follow you into every home you share. You also need a steady supply of affection, and you sulk when the fun drains out. In your ideal family life, love and play are the same thing.",
      "6": "Daily routine is what makes you feel safe at home: order, rhythm and everyone doing their fair share. You keep track of what the household needs and quietly see to it before anyone else notices. Care for your family means doing the everyday tasks and spotting who is run down. Your mother or carer may have been a worker, a worrier or someone who showed love through service. Your household runs smoothly and everyone's wellbeing is gently looked after. Small domestic details, though, can take over your mood when you are anxious. Home feels best once care includes rest for you, not only work.",
      "7": "Partnership matters more than place to your sense of home, and living with someone you love is central to your emotional security. An empty home makes you restless, and you relax the moment the person you love comes back. You tend to seek a partner who offers the nurturing you had, or lacked, from a parent. Family life works for you when responsibilities and feelings are shared evenly. Companionship is the heart of every home you make. Relying on a partner for all your emotional stability, however, lets their moods set the temperature of the whole house. Partnership that supports you without replacing your own centre is what brings lasting security.",
      "8": "Your family bonds carry an intensity others rarely see, including secrets, inheritances or emotional debts passed down the line. You may be the one who sensed what was hidden, or who was trusted with something as a child you were never meant to repeat. You need a home where deep trust is possible and privacy is respected completely. Childhood may have included a loss, a crisis or a parent whose feelings ran very strong. In family emergencies you are steady, able to sit with grief when others run from it. People who love you can find themselves kept outside, because you guard your emotional core so closely. Bonds deep enough to survive complete honesty are what you are looking for.",
      "9": "Far from your birthplace may be where you feel most rooted, perhaps abroad or within a culture you have made your own. You can feel homesick for places that were never officially home, and you weave other cultures into the way you live. Family life thrives for you on shared beliefs, big conversations and a household open to new places and learning. A parent may have been religious, well read or a restless traveller. The home you create widens everyone's horizons. Ordinary domestic routine can leave you hemmed in and always wanting to be elsewhere. A base that holds both roots and wings is the kind of home that suits you.",
      "10": "Your mother or main carer was a strong public presence in your early life, and their ambitions shaped your own. When you make big choices about your path, you still hear a parent's voice in your head, and you want your family to be proud of how you turned out. Emotional security comes when home life and your standing in the world support each other. Family reputation matters to you more than you admit. Your household can be both a source of pride and a launch pad for achievement. Work, however, easily crowds out home, and outside recognition can start to feel like a condition of feeling safe. Security that exists in private, not only in public, is what you are learning to build.",
      "11": "Friends are your chosen family, and you feel at home within a circle of like-minded people. Your home is where friends naturally gather, and you open your door to anyone who has nowhere else to go. You may have grown up in an unconventional household or felt more understood by friends than by relatives. The home you create is open, inclusive and full of people who share your values. Blood family can feel distant, most of all when their expectations clash with your ideals. Your roots are often found rather than inherited, and a community that feels like kin is what makes you feel safe.",
      "12": "Much of your emotional life stays hidden, even from those you live with, and you need a private sanctuary at home to recharge. You slip away quietly when it all gets too much, and return a little later able to face everyone again. Early family life may have included an absent or unknowable parent, or feelings that nobody spoke about. You nurture others instinctively, often picking up on a relative's pain they have never mentioned. Your home can be a quiet, healing refuge for everyone in it. Your own needs, though, stay hidden until they overwhelm you. Feeling safe means having a place where your inner life is allowed to be seen."
    }
  },
  "home:house4": {
    "sun": "Your identity shines brightest at home, closely bound to your roots and the household you build. Making your home truly your own leaves you feeling more yourself than any work success. One parent, often the father, left a strong mark on who you became, whether through their example or their absence. Your home tends to be where people gather, with you at the warm centre. When family life changes, though, you can feel as if you have lost part of yourself. Later life often brings a stronger sense of identity as you settle into your own base and your own way of living.",
    "moon": "Your emotional roots go deep, and the atmosphere of your family home still shapes your moods today. A familiar taste, smell or sound can carry you straight back to childhood in an instant. You nest instinctively, filling rooms with meaningful objects and making guests feel cared for within minutes. Your mother or primary carer is a defining figure in your story, for better and for worse. Friends ask to stay with you when life falls apart, because your home feels like an embrace. Moves and household upheavals hit you much harder than most people realise. Having a safe place of your own that no one can take away is a lifelong need.",
    "mercury": "Your home is full of talk, ideas and information, and it often doubles as the place where you think and work. Every family story is stored in your memory and retold at gatherings, gaining a new detail each time. Lively talk and shared jokes at home shaped the way you think. A parent may have been a talker, a teacher or someone always busy with news and ideas. When the family needs to clear the air, you are usually the one who finds the words that do it. A tense exchange with a relative, however, can replay in your head for days. The household that suits you best is one where everything can be said.",
    "venus": "You create a beautiful, welcoming home and care a great deal about colour, comfort and atmosphere. You take real care over how your space looks and feels, and people relax the moment they walk in. Family relationships tend to be affectionate, and a parent may have passed on a love of beauty and pleasure. Sharing good food and easy company in your own space is among your deepest pleasures. Love is easy to show in the home you make. Domestic conflict, though, gets avoided to keep things pretty, and the house can absorb more money than it should. A household that is as lovely in its relationships as in its decor is what you want.",
    "mars": "Energy runs hottest for you at home, both in building it and in arguing within it. You throw yourself physically into changing your space, and at home you can go from calm to furious over something small in seconds. Anything that improves or builds your home gets your full drive. Family life in childhood may have been loud, competitive or marked by clashes with a parent. You defend your household fiercely and get done what others only talk about. Tempers flare at home more easily than anywhere else, and old family battles can repeat themselves. Turning that heat into building rather than fighting is where your home life thrives.",
    "jupiter": "Luck with property and generosity with hospitality run in your blood, and a large, open house full of people suits you. There is always room for one more in your home, and somehow there is always enough to go round. Family life in childhood was often warm, expansive or rich in values, travel or faith. A parent may have been big hearted, well travelled or larger than life. Guests feel welcome and children feel free in the home you create. Excess is the catch: overbuying, overstretching on a house, or a household that never quite has enough room. Family life for you is at its happiest when it is full of meaning, laughter and open doors.",
    "saturn": "Security at home was something you felt you had to earn, and family has always carried weight for you. You may have grown up fast, carrying responsibilities at home that were heavy for your age. Childhood could have involved strict rules, a distant or burdened parent, or a sense that feelings were not a priority. You build your own home slowly and carefully, and property often comes later in life than for others. What you create lasts, a solid foundation your family can rely on for decades. Warmth, however, can take time to thaw, and home can feel more like a duty than a refuge. Letting comfort in alongside responsibility changes everything about how home feels.",
    "uranus": "Conventional patterns rarely fit your home life, and you may have moved often or grown up in an unusual household. Changing your surroundings on a whim feels perfectly normal to you, and your living arrangements rarely stay the same for long, because staying put too long feels like a cage. Freedom inside your own four walls is essential. A parent may have been erratic, eccentric or abruptly absent, which taught you to expect the unexpected. People are free to be themselves in the original, open home you create. Stability, though, feels both desirable and suffocating, so domestic life changes in sudden jumps. A base secure enough to hold your independence is what you keep searching for.",
    "neptune": "You long for an ideal home, a sanctuary that feels almost spiritual, and you are often drawn to live near water. You carry a quiet longing for a place that feels like peace, and you dream about it more than you admit. Family life can feel hazy, with a parent who was elusive, idealised or struggling in ways that were never named. You feel the sadness in a room before anyone speaks. Your home, when it works, is a gentle, soulful refuge full of music and quiet. Confusion creeps in too, from blurred family boundaries to living arrangements that turn out differently than they first appeared. A lived-in sanctuary, not only a dreamed one, is what you are reaching for.",
    "pluto": "Powerful, sometimes hidden forces run through your family roots, and your home life has been through at least one major upheaval. A hidden truth, a sudden change or a loss may have reshaped your family overnight, and it still echoes. A parent may have been controlling, intense or at the centre of a family crisis. Anyone intruding on your private space can feel like an invasion, because you need complete control of it. Old family patterns often stop with you. Power struggles at home are the price when control tightens too far. Over time you dig into the family past and rebuild your home on truer foundations.",
    "chiron": "An old wound lives in your sense of home, perhaps a childhood in which you never quite felt you belonged, or a parent who could not give what you needed. You can feel oddly unsettled even where you are perfectly comfortable, and talk of happy families can touch a nerve. That early experience makes you understanding of others who feel rootless. Friends often turn to you when their own families let them down, and your door is open to anyone who needs a place to land. Never feeling fully at home anywhere is the ache that lingers. Building a household on your own terms, and choosing who counts as family, is part of your healing.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in putting down roots and learning to prioritise home, family and your private emotional life. Letting work crowd out private life and missing family moments for the sake of achievement may be a long habit. Public success has come more easily, but it rarely fills the gap at home. Creating a home, looking after family and letting yourself be looked after is where fulfilment grows. Stepping back from the world can feel uncomfortable at first, even lazy. A private life that matters as much as your public one is the direction of your growth.",
    "lilith": "Something in your family history was suppressed or taboo, and you refuse to play the dutiful role at home. You would rather break the peace than keep pretending, and you say out loud what everyone else has agreed to ignore. You may have rebelled against a parent, particularly your mother, or felt that your true feelings were not welcome in the household. Traditional domesticity can feel like a trap. The home you create is honest, free and entirely on your own terms. Anger at family can follow you into every home you make until it is faced. Your household becomes yours once you stop living by the old family rules and let it reflect who you are."
  },
  "health:mars": {
    "sign": {
      "aries": "Energy arrives in fast, intense bursts for you, and you feel best when you can move hard and properly sweat. Anything with speed, force and a clear challenge suits you far better than slow, gentle routines. You run when you could walk, and you push harder the moment someone nearby seems to be doing more. Your get up and go is remarkable, and you bounce back quickly from most knocks. Fatigue gets pushed through until you crash without warning. Stress shows up as heat, impatience and a clenched jaw, and minor bumps happen when you rush. Your body thrives on regular, vigorous release, and just as much on the rest you tend to skip.",
      "taurus": "Your stamina is steady and long lasting, and you do best with regular, unhurried exercise that builds strength over time. Once a routine is set you stick to it for years, but getting started can feel like pushing a boulder uphill. You know how easily good intentions slide into tomorrow when you feel settled exactly where you are. Stress tends to settle in your neck and shoulders and stay there for days. Given time, you become strong, grounded and capable of work that outlasts everyone else. Comfort food and rest pull hard when you feel tired or unsettled. Slow, reliable strength built through habits you enjoy is what serves you best.",
      "gemini": "Quick, nervous energy drives you, and you need variety in movement or you get bored within a week. You take up something new with total enthusiasm, then swap it for something different once the novelty fades. Stress shows up as racing thoughts, restless hands and shallow breathing, and you often catch yourself holding your breath while you concentrate. Nimble and quick, you get a surprising amount done in a day. Scattering yourself across too many tasks leaves you wired rather than pleasantly tired. Movement that quiets your busy mind restores you more than anything else.",
      "cancer": "Mood and energy are closely linked for you, so an emotional upset can flatten you for a whole day. Tension with the people closest to you can leave you too drained to do what you had planned. Exercise that feels protective and comforting suits you, especially in company you trust or in the privacy of home. Stress often lands in the stomach, and you tend to eat for comfort when angry rather than let the anger out. Your strength is tenacious and enduring, especially when you are protecting someone you love. Swallowed frustration drains your stamina. Routines that feel safe enough for you to let go are the ones that last.",
      "leo": "Strong, warm vitality is yours, and you love movement that feels expressive and lets you shine. You try harder when someone is watching, and you would rather move for the sheer joy of it than grind through a plan. Motivation soars when exercise is fun or earns recognition, and sags when it feels like a chore. Your back and posture benefit from regular activity and a proud, upright stance. Your enthusiasm is contagious and brings others along with you. Pride, though, pushes you beyond your limits to prove a point, and admitting you need rest does not come easily. Joyful movement that keeps your heart light is what sustains you.",
      "virgo": "You approach your body like a project, tracking steps, planning meals and refining routines. Nothing goes into your body or your routine without some thought, and there is a plan behind almost everything you do. Precise, skill based activity suits you well, especially anything you can measure and refine. Stress goes straight to the gut, making you restless and fussy about small things. You are disciplined, well informed and able to fine tune your habits with skill. Fretting about your health, however, can drain you more than any workout. Routines that are effective without becoming one more thing to perfect bring out your best energy.",
      "libra": "Balance is the key to your energy, and you often exercise more happily with a partner or a class than alone. Graceful, flowing movement appeals to you far more than brute effort. Conflict drains you physically, and a day spent keeping everyone happy leaves you strangely exhausted. You have an elegant, harmonious relationship with your body and a good sense of proportion. Indecision gets in the way, with a new routine postponed until the perfect moment arrives. A rhythm where effort and ease are held in balance is where you feel strongest.",
      "scorpio": "Deep reserves of stamina let you push through intense training or long stretches of pressure. All or nothing is your default: you commit fiercely to a new regime, then drop it entirely when it loses its hold on you. You know the thrill of a punishing session that leaves you completely spent, and the strange calm that follows. Stress is held inside, building until it releases as a surge of tension or sudden exhaustion. Your ability to regenerate after a setback is extraordinary. Driving yourself to extremes is the risk. Demanding, focused training suits you, and full recovery after every period of intensity keeps that power renewable.",
      "sagittarius": "Open air and wide horizons feed your energy, and you feel most alive moving freely with space all around you. Too long confined to the same four walls leaves you feeling caged and flat. Repetitive exercise routines bore you quickly, however good your intentions. Enthusiasm pushes you further than your body is ready for, and the hips and thighs take the strain. Your energy is buoyant and generous, with a zest for movement that gets other people moving too. Skipped warm ups and overconfidence lead to small, avoidable injuries. Stress lifts fastest when you can get outside, move far and see a long view.",
      "capricorn": "Discipline is your strength when it comes to exercise, and stamina that is built slowly lasts for you. Early starts and hard sessions are not a sacrifice to you, and you keep count without being asked. Long term goals, structured programmes and steady endurance work suit your temperament. You carry stress as stiffness in the knees, back and shoulders, often noticing it only when you finally stop. You tend to grow physically stronger with age, outlasting those who started out fitter. Treating your body like a machine, ignoring tiredness until it forces you to stop, is the cost. Endurance that includes rest as part of the plan is what keeps you going.",
      "aquarius": "You move best when you can do it your own way, and anything new or a little unusual keeps you interested. Sudden passions for new ways of moving come and go, each one pursued with total conviction while it lasts. Your energy comes in erratic surges rather than a steady flow, and it is hard to predict how you will feel on any given morning. Stress shows as nervous tension, restlessness and broken sleep. Others often try something new because you made it look exciting. Swinging between enthusiasm and complete neglect is your usual pattern. Freedom within a loose, flexible structure keeps your energy alive.",
      "pisces": "Fluid and changeable, your physical energy rises and falls with your mood and surroundings. Gentle, rhythmic, flowing movement suits you far more than forceful competition. After time in crowds or tense company, you can feel as if someone has drained your battery. Other people's stress settles in your body as a heaviness in the limbs. You move with grace and intuition, and water and music restore you beautifully. Low motivation can make routines drift away altogether. Tiredness is usually a sign that you need solitude, water or rest rather than more effort, and movement that feels like flow suits you best."
    },
    "house": {
      "1": "Your physical energy is visible and immediate, and you feel restless if you cannot move every day. You move at full speed without thinking, and your body often shows the evidence before your mind notices. You throw yourself into exercise with enthusiasm and heat, but rushing leads to bumps, cuts and minor strains. Your temperature runs warm, and stress shows quickly as a flushed face or clipped voice. Natural vigour gives you a strong physical presence that others notice. Burnout comes from pushing on without pause and trusting willpower over your body's signals. Daily movement, and recognising sooner when to stop, keep you at your strongest.",
      "2": "Energy builds slowly for you and then stays, so you prefer steady, tangible effort over sprints. Physical work that produces something you can see keeps you well. Effort with a tangible result leaves you feeling better than exercise for its own sake ever could. Stress tends to rise around money, and financial worry can sit in your neck and throat for days. Your stamina is solid and dependable, and your body responds well to consistency. You can grind on too long in one gear, keeping a stale routine long after it stops working. Effort that feels worth something, at a pace you can sustain, is what serves you.",
      "3": "Constant small movement is where your energy goes, in busy days full of coming and going. You stay active without really trying, simply because you rarely sit still for long. Variety keeps you well, and your hands like to be occupied. Mental overload drains you as much as physical effort, and too much talk or information leaves you wired long after you should be asleep. Alert and agile, you get a great deal done on nervous energy alone. Letting your mind go quiet is the hardest thing for you. Your body settles when your mind is given a break and your movement becomes rhythmic and simple.",
      "4": "A tense household affects your energy directly, because home is both where you recharge and where stress builds. A small family disagreement can leave you restless and keyed up long after everyone else has moved on. You exercise best in private, on your own ground and at your own pace. Frustration held in around family turns into restlessness or poor sleep. Your reserves of energy tend to grow stronger with age as you build a secure base. Swallowing anger at home rather than releasing it wears you down. A peaceful home routine that lets you recover fully is essential to your stamina.",
      "5": "Plenty of energy is available for play, and exercise works best for you when it is fun, social or competitive. Hours of play feel effortless, while a short, joyless workout feels unbearable. Pleasure gets your full commitment, and you pay later for late nights, rich food and overexertion. You have a youthful, playful vitality that tends to last well into later life. Burning bright and then crashing is the pattern. Stress eases through creative outlets, and your vitality drops quickly when life has no joy in it.",
      "6": "Your body responds best to a structured daily routine with regular, purposeful exercise. There is a set time for your training, and a missed session nags at you for the rest of the day. You work hard and keep going, and physical effort is part of how you manage stress. Efficient and physically capable, you keep yourself strong through habit rather than bursts of enthusiasm. Overwork, however, means pushing through tiredness until your body forces a stop with strain or exhaustion. Small daily frustrations build into tension that needs a physical outlet to clear. Recovery deserves the same seriousness from you as effort.",
      "7": "You exercise more willingly with a partner, trainer or rival to push against. The moment someone pulls ahead of you, you find another gear, and you keep commitments to others more easily than promises to yourself. Relationships have a direct effect on your energy: conflict with a partner drains you, while a supportive one lifts you. Competitive sports and training in pairs suit you well. Healthy challenge brings out your courage and motivation. Taking on other people's battles leaves you tense and depleted without quite realising why. Partnerships that support your wellbeing rather than use it up keep your energy strong.",
      "8": "Crisis tends to bring out your strength, and you can handle extreme effort and pressure for long stretches. You get everyone through the emergency, then collapse with exhaustion a week later. The cost is ignored until you crash. Stress is held deep and released in surges, and hidden tension disturbs your sleep and appetite. Your powers of recovery are remarkable, and you often come back from setbacks stronger. Pushing to extremes, in training or in enduring stress, is the risk. You work in cycles of full exertion and full recovery, and honouring the recovery phase is what keeps you whole.",
      "9": "Adventure feeds your energy, and movement that takes you somewhere new keeps you well. Your body feels strongest when your spirit is stirred, and a sense of freedom lifts your stamina more than any plan. Repetitive routines bore you unless they serve a bigger goal that excites you. Optimism leads you to assume you can do more than you prepared for. Your buoyant, adventurous energy inspires others to get moving. Stay in one place too long and you turn sluggish. Stress lifts when you change your scenery, and movement that feels like exploration is what keeps you going.",
      "10": "Ambition takes most of your energy, and your body often comes second to achievement. Long working hours, pressure from authority and public responsibility drain you fast. You exercise best with a clear goal or measurable target to hit. Drive and discipline make you physically resilient and capable of great feats of endurance. Burning out in pursuit of success is the danger, with stress showing up as a stiff back and a feeling of permanent tension. Your body works best when it is treated as part of your success, not a tool for it.",
      "11": "Group activity keeps you motivated, and you exercise best alongside other people who share the goal. You keep going because others are counting on you, then feel brilliant afterwards. Your energy rises through shared goals and causes you believe in. You push yourself hard for others or for an ideal, then find yourself depleted by the end of the season. Whole groups get fitter and have more fun because of you. Overcommitment brings irregular sleep and an overcrowded calendar. Stress builds when friendships clash, and communities that lift your wellbeing are where your energy flows best.",
      "12": "Much of your energy works behind the scenes, and you often fail to notice how tired you are until it hits all at once. You insist you are fine right up until your body simply gives out. Solitary, quiet forms of movement suit you best. Anger and stress tend to be held in, leaving you vaguely drained without a clear cause. Quiet, intuitive strength is yours, and you recover fully through rest and solitude. Hidden fatigue and suppressed frustration build up if you never retreat. Regular sleep and quiet time recharge you more than intense training ever could."
    }
  },
  "health:house6": {
    "sun": "Your vitality is strongly linked to your daily routine, and you feel best when your days have structure and purpose. A day that starts with a sense of order and purpose sets you up for everything that follows. You notice quickly when your body is out of balance and take pride in looking after yourself. Being useful energises you, and a productive day leaves you glowing. Others copy your habits because they so obviously work. Overwork is your main drain, and a week of long hours shows on your face. Your sense of self can become too bound up with productivity, so learning that rest is not wasted time matters greatly for your health.",
    "moon": "Emotional upset tends to show up in your body as tiredness, an unsettled stomach or disrupted sleep. When you are upset, your appetite either disappears completely or turns into a hungry need for comfort. Regular meals, familiar routines and a calm household rhythm keep you steady. You look after other people's wellbeing instinctively, noticing when they are run down while ignoring the same signs in yourself. You listen well to your body's moods when you slow down enough to hear them. Your own needs tend to come last while you tend to everyone else. Your energy moves in cycles, so flexible, nourishing routines serve you better than rigid ones.",
    "mercury": "Your nervous system is the key to your wellbeing, and an overloaded mind quickly drains your body. When something feels off, your mind keeps searching for an explanation long after you should be resting, sure there is an answer to find. You track habits, read up on nutrition and think a great deal about what is good for you. Worry is your main source of stress, showing as restlessness, fidgeting or broken sleep. Observant and well informed, you spot small changes in your routine before they grow. Anxiety can turn health into yet another thing to fix. Mental breaks, walking and simple, predictable routines bring your energy back into balance.",
    "venus": "You feel well when daily life is pleasant and your routine includes some comfort and beauty. A little beauty and comfort built into a habit makes all the difference to whether it sticks, because you keep what feels good. Gentle exercise, good food and a calm, attractive environment support your energy. Anything harsh or joyless, including overly strict regimes, you tend to avoid. Your healthiest habits are balanced, sociable and enjoyable. Indulgence is the flip side: sweet treats, skipped workouts and choosing comfort when your body needs activity. Routines that feel like pleasure rather than punishment are the ones you keep.",
    "mars": "Your routine runs at a fast pace, and you cram workouts, errands and tasks into every day with no slack. You eat on the move and rest in a hurry, and the idea of a slow start feels almost unbearable. Heat, irritation and small strains tend to be your body's signals to slow down, and you usually ignore the first few. Slow recovery frustrates you, and you want to be back on your feet the day after any setback. Energetic and efficient, you handle a demanding workload with ease. A disrupted schedule, though, makes you irritable out of all proportion. Vigorous, scheduled exercise keeps your restlessness in check, and pauses built into the day keep you well.",
    "jupiter": "Good resilience and a quick bounce back are among your strengths, and an optimistic outlook supports your wellbeing. Your days fill up quickly because you say yes to everything that sounds good, with wholehearted enthusiasm. Just a little more of whatever feels good always seems like a good idea at the time. Too much food, too many tasks, too much of a good thing: excess is the main tendency. Your energy is generous and buoyant, and you recover well from most strain. Overextending can make your routine collapse under its own weight. You thrive on a varied day that includes learning, movement outdoors and something to look forward to.",
    "saturn": "You take your health seriously and become disciplined once you commit to a routine. Once a routine proves itself, you can keep it going for years with remarkable consistency. Stiffness and tension in the back and joints tend to be how your body signals stress. Earlier in life you may have ignored your body or felt it held you back. Your habits strengthen with age, and you can easily feel healthier at fifty than you did at twenty. Rigidity and anxiety appear when things fall out of order. Structure that supports you without becoming a burden is what your body responds to.",
    "uranus": "Rigid routines rarely last for you, and your habits change in sudden bursts. You can start a new regime with total conviction, then abandon it for an entirely different approach only a few days later. New or unconventional approaches to wellbeing suit you, especially the ones others have not caught on to yet. Your nervous system is sensitive, and stress shows as erratic energy, restlessness or broken sleep. Irregular hours and sudden changes unsettle your body more than you expect. A loose framework, with freedom built into the day, brings out your healthiest self.",
    "neptune": "Noise, crowds and other people's moods affect your body more than most. After a busy day around people you can feel exhausted without having done anything physical. Gentle, holistic approaches to wellbeing suit you, anything that calms the senses and lets your body soften. Routines drift easily, and you can lose whole hours before you realise you have forgotten to eat. Your instinct for what your body needs is strong, and restorative practices come naturally to you. Escapism and blurred routines slowly wear your energy down. Stress shows up as fatigue or a foggy vagueness, a sign that you need more rest and clearer boundaries.",
    "pluto": "Health is something you approach with intensity, often overhauling your diet or exercise all at once. When you decide to change, you tend to sweep away old habits all at once and follow the new regime with fierce determination. Your body works in cycles of depletion and regeneration, and your powers of recovery are strong. Stress builds under the surface and can erupt as sudden exhaustion. Remarkable physical change is possible for you when you commit. Habits around food or training can tip into obsession and become about control. Change that grows from understanding your body, rather than forcing it, lasts far longer.",
    "chiron": "Your relationship with your body carries an old sensitivity, perhaps from feeling fragile, different or misunderstood as a child. Old messages about your body, that it was weak, awkward or not quite right, can still echo in how you treat it today. You become knowledgeable about wellbeing through your own experience rather than from books. Stress tends to show up where you feel least confident about your body. Your daily habits can become a place of healing, and you are gifted at supporting other people's routines. Treating your body as a problem to be managed keeps the old hurt alive. Acceptance and patience with your own rhythms are what let you thrive.",
    "northNode": "Growth comes through building healthy, practical routines and paying attention to your body's everyday needs. You may be used to escaping into daydreams or distraction, ignoring hunger and tiredness until they become impossible to miss. Learning the value of regular sleep, meals and exercise brings a steadiness you did not know you needed. Simple habits gradually become a source of calm and confidence. Routine can feel dull or limiting at first, even like a loss of freedom. Small, consistent habits matter more for you than grand gestures, and they ground you firmly in ordinary daily life.",
    "lilith": "Conventional health rules rarely sit well with you, and you rebel against routines imposed by others. Well meant health advice from anyone else can make you do the exact opposite, purely on principle. Your body's signals are strong, and ignoring them tends to bring tension or exhaustion. You may have felt judged about your body or eating habits in the past, and that memory still shapes your choices. Your instinct for what your body needs is fierce and often right. Defiance, however, can work against your own wellbeing. A rhythm that honours your instincts rather than someone else's regime is what keeps you well."
  },
  "mind:house3": {
    "sun": "Your sense of self is built through talking, reading and working things out on the spot. You are the one who has already found the answer while everyone else is still guessing, and you love to share it. Quick exchanges light you up, and a friendly argument or a conversation that runs on and on leaves you buzzing. People come to you because you make information feel warm and usable. Restlessness is the catch: a busy head passes for thought, and you feel you must have an opinion on everything. Writing, teaching and local, everyday communication are where you shine brightest.",
    "moon": "Your thinking is coloured by mood, so a subject that fascinates you one day can feel flat a few days later. You process feelings by talking them through, and you often need to say something out loud to someone close before you know what you think. Putting your feelings into words settles you faster than turning them over in silence. Familiar voices and familiar surroundings give your mind a sense of safety. Anxiety turns this into looping: replaying someone's words over and over and deciding that a short reply means they are upset with you. Handled kindly, this makes you an emotionally intelligent speaker who hears the feeling behind the words.",
    "mercury": "Mercury is at home here, giving you a quick, curious mind that absorbs words, facts and local news with ease. You notice every small error, pick up news before anyone else and seem to know what is happening around you before it is announced. You learn by asking questions and talking things through, and you can switch subjects mid-sentence without losing the thread. Words, quick exchanges and clever problems are your playground. Your blind spot is scattered attention: too many threads started at once and a mind that keeps chattering long after you want to rest. When you finish one line of thought properly, that quick wit turns into lasting skill.",
    "venus": "You speak gently and choose words that put people at ease, and you are often the one trusted to find the right words when tact matters most. Pleasant surroundings help you think, and you learn best when the setting is calm and the company is good. Relationships with siblings, cousins or neighbours tend to be warm and chatty. Your voice persuades because it is kind, and people enjoy listening to you. Hard truths are what you dodge: you soften a message so much that the point disappears, then agree to something just to keep the peace. Graceful writing, languages and poetry suit this mind beautifully.",
    "mars": "You argue fast and think on your feet, and a good debate wakes your mind up like nothing else. You have your reply ready before the other person has finished, and you cannot let a wrong fact slide. Rivalry with a sibling or a classmate sharpened your wits early, and you still enjoy proving a point. You cut through waffle and say out loud what everyone else is thinking. It sours into heated words: things you regret moments after saying them, interruptions and treating every disagreement as a contest. Campaigning, sharp journalism and quick-fire teaching all use this energy well.",
    "jupiter": "Your mind is generous and expansive, and you love sharing what you know with anyone who will listen. You talk easily to almost anyone, and a casual conversation with someone you barely know regularly turns into an opening, a fresh idea or a new friendship. Everyday connections and word of mouth bring you luck more often than grand plans. Siblings or early teachers tended to encourage your curiosity rather than squash it. Enthusiasm tips easily into overstatement: taking on more learning than you can finish and making big pronouncements when the detail is what matters. In full flow, you make learning feel like an adventure for everyone nearby.",
    "saturn": "Thinking and speaking felt like hard work early on, as if every word you said might be judged and found wanting. You still rehearse important conversations in advance, and you check your words several times before you let them go. That pressure built a careful, precise mind that checks facts before it speaks. Your words carry weight precisely because you do not waste them. Self-doubt about your intelligence lingers long after you have proved it wrong, and casual conversation can leave you stiff and guarded. Over time you earn authority as the person whose writing, editing or explanations can be trusted completely.",
    "uranus": "Your mind jumps in sudden flashes, arriving at answers without showing the working. Solutions arrive when you least expect them, and you can blurt out an idea that makes everyone stop and stare. Unusual subjects, new technology and ways of speaking that break the habits of your surroundings excite you. Formal learning often felt like a poor fit, and you learned more from your own experiments than from lessons. Focus comes and goes without warning: brilliant one moment, jittery and scattered the next, with conversations that leave others behind. Original thinking, coding, science writing and fresh formats are where this mind flourishes.",
    "neptune": "You think in images and impressions rather than tidy lines of logic, which gives your speech and writing a poetic, suggestive quality. You sense the mood of a message before you have taken it in properly, and a single beautiful phrase can stay with you for days. What people mean beneath what they say reaches you, even when the facts slip past. Fog is the price: details that slip away, things you were sure you had said and hearing what you hoped rather than what was said. When you trust it, you communicate with rare empathy. Storytelling, imagery and gentle, intuitive conversation are your natural language.",
    "pluto": "Your mind goes deep and refuses surface answers, so you research, question and dig until you reach the root of an idea. A remark made in passing can send you digging for hours, and you notice instantly when someone is not telling the whole story. Words carry power in your mouth: a single sentence from you can persuade, provoke or silence a room. Early experiences taught you that words can hide secrets and carry real power. Left unchecked, the digging becomes obsession, and you can quote word for word what someone said years ago. Investigative writing, research and psychology give this penetrating intelligence its proper outlet.",
    "chiron": "At some point you were made to feel slow, misunderstood or not clever enough, and that early judgement left a mark on how you think about your own mind. Being put on the spot can still make your face go hot, and you over-prepare for conversations others would simply wing. The belief that your writing is never quite good enough keeps many drafts unsent. As this heals, you develop a gift for explaining things to people who struggle. You notice at once when someone is lost, and you slow down for them. In time you become the patient, careful teacher you once needed.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in becoming curious, asking questions and engaging with the people and ideas right in front of you. You catch yourself delivering a long explanation when a simple question would have taught you more, and the conversations that change you are the ordinary, everyday ones you almost overlooked. Writing, practical skills and staying close to the people around you all move you forward. The old pull is to lecture from certainty and dismiss small talk as beneath you. The more you lean into it, the more you become a lively learner who enjoys being corrected. Each everyday exchange, taken seriously, widens your mind more than any grand theory.",
    "lilith": "Your voice carries a raw, unfiltered edge that others have tried to quieten. You remember being told to be quiet, or learning early that certain subjects were never to be discussed. Now you are the one who says the awkward thing everyone else was thinking, even when it makes the people around you uncomfortable. Your fearless honesty frees other people to be truthful too. Trouble comes when you swing between biting your tongue for weeks and an outburst that ends the conversation entirely. Your words are most powerful on uncomfortable subjects that polite company avoids."
  },
  "mind:house9": {
    "sun": "You come fully alive as a student of big subjects, and your identity is bound up with what you know and understand. You remember whole years of your life by what you were learning at the time, and knowledge still gives you a genuine thrill. Lecturing, teaching or publishing your views feels natural rather than daunting. You have a talent for helping others see the larger picture. Intellectual pride creeps in when you grow impatient with people who have not done the thinking, or treat your worldview as the final word. Academia, publishing and expert roles give your mind the stage it wants.",
    "moon": "Learning feeds you emotionally, and you feel most secure when absorbed in a subject that stirs your heart. The people who taught you well stay close to your heart, and learning itself can feel like coming home. Ideas reach you through stories and personal connection rather than dry analysis, so you remember the story long after the formula. You teach with warmth and intuition, making complex ideas feel human. Concentration rises and falls with your mood: long spells of devoted study, then stretches when you cannot bring yourself to begin. History, languages and the humanities nourish you in a personal way.",
    "mercury": "Your mind reaches for the large picture, turning facts into theories and details into principles. One idea leads you to the next, and you follow the trail until you have opened up whole new subjects along the way. Foreign languages, academic writing and complex arguments come to you with relative ease. Given an audience, you explain difficult ideas with crisp clarity. Your blind spot is abstraction: you miss the plain detail and talk over people's heads without noticing. Lecturing, translation, serious non-fiction and publishing all suit this broad, busy mind.",
    "venus": "You love learning for its own beauty, and anything elegant, artistic or expressive tugs at your curiosity. You can fall for a subject simply because it sounds or looks beautiful to you. Study is far more enjoyable alongside someone you admire, and you often form close bonds with teachers. As a teacher you are gracious, making difficult ideas feel welcoming. You are quick to abandon a subject the moment it stops being pleasant and demands dull memorisation. The arts and cultural study give this appreciative mind its richest ground.",
    "mars": "You tackle big questions with energy, arguing your views hard and defending what you have learned. You challenge authority in ideas without hesitation, and when a subject grips you, you throw everything you have into it. Debating, intensive courses and deadline-driven research suit you better than slow, quiet reading. Lazy assumptions do not survive long around you, and students remember your classes for years. Combative certainty is the danger: turning a discussion into a fight and dismissing an idea because you dislike the person who said it. Law, advocacy and campaigning scholarship put this fire to good use.",
    "jupiter": "Jupiter is at home here, making you a natural scholar and teacher with a hunger for knowledge that rarely runs out. Your appetite for ideas outruns your time, and you gather far more to learn than you could ever finish. Universities, libraries, foreign languages and publishing tend to bring you luck, and mentors turn up at the right time. People seek you out because you can explain the meaning behind the facts. The risk is sprawl: collecting qualifications and half-finished courses without settling into one area properly. Your enthusiasm makes learning contagious for everyone you teach.",
    "saturn": "Higher education was often delayed, expensive or hard won, and you treat study with gravity as a result. Nothing about learning was simply handed to you, and you earned every piece of knowledge through effort and persistence. You respect rigour, proper sources and proven expertise, and you build knowledge slowly and thoroughly. Rigidity sets in when you dismiss unfamiliar ideas or feel you are never qualified enough to speak, even when your knowledge says otherwise. Eventually you become an authority yourself, writing or teaching with depth. Time is on your side: expertise here matures beautifully with age.",
    "uranus": "Your intellect rebels against standard curricula, and you learn best by following sudden obsessions wherever they lead. You can throw yourself into teaching yourself something new, then drop it soon after for a completely different field. Science, technology, astrology or radical philosophy attract you, and unconventional teachers suit you better than traditional institutions. You make surprising connections between disciplines that specialists, buried in their own field, tend to miss. Finishing is another matter: the brilliant idea arrives, but the long work of completing it often stalls. Innovative research and future-facing ideas are this mind's natural territory.",
    "neptune": "You are drawn to studies that touch the imagination: poetry, mysticism, music, psychology or comparative religion. You understand a subject before you could explain how, and a single idea can move you so deeply that everything else falls away for a while. Teaching comes through image and story rather than structure. Vision and compassion are what you bring to any classroom. Vagueness and gullibility are the weak spots: following a charismatic teacher uncritically, or drifting away once study demands structure and deadlines. Creative writing and spiritual scholarship give this dreaming mind its home.",
    "pluto": "You study to transform yourself, and a single book, teacher or course can change the direction of your life completely. You know the feeling of meeting an idea and realising you could never see the world the same way again. Psychology, law, forensic research or hidden history attract you, and you read everything on a topic before moving on. In time you become a formidable expert whose insight changes how others think. The risk is fanaticism, clinging to one intellectual system and fighting anyone who questions it. Research and publishing that challenge accepted thinking suit you perfectly.",
    "chiron": "You carry a wound around education: missed chances, being shut out of learning or told your ideas were foolish or too ambitious. You can still feel like an impostor among the learned, even when you know the subject better than anyone present. You either collect qualifications out of insecurity or steer clear of formal study altogether. Healing comes through learning on your own terms, at your own pace. You recognise the quiet person who thinks they do not belong, and you make room for them. That understanding makes you a remarkable mentor in adult education and open learning.",
    "northNode": "Your path forward involves stretching your mind beyond everyday facts into larger questions. You notice that you can quote twenty articles on a topic yet hesitate when asked what you believe. The pull now is to commit to a subject, pursue higher study, learn a foreign language properly or share what you know as a teacher or writer. The comfortable habit is endless information gathering and chatter without conclusion. Gradually you become someone with a considered perspective that others value. Forming a view and standing behind it, even without certainty, is exactly where your growth lies.",
    "lilith": "Your mind is drawn to forbidden or fringe knowledge, subjects that institutions ignore, dismiss or ridicule. You have always been drawn to the questions others would not dare ask, and you learned early that some curiosity is met with scorn. You learned to study alone, following threads that official learning left out. You bring suppressed ideas into the light and challenge intellectual gatekeeping. Contempt for every authority in learning can cut you off from teachers who could properly help. Independent scholarship and topics others are afraid to touch are where your mind burns brightest."
  },
  "growth:house9": {
    "sun": "You find yourself through the search for what life means. The version of you that is exploring something unfamiliar, hungry to understand how other people live, feels more like the real you than the one caught up in routine. A personal philosophy drives your choices, and you want your life to stand for something larger than yourself. When this works, you become a living example that a bigger life is possible. It sours into preaching when a new insight turns into telling everyone how they ought to live now. Adventure, faith and purpose are where your spirit fully shines.",
    "moon": "Faith and belief are emotional needs for you rather than intellectual positions. You can feel oddly at home in places and traditions that are not your own, and be moved to tears by rituals you do not fully understand. Beliefs inherited from family stay with you for years, then slowly reshape themselves into something your own. When life feels lost or heavy, a change of scene or a moment of quiet faith restores you faster than any sensible routine. Part of you always longs to be somewhere else, which makes settling hard. Belonging to a wider world, and to a faith that comforts you, gives your heart its deepest security.",
    "mercury": "Your search for meaning happens through conversation. A single conversation with someone who sees the world differently can reshape your outlook for years. You compare beliefs across cultures, soak up other ways of speaking and thinking, and enjoy turning over the big questions out loud. Travel keeps your mind flexible and your worldview honest. Left unchecked, you debate every philosophy without ever letting one change how you live. Meaning becomes solid for you when your ideas about life are tested on the road, among people who see it differently.",
    "venus": "You find meaning through beauty, love and connection across borders. Beauty is what draws you towards the wider world, and you fall easily and deeply for places, cultures and people that feel far removed from your own. Your faith tends to be gentle, centred on kindness, harmony and the sense that life is fundamentally good. Travel is a pleasure you protect, even on a tight budget. You tend to choose comfortable beliefs over ones that challenge you, and to avoid places or ideas that feel harsh. Love and beauty remain your truest path to the sacred.",
    "mars": "Adventure fuels you, and you chase your beliefs with physical energy. You throw yourself into challenges that test your body and your nerve, and you stand up physically for what you believe. Holding a belief quietly never satisfies you: you act on it, argue for it and put your body where your convictions are. Crusading for something you believe in gives your life direction and fire. Zealotry is the danger: fierce arguments over religion or politics, and a restlessness that turns every journey into a conquest. Your spirit grows through bold experience rather than safe theory.",
    "jupiter": "Jupiter is at home here, bringing a deep faith in life, luck on the road and natural optimism about the future. Your detours tend to turn into gifts, and the chance meeting that changes everything often comes when you have strayed from the plan. Opportunities arrive through foreign contacts, generous mentors and a willingness to say yes. Your worldview keeps expanding with experience, and you inspire others to widen theirs. The risk is excess: overconfidence, one leap too many and promising more than you deliver. Wherever your horizons grow, good fortune tends to follow.",
    "saturn": "Your beliefs are hard won and tested, often through doubt, loss or strict rules you had to work your way out of. You were the child who asked awkward questions about what the adults believed, and later you sat alone with convictions that no longer fitted. Travel was delayed, came with responsibilities or only happened once you had earned it. Over time you build a solid, practical philosophy that holds firm when life gets hard. Cynicism tempts you, a refusal to trust anything larger than yourself. Meaning you have built slowly becomes an unshakeable foundation that others lean on.",
    "uranus": "Your beliefs shift abruptly, and you can walk away from a faith or worldview overnight when something new rings true. You remember the exact moment an old certainty collapsed, often in a flash of insight nothing had prepared you for. Sudden changes of plan and chance encounters with other worlds jolt your life in unexpected directions. Unconventional spirituality and freedom of thought matter more to you than tradition. Meaning can feel like a moving target, the beliefs of last year already out of date, and commitment to any belief system makes you itch. You show others that faith can be free, personal and alive.",
    "neptune": "You long for transcendence and seek meaning through spirituality, art and a sense of the sacred. You know the moments when beauty or stillness makes time seem to stop. Anything with a sense of pilgrimage moves you profoundly, and you idealise gurus, faiths and faraway lands. Disillusionment hits hard when a teacher or tradition turns out to be human, and you carry a vulnerability to charismatic leaders who promise too much. Compassion and imagination are your faith. Your spirit grows whenever you let yourself be moved by something larger than you.",
    "pluto": "Your beliefs go through death and rebirth, often after a crisis that shattered the worldview you grew up with. There is a before and after in your life: an experience after which you could never believe the same things again. Intense spiritual paths, deep philosophies and travel to places marked by history or hardship draw you. When this works, you emerge with a faith that is your own and nearly impossible to shake. The risk is fanaticism, imposing your newfound convictions with the same force that changed you. Transformation of meaning is your lifelong journey.",
    "chiron": "Faith or meaning has been a source of pain for you: a sense of not belonging to what others believed, or of never quite feeling at home in the world. You know the loneliness of standing among people who seem certain while you feel only doubt, and of never quite fitting wherever you land. For a time you feel spiritually homeless. Healing comes through building your own philosophy from lived experience rather than borrowed doctrine. In time you become the one who sits with people whose beliefs have broken down, helping them find meaning again without forcing answers on them. The faith you end up with is quieter than the one you lost, and far more your own.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in widening your world, taking risks, travelling and trusting a larger purpose. You notice how often you gather information for weeks without acting, or collect opinions without deciding what you believe. The pull is away from endless detail and chatter towards the big questions of meaning and faith. Leaving familiar surroundings, even briefly, is part of the path. The old habit is staying small and safe. Each time you choose the unknown road, commit to a belief or follow a sense of calling, your life opens in ways the careful planner in you never expected.",
    "lilith": "You rebel against orthodoxy and inherited faith, and you tend to reject the moral codes you were handed, sometimes loudly. You remember the relief of breaking away from what you were taught to believe, and the friction it caused with those who held on to it. Taboo beliefs, alternative spirituality and journeys others disapprove of draw you strongly. This gives you a fierce, authentic freedom of spirit. The trap is defining yourself only by what you reject, leaving no positive faith to live by. Your deepest meaning is found in the wild places others fear to go."
  },
  "spirit:house12": {
    "sun": "Your deepest sense of self develops away from the spotlight, in solitude, quiet work and inner reflection. Even in good company you need a few minutes entirely alone, and you come back restored. Your best work often happens behind the scenes, and you feel oddly uncomfortable being thanked in public. Spiritual practice, service or creative retreat helps you feel whole. Hiding comes too easily: underestimating yourself, avoiding recognition and feeling invisible even to those closest to you. Vitality comes when you trust that your quiet inner life is a source of strength, not a hiding place.",
    "moon": "Your emotions run deep and often stay hidden, even from yourself. You absorb the moods of everyone you meet, and later a sadness settles on you that you cannot quite explain. Time alone is a firm need, and dreams are vivid, emotionally revealing and sometimes uncannily accurate. Caring for others in private, quiet ways comes naturally. Secret loneliness is the cost: carrying feelings you never voice, and retreating precisely when you most need comfort. Your inner life is a deep well, and tending it gently brings a quiet, lasting peace.",
    "mercury": "Your thinking is intuitive, and much of it happens below the surface. Answers arrive when you are not looking for them, and you have woken up knowing the solution to something that baffled you the night before. Much of your truest thinking stays private, a store of half-formed insights you rarely share with anyone. Words drawn from the unconscious come easily in poetry or reflective writing. Secrecy and self-doubt hold you back, leaving you hesitating to speak, or carrying fears you cannot put into words. Quiet reflection turns your hidden thoughts into wisdom.",
    "venus": "Your love and compassion have a spiritual quality, and you give without needing credit. You notice who has been forgotten, and your kindness often arrives without a name attached. Beauty found in solitude restores you, and quiet moments alone with something lovely refill you completely. Secret affections and hidden longings play a part in your inner life. Self-sacrifice creeps in: loving people who cannot love you back and keeping your needs invisible, then wondering why nobody notices you are tired. Gentle devotion is your spiritual gift and your truest source of peace.",
    "mars": "Your drive often works behind the scenes, in private effort or causes you pursue without announcing them. Anger tends to be swallowed, then surfaces in dreams, sudden tiredness or a sharp remark that surprises even you. You carry tension in your body without noticing, or feel exhausted after a day of biting your tongue. Moving your body alone, at your own pace and away from any audience, helps you release what builds up. Left unexpressed, that energy turns inwards as self-sabotage rather than open action. When hidden courage is channelled into service or spiritual discipline, it becomes quietly formidable.",
    "jupiter": "You have a hidden protector, a sense that something larger is looking out for you in hard times. You can name moments when help arrived out of nowhere, so perfectly timed that it felt almost arranged. Faith, meditation and charity bring you peace, and you are generous in private, helping without being seen. Stillness and time alone tend to lift your spirits more than any outing could. Escapism is the risk, using spirituality, sleep or indulgence to avoid problems in the world you live in. Your inner optimism is a grace and a steady source of healing.",
    "saturn": "Hidden fears and a sense of guilt or inner restriction shape your inner life, often rooted in early experiences you do not fully remember. You lie awake running through everything that could go wrong, or feel oddly guilty when you rest. Solitude can feel heavy rather than peaceful at first. Over time, discipline in spiritual practice, therapy or quiet routine turns this into deep inner strength. The risk is isolation disguised as self-sufficiency. As you mature, you become a steady, grounded presence for others in their darkest moments, precisely because you have faced your own.",
    "uranus": "Your unconscious produces sudden insights, strange dreams and flashes of intuition that seem to arrive from nowhere. You have had a hunch about someone that turned out to be right, or a dream so vivid it changed a decision. Unusual spiritual practices and breaking free from inherited beliefs about the unseen appeal to you. Much of your independence stays hidden from others. Nervous tension builds silently, too, disrupting your sleep and inner calm, until your thoughts race just when you most need rest. When you give your restless inner life room to breathe, it becomes a source of astonishing insight.",
    "neptune": "Neptune is at home here, giving you deep sensitivity to the unseen, vivid dreams and a strong spiritual imagination. You walk into a room and feel the grief or tension in it before anyone speaks, and crowds leave you drained for a day afterwards. Quiet, beauty and stillness restore you in ways nothing else does. Solitude and creative practice are essential rather than optional. When reality feels too harsh, you drift into fantasy or numbing escapes, and whole stretches of time can vanish. Your compassion and receptivity make you a quiet healer for anyone who is suffering.",
    "pluto": "Powerful forces work in your unconscious, and you face hidden fears head on, through crisis or deep inner work. You have dreams that feel like messages, and you sense buried family secrets long before anyone confirms them. Psychology, therapy and occult subjects fascinate you. You are the one who uncovers old patterns and refuses to pass them on. Secret control and a fear of being exposed can keep old wounds hidden for years, even from the people you love most. Inner transformation is your lifelong spiritual work, and it gives you the power to help others face their own depths.",
    "chiron": "Your wound lies in hidden places: grief you never expressed, a feeling of not belonging or a sense of spiritual abandonment. You know the strange loneliness of feeling sad for no clear reason, even when life is going well. Solitude can feel both healing and haunting, and trust in anything larger comes slowly. As you heal and turn inwards to meet what you once avoided, you gain a remarkable ability to sit with others in their suffering without flinching. Quiet service, far from any spotlight, is where that gift tends to find its work. Your own hidden pain becomes the source of deep compassion.",
    "northNode": "Your growth lies in surrender, solitude and trust in the unseen. You catch yourself finding one more thing to sort or fix when what you need most is to sit still. The pull is away from over-analysis, criticism and constant busyness towards rest, meditation and compassion. Retreat is part of your path rather than a luxury. The old habit is trying to fix and control everything, and exhausting yourself in the process. When you let go, trust your intuition and allow things to unfold, a deep, quiet peace opens that no amount of effort could create.",
    "lilith": "Your raw, instinctive side lives in the unconscious, surfacing through dreams, secret desires and hidden anger. You have woken from a dream of rage or longing that felt more honest than anything you said that day. Buried shame or an intense private life that others know little about is part of your story. Spiritual practice that honours your darker feelings, rather than asking you to transcend them, sets you free, and journaling what you would never say aloud releases a great deal. Self-exile is the danger, retreating so far into isolation that you disappear. Facing your hidden self brings extraordinary power and inner freedom."
  },
  "spirit:neptune": {
    "house": {
      "1": "You carry an otherworldly air, and people project their hopes and fantasies onto you before you have said a word. Your sense of self is fluid, shifting to match whoever you are with and the atmosphere of the room. You feel connected to something larger through your body and presence, most of all when you move freely or stand still and simply feel. Strangers often tell you their troubles within minutes of meeting you. It is easy to lose yourself entirely in other people's expectations and forget where you end. Your open, luminous presence makes others feel the sacred is close.",
      "2": "You idealise what you value and feel connected to something larger through beauty, music and the textures of the physical world. Beauty you can take in through your senses can feel almost like prayer to you. Money and possessions slip through your fingers, because material things never feel entirely solid. Giving freely feels spiritual, and you have handed over money you could not spare. Confusion about your own worth and blurred boundaries with resources follow you, and you rarely know what you have in the bank. Simple, sensual pleasures become your doorway to the divine.",
      "3": "Your imagination flows through words, and you dream in stories, songs and poetic images. Everyday conversations carry a sense of the sacred for you, and you pick up the message beneath the message. Lines and images come to you out of nowhere, and a chance remark can feel as if it was meant just for you. Putting your inner life into words becomes a spiritual practice for you. Misunderstandings creep in: missing plain facts, idealising a sibling or neighbour and forgetting what was agreed. Your language makes ordinary life feel enchanted, and people hold on to the words you give them.",
      "4": "Your deepest dreams are about home and family, and you idealise belonging. A place that feels truly peaceful can seem sacred to you, a refuge you carry inside. You sense ancestors close by, and reminders of your family's past can move you to tears. A hazy or idealised picture of childhood, or a parent who was absent, lost or needing rescue, can leave you searching for a home that feels safe. You sometimes feel the whole family's mood as your own. In the end you create a home that feels like a sanctuary for everyone who enters.",
      "5": "Romance, creativity and play are where you dissolve into something larger. Creating something or falling in love feels spiritual to you, and you lose all sense of time when absorbed in making something. You have fallen for someone's potential rather than who they were, and you see magic in the people you cherish and the things you create. Disappointment follows when the dream fades, and escapist pleasure or a fleeting crush can replace lasting joy. Fantasy and reality blur easily in matters of the heart. Your imagination brings wonder, tenderness and inspiration into everything you create.",
      "6": "You feel connected to something larger through service and daily ritual: caring for others, helping quietly and giving ordinary tasks your full attention. Your body is highly sensitive to atmosphere, food and other people's stress, and you feel a tense atmosphere in your stomach. Routine becomes sacred when it has meaning, and small repeated acts can steady you like a quiet prayer. Blurred boundaries at work lead to burnout from taking on everyone's problems, and to a chaotic daily life when structure feels impossible, with small tasks piling up while you daydream. When this works, your ordinary days become a quiet devotional practice.",
      "7": "You dream of a soulmate and idealise partners, seeing the very best in them. You have stayed with someone because of who you believed they could become, or felt you had known a new person in another life. Relationships are where you dissolve boundaries and feel spiritually connected, and your compassion for others runs deep. It turns painful through rescuing, being deceived or sacrificing yourself in partnerships that do not return your devotion. When you choose well, love becomes soulful, a meeting of two spirits rather than a contract.",
      "8": "You dissolve boundaries through intimacy, and deep emotional or physical connection feels mystical to you. Death, the afterlife and hidden realms fascinate you, and you have sensed a presence after a loss or dreamt of someone just before hearing news of them. Psychic sensitivity is strong, and you pick up other people's secrets without being told. Merging too completely means losing yourself in another person, along with confusion or deception over shared money, debts or inheritances. This makes you a compassionate guide through grief, crisis and transformation, unafraid of the mystery, and people turn to you when someone has died.",
      "9": "You dream of meaning and seek transcendence through faith, travel and philosophy. Faraway places and sacred traditions call to you, and certain teachings bring a shiver of recognition, as if you had always known them. You feel connected to something larger whenever you venture beyond the familiar, in body or in mind. Gullibility is the weak spot: following a false teacher or an idealised belief system and feeling betrayed when it falls short. Your faith is poetic rather than literal. You inspire others with a vision of life that is uplifting.",
      "10": "Your ideals shape your ambitions, and you want work with meaning, often in the arts, healing, charity or spiritual fields. People project glamour or mystery onto your public image, and you are never quite sure how others see you. You have lain awake wondering whether your career matters at all, or felt a sense of calling you could not put into words. Confusion about direction brings drifting between roles and a reputation that does not match who you are. Your life's work can become an act of service that touches people profoundly, even if the job title never quite explains it.",
      "11": "You dream of a better world and feel connected to something larger through groups, friendships and shared ideals. Communities built around a shared ideal draw you, and moments of real unity with others can feel transcendent. You idealise friends and believe the best of every cause you join. Disillusionment arrives when a group falls short, or when you are used by people who share your ideals less sincerely. You sometimes lose yourself in a crowd's hopes, giving time and money to causes long after they stopped nourishing you. You help a community believe in something beautiful and work towards it together.",
      "12": "Neptune is at home here, and your inner life is rich with dreams, intuition and spiritual sensitivity. You wake from dreams that feel like visits, and you need long stretches of quiet to process what you absorb from others. Solitude, stillness and anything that softens the edges of ordinary life connect you to something vast. Your compassion runs deep, above all for people who are hidden or suffering, and strangers somehow sense they can confide in you. Escapism tugs at you, drifting into fantasy, sleep or withdrawal when life feels too harsh. Over time you become a quiet channel for healing and grace, often working unseen."
    }
  },
  "spirit:chiron": {
    "house": {
      "1": "Your wound centres on identity and the body: feeling out of place, awkward or not allowed to simply exist as yourself. You have caught sight of yourself and felt a sharp wave of not being enough. You either hide or overcompensate with a polished image. Spiritually, the healing comes through learning to feel at home in your own skin and trusting that your presence alone has worth. Endless self-scrutiny is the trap. Once that acceptance takes root, your very presence reassures others, and you help people accept themselves wholly as they are.",
      "2": "Your wound concerns worth and security: a deep sense that you are not valuable enough, often linked to money worries or scarcity early in life. You have checked your bank balance with dread even in good times, or clung to possessions as proof you are safe. Spiritually, you are learning to separate your worth from what you own or earn. You swing between hoarding and giving everything away just to feel needed. Over the years you discover a quiet inner wealth that nothing can take away, not a bad month, not a lost job. You help others rediscover their worth and find peace with enough.",
      "3": "Your wound concerns being heard: feeling stupid, misunderstood or silenced, often in childhood or at school. You have felt your throat tighten when asked to speak in a group, or rehearsed a sentence so long the moment passed. Slowly you learn that your voice carries something valuable, even when it trembles. Over-explaining, apologising before you speak or falling silent entirely in a meeting are the old reflexes. Bit by bit, words become a medicine you offer others, gentle and exact. You help people find their voice, through teaching, writing or simply listening in a way that makes them feel understood.",
      "4": "Your wound lies in the home and family: a childhood that felt unsafe, a missing parent or a sense of never quite belonging. You have stood among your own family and felt like a visitor in your own history. Spiritually, healing comes through creating an inner home and tending the family story with compassion. Left unhealed, you keep searching for a place that feels safe, moving house or pulling away from relatives before they can let you down. Eventually you build a sanctuary, a home or a feeling, that others can enter. Your gift is offering belonging to people who have never had it.",
      "5": "Your wound concerns joy, creativity and being seen: perhaps your play was criticised, your talent ignored or your childhood cut short. You have held back from showing what you make or letting your joy be seen, for fear of being laughed at. Healing means reclaiming delight as something sacred rather than frivolous. You swing between performing for approval and refusing to create at all, calling it being sensible. As you heal, your creativity becomes moving because it carries raw feeling, and making things turns into a form of prayer. You encourage others, especially children, to play and create without fear.",
      "6": "Your wound lives in daily life, work and the body: feeling never useful enough, or struggling with routines and health worries. You have pushed through exhaustion because stopping felt like failure, or felt anxious about every twinge. Slowly you learn that service and self-care are equally sacred. Perfectionism shows up as working on when you should be resting and overworking to prove your worth. The wound becomes a gift for caring for others with patience and humility, noticing whoever is quietly struggling. Your daily work becomes a healing practice, and you help people find kinder rhythms in their own lives.",
      "7": "Your wound lies in partnership: rejection, betrayal or feeling you must earn love by fixing others. You have found yourself cast as therapist in a relationship, or chosen partners who needed rescuing. Spiritually, the lesson is meeting another person as an equal soul rather than a project or a threat. The pattern is either avoiding closeness altogether or losing yourself so completely in a partner that your own needs vanish. With time you become a wise, compassionate companion. You help others heal their relationships, through counselling, mediation or by showing how respect and tenderness can coexist.",
      "8": "Your wound runs through intimacy, loss and power: betrayal, grief or a crisis that left you feeling exposed. You know the fear of letting someone close, or the way a single loss reshaped your whole life. Healing asks you to face death, change and vulnerability instead of armouring against them. Control and suspicion creep in, testing people to see whether they will leave. Having survived your own losses, you become steadily unafraid of other people's darkest moments. You guide others through grief, trauma and transformation, whether as a counsellor, a friend or someone who will not look away.",
      "9": "Your wound concerns meaning and faith: a harsh religious upbringing, a crisis of belief or being made to feel foolish for your ideas. You have felt like an outsider among people who seemed sure of what they believed, or felt lost without any philosophy to hold on to. Your faith has to be built from your own experience rather than borrowed doctrine. Some days you drift into cynicism, mocking every faith, or cling to rigid beliefs because doubt feels unbearable. What you piece together from your own doubts becomes wisdom. Your gift is helping others through spiritual doubt, offering meaning without dogma.",
      "10": "Your wound concerns calling and recognition: feeling you have failed, disappointed a parent or never quite found your place in the world. You have looked at other people's careers and felt a sharp ache of being behind. Spiritually, the lesson is that your worth is not measured by status or title. You either chase success to silence doubt, collecting titles that never quite satisfy, or hide from ambition entirely. Once the old ache softens, your work becomes a vocation of service rather than a scoreboard, and success starts to feel like something you give. Others then find in you a guide through their own struggles with direction and purpose.",
      "11": "Your wound lies in friendship and belonging: feeling left out of groups or different from the crowd. You know the feeling of standing at the edge of a group, or discovering that others gathered without you. Healing comes through kinship with other outsiders and trust in your unusual vision. Old habits include keeping groups at arm's length, leaving before you can be excluded, or trying too hard to fit in. As you heal, you build communities, circles and gatherings where everyone feels welcome, including the quiet ones. Your gift is making outsiders feel they belong somewhere at last.",
      "12": "The healing you offer works best in the quiet places other people avoid. You are the one who stays when others leave, who can face what someone cannot face alone, and who knows when to say nothing at all. That steadiness was learned the hard way, through years of carrying something heavy that you could not name or explain to anyone. Therapy, dream work, prayer or art slowly bring it into the light, and each piece you understand becomes something you can hold for another person. The danger is disappearing into service, so tired from absorbing everyone else's pain that your own goes untended again. In your hands, private suffering turns into a gentleness that people remember for years."
    }
  },
};
// the sign on each house, read through the page
window.AstroDeep.areaCusps = {
  "love:house5": {
    "aries": "Falling in love happens to you at speed. One glance across a crowded room, one sharp bit of banter, and you are already planning the second date before the first has ended. You flirt like a dare, teasing and challenging, and the chase itself is half the pleasure. Dates work best when there is something to do, a shared challenge where you can both be a little reckless and laugh at yourselves. Romance with you feels brave and alive, and people remember how openly you showed your interest. Boredom is the enemy, and once the pursuit is over the thrill can drain away faster than you expected. The love that lasts is the one that keeps surprising you.",
    "taurus": "Romance for you is something to be tasted, slowly. You fall in love through the senses: the warmth of a hand on your back, a voice you could listen to all evening, a meal that stretches long into the night. Flirting is unhurried and physical, more lingering eye contact than clever lines, and you would rather share something comforting than go somewhere loud. You are the one who remembers every detail of the first date and treasures it for years. Pleasure is sacred to you and you refuse to rush it, which makes you a wonderfully generous companion in good times. The catch is that you can stay in a comfortable flirtation long after it has stopped going anywhere, because letting go feels like a loss.",
    "gemini": "Words are your first language of love. You flirt with words before anything else, and a quick, funny exchange can light you up for days. Dating feels like a conversation you never want to end, with hours slipping by as you talk about everything. You fall for minds first, and someone who can keep up with your jokes and your tangents has you hooked. Variety keeps romance alive, so you are drawn to new places, new ideas and occasionally more than one interesting person at once. The trouble comes when feelings get heavy and you reach for a witty line instead of saying what you mean. Your heart opens fully to someone who keeps you curious for years, not weeks.",
    "cancer": "You fall in love quietly and then completely. Early on you hold back, watching whether someone is kind to people who can do nothing for them, and only when you feel safe do you let the romance show. Your idea of a perfect date is often close to home, warm and unhurried, the kind of evening that feels like a nest built for two. Flirting comes through care, remembering the small things about someone and making sure they are safe. Once smitten, you are tender, loyal and devoted in ways that leave partners feeling cherished. Rejection lands hard, though, and you can retreat into your shell for weeks after a small slight. What you want from pleasure is belonging, not a thrill.",
    "leo": "Romance is theatre to you, and you want a leading role. You love the big gesture: the grand surprise, the effort that turns heads, the declaration made openly for all to hear. Flirting is warm and playful, and you glow when someone looks at you as if you are the most delightful person in the room. Dating should feel like a celebration, full of warmth, laughter and a real sense of occasion. When you fall in love you do it with your whole heart, generous with praise, gifts and attention. The hard part is that you need admiration returned, and a lover who forgets to notice you can leave you wounded and a little dramatic. Joy, for you, is meant to be shared out loud.",
    "virgo": "You take romance seriously, perhaps more carefully than anyone realises. Before you fall, you notice everything: how someone treats the people who serve them, whether they reply when they said they would, the small inconsistencies in their stories. Flirting shows up as helpfulness, quietly solving a small problem for someone you like, and your affection lives in the details. The dates you enjoy are thoughtful rather than flashy, well planned and full of small considerate touches. Once you trust someone, you are devoted and privately sensual, far warmer than your cool first impression suggests. Self-criticism can spoil the fun, with you replaying a date for flaws long after the other person has gone home happy. Some of your happiest romantic memories are the evenings where the plan fell apart and you laughed anyway.",
    "libra": "Courtship is something you do beautifully. You know how to make a date feel special, creating an atmosphere where everything feels lovely, and you flirt with a charm and lightness that puts people at ease. Being in love suits you, and you are rarely happier than when you are part of a lovely pair. Romance for you is about harmony: shared taste, easy conversation, a partner who looks good beside you and treats you as an equal. You make people feel chosen and admired. The difficulty is decisiveness, and you can keep two admirers in play because disappointing either one feels unbearable. Keeping the peace can also mean swallowing what you want, and the love that fulfils you has both beauty and honest friction.",
    "scorpio": "Casual dating rarely interests you. When you are drawn to someone the pull is magnetic and all consuming, and you can feel it from across a room before a single word has been exchanged. Flirting is intense and a little mysterious: long looks, private jokes, the sense that you see straight through someone's performance. Pleasure has to go deep to count, and a pleasant evening with no charge in it leaves you cold. Falling in love can feel like a small death and rebirth, and you remember every lover as a turning point. Jealousy and testing are the traps, watching too closely or withdrawing to see whether someone will follow. Romance transforms you when you trust enough to be seen without your armour.",
    "sagittarius": "You need romance with open horizons. You fall hardest for someone who makes you laugh, broadens your mind or arrives with a plan for something new. Flirting is frank, funny and a little outrageous, and you would rather say what you are thinking than play games. The best dates feel like adventures, taking you somewhere unfamiliar, with talk that runs late into the night and ranges across the biggest ideas. You bring enthusiasm and generosity to love, and people feel freer for being around you. Commitment can feel like a cage when it arrives too early, and you have been known to pull away just as things were getting serious. Love that grows alongside your freedom is the kind that stays.",
    "capricorn": "You approach romance with care and a certain reserve. Flirting does not come easily in public, and you would rather prove your interest by turning up, reliably, than by sending a stream of compliments. Early dates can feel slightly formal, carefully planned, with a conversation that discreetly checks whether this person has direction. Yet beneath the composure is a dry wit and a surprising sensuality that only emerges once you feel secure. Pleasure often comes to you later in life, as though you had to earn the right to play. You can take love so seriously that the fun gets lost, treating a new relationship like a project to be managed. Relaxed and sure of someone, you offer a devotion that is steady, grown up and felt to the bone.",
    "aquarius": "Love usually starts as friendship for you. You are drawn to people who are a little unusual, and the spark comes through ideas, shared causes or a conversation that surprises you. Flirting is cool, witty and sometimes so understated that the other person misses it completely. Your idea of a good date is something unexpected, a shared cause or an unplanned night with friends that slowly turns into something more. You bring freshness and honesty to romance, and you respect a partner's independence as fiercely as your own. The difficulty comes when emotions run hot and you detach, treating feelings as a puzzle rather than something to be felt. The person who wins you is usually the one who likes every odd corner of you and says so.",
    "pisces": "Love, for you, is like stepping into a dream. You romanticise easily, imagining whole futures from a single lovely evening, and the smallest reminder can bring an old crush flooding back years later. Flirting is soft and intuitive, and you often sense someone's interest before either of you has said a word. The dates that move you have atmosphere, the kind of beauty and stillness that leaves you both quiet afterwards. You are tender and imaginative in love, able to see the best in a person even when they cannot. The risk is seeing only what you wish to see, and trying to rescue people who do not want to change. The love that holds you rests on truth as well as longing."
  },
  "love:house8": {
    "aries": "Intimacy with you begins with heat and honesty. Sexually you are direct and eager, more likely to initiate than to wait, and you trust a partner who meets your intensity head on. Vulnerability is harder: you would rather wrestle than weep, and emotional exposure can feel like losing a fight. Closeness often grows after conflict, when a blazing row clears the air and pulls you both back to bed. You bring courage to the deep end of love, willing to name desire plainly and face what others avoid. Anger can become a shield, though, flaring the moment you feel too exposed or too needed. Merging happens for you when being soft stops feeling like a defeat.",
    "taurus": "Trust, for you, is built through the body. You need to feel physically safe before you can open up, and touch says more than any confession ever could, above all the slow, unhurried closeness that is about presence rather than performance. Once you let someone in, your loyalty runs deep and your sensuality becomes a quiet, steady devotion. Vulnerability arrives slowly, sometimes years into a relationship, when you admit how much you depend on this person. You offer a partner a sense of solid ground that few others can. The hard part is possessiveness, a feeling that whatever you have merged with is now yours to keep. Holding on loosely is the hardest and most rewarding thing this placement asks of you.",
    "gemini": "Closeness for you starts in the mind. You talk your way into intimacy, and the late night conversations where secrets tumble out can feel as charged as sex itself. Desire is curious and playful, full of words, teasing and a willingness to try new things. You want a partner who can talk about everything, including what happens in bed, without awkwardness or embarrassment. Yet exposure can make you skittish, and you might crack a joke or change the subject just as a moment becomes raw. Trust grows through transparency, and a lover who hides things unsettles you more than you admit, sending your mind racing through every possibility. Your deepest nights are the ones where the talking stops.",
    "cancer": "You open up sexually only where you feel emotionally held. Intimacy for you is tender and nurturing, and the most powerful moments are often the quiet ones afterwards, curled up and talking softly in the dark. Trust takes a long time to build, and you test it gently, noticing whether someone remembers the story you once told about your childhood. When you do let someone in, you merge completely, sensing their moods and caring for their wounds as if they were your own. A careless word about your body or a rebuff in bed can sting for months. Moods shape desire, and you can withdraw into your shell without explaining why. With a safe partner, your vulnerability becomes a source of strength.",
    "leo": "Sex, for you, is a place to feel adored. You want to be desired openly and warmly, and a partner who delights in you brings out a generous, playful and slightly theatrical lover. Intimacy means being seen in full colour, and you give lavishly in return, wanting your partner to feel like royalty too. Vulnerability is complicated, because underneath the confidence lives a fear of looking foolish or unwanted. You can hide hurt behind pride, pretending not to care when you feel slighted, and sulk magnificently rather than admit you were wounded. Trust grows when someone admires you on your off days as well as your glorious ones. The partner who holds your heart is the one allowed to see the frightened child behind the star.",
    "virgo": "Intimacy for you is built on attention to detail. You notice what a partner likes, remember the small things that help them relax, and treat sex as a skill worth refining. Trust takes time, because you want to understand someone fully before you let them near your tender places. Beneath the careful exterior sits a good deal of anxiety about being good enough: your body, your performance, your worth. You can hold back, analysing the moment instead of feeling it, or needing everything to feel in order before you can let go. Yet once you trust someone you become devoted, earthy and surprisingly uninhibited. Being imperfect in someone's arms, and staying there, is what closeness turns out to mean for you.",
    "libra": "You want intimacy to be beautiful and fair. Sex works best when it feels like an exchange between equals, attentive, romantic and full of consideration for how your partner feels. Atmosphere matters to you, and closeness feels right when it carries tenderness and a sense of occasion rather than haste. Trust grows through balance, and you notice immediately when one person is giving more than the other. Vulnerability is tricky, because you are so tuned to keeping the peace that you can hide your desires to avoid friction. Sometimes you merge so fully with a partner's wants that you lose track of your own, and resentment builds unspoken. Your most intimate moments are often the least graceful ones, and the most honest.",
    "scorpio": "Intimacy is where you feel most alive. Sex for you is intense, transformative and often close to spiritual, a way to dissolve boundaries and touch something raw in yourself and another person. You want total honesty and total merging, and anything shallow feels almost insulting. Trust is hard won, and you test it, watching for betrayal long before it happens. Once someone has earned your faith, your loyalty is fierce and your capacity for depth is extraordinary. Jealousy, control and old wounds surface easily, and you may hold on to a hurt far longer than you ever show. When you allow yourself to be as exposed as you ask a partner to be, closeness becomes a kind of rebirth.",
    "sagittarius": "You bring openness and adventure into the most private parts of love. Sex is playful, exploratory and often full of laughter, and you are willing to try new things when it feels like a shared journey. Trust grows through honesty, and you would rather hear a difficult truth than a comfortable lie. Vulnerability is the harder terrain, because heavy emotional intensity can make you long for open air and an easy way out. You sometimes turn deep feelings into philosophy, talking about closeness instead of sinking into it. A partner who gives you space earns far more intimacy than one who clings, and you come back warmer for having been allowed to wander. Merging, for you, needs room to breathe.",
    "capricorn": "You take intimacy seriously and earn it slowly. You rarely open up until you are sure someone is committed and reliable, and your trust is built on actions over time, not words in the heat of the moment. Sexually you can be surprisingly earthy and enduring once the walls come down, with a dry humour that appears only in private. Vulnerability can feel like losing control, and you may keep a part of yourself locked away, even from a long term partner. Old responsibilities and fears follow you into the bedroom, sometimes without your noticing. A patient partner finds a lover of depth and loyalty. Letting yourself need someone is the quiet breakthrough here.",
    "aquarius": "Closeness, for you, has to leave room for freedom. You approach sex with curiosity and little regard for convention, happy to explore and experiment without shame, yet emotional merging can make you step back and observe. Trust grows through friendship and honesty, and you are most at ease with a partner who respects your independence. Vulnerability shows up in unexpected ways: a sudden confession in the middle of an ordinary conversation, a cool detachment the moment things feel too intense. You bring openness and acceptance to intimacy, rarely judging a partner's desires. Staying present when feelings become overwhelming is the stretch. Closeness and freedom at once is the combination you are looking for.",
    "pisces": "For you, intimacy is a way to dissolve. Sex can feel mystical, emotional and boundaryless, a merging where you lose track of where you end and your partner begins. You sense a partner's moods and needs almost telepathically, and you give yourself tenderly and fully. Trust comes easily at first, sometimes too easily, and you can idealise a lover before you know who they are. Vulnerability is your natural state, which is both beautiful and risky, because you absorb a partner's pain as if it were your own. Escape creeps in when reality disappoints, through fantasy, withdrawal or drifting away. Deep intimacy works best with someone who honours your softness and holds clear edges for you both."
  },
  "money:house8": {
    "aries": "Shared money makes you restless. You would rather make the call yourself, commit to the deal or take the loan to launch the business, than sit through another long evening of weighing options. You are the one who suggests borrowing to fund something exciting, and the one who pays off a debt in one fierce burst once it starts to annoy you. That courage can pay off handsomely, and people who share finances with you rarely feel stuck. Financial paperwork gets done in a flurry just before the deadline. Arguments over a joint account flare quickly if you sense someone trying to rein you in, and you can sign before reading the terms. Your best financial partnerships pair your speed with a second, slower pair of eyes.",
    "taurus": "Money that is shared has to feel solid before you relax. You are slow to take on a loan, happiest when commitments are fixed, savings are growing and there is a reserve nobody touches. A partner's spending is noticed in detail, and an unexplained cost or a broken agreement about money stays with you. Property and inheritance often weigh heavily in your story, and whatever is passed down to you feels like something to protect rather than spend. Once someone proves reliable with money, your financial trust is steady and generous. Possessiveness is the snag, a sense that what went into the joint pot still somehow belongs to you. Wealth built with you tends to last for decades.",
    "gemini": "Joint finances become a running conversation for you. You compare every option side by side, read the small print on a loan out of sheer curiosity and talk each choice through with a partner at length. That quick mind finds the better interest rate, the tax allowance nobody claimed and the switch that saves hundreds a year. Yet attention scatters, and small payments renew unnoticed or paperwork sits half finished for weeks. Debt tends to arrive in many small pieces rather than one big decision, which makes it easy to lose track of. Arguments about money are lively and rarely bitter. Financial trust with you depends on everything being said out loud, including the awkward numbers.",
    "cancer": "Money you share with someone is tied up with home and family. Joint savings feel like a nest, and you want the home, the emergency fund and the people who depend on you protected above everything else. Family money shapes your story, through help that came with expectations or an inheritance that came with old feelings attached. You are the one who covers a partner's shortfall at the end of the month and never mentions it. Financial secrets hurt you as much as an emotional betrayal would, and a hidden debt can shake your trust for years. Worry makes you hoard, and a low mood can tip you into anxious saving or comfort spending. For you, shared money is only ever as good as the care it provides for the people you love.",
    "leo": "Pooling money with someone brings out your generosity and your pride. You like shared resources to create something worth celebrating, something beautiful and generous that carries your mark for years. You are often the first to treat everyone or lend a friend money with a grand wave of the hand. Debt can creep in through keeping up appearances, spending to match your image rather than your budget. Financial paperwork bores you unless it comes with a sense of achievement. Being left out of a financial decision wounds you far more than the decision itself. With respect flowing both ways, shared wealth in your hands becomes warm and abundant.",
    "virgo": "Your eye for detail shows in joint finances. You are the one who checks the shared accounts line by line, reads every clause of a loan agreement and keeps every record in perfect order. Debt unsettles you, and you would rather clear it methodically, month by month, than let interest pile up. Partners and relatives often hand you their finances to sort out, trusting you to make sense of what baffles them. That care catches mistakes others never even notice. Worry is the cost: a small overspend can feel like a crisis, and your quiet monitoring may read as control to a partner. Order and trust, side by side, are what make shared money feel calm to you.",
    "libra": "Fairness is the first thing you look for when money is shared. You think instinctively in terms of balance: who pays the rent, how the bills split when one person earns more, whether a joint investment treats both names equally. You are good at negotiation, and in a divorce, an inheritance or a family loan you often become the calm voice that finds a settlement. Yet avoiding conflict can cost you. You may agree to an arrangement that quietly disadvantages you, or let a partner manage everything to dodge an awkward talk about debt. Financial choices can also bend towards appearances, paying for style and status as much as for comfort. Joint wealth does best in your life with fairness spoken aloud rather than silently assumed.",
    "scorpio": "Shared money is charged with power for you. You always know who controls the purse strings, and you notice at once when a partner is vague about a balance or a debt. Financial secrets feel like a betrayal of the whole relationship, and you can keep your own accounts private while demanding full disclosure from others. Strategy is your instinct: you are shrewd with investments, inheritances and complicated deals, and you rarely panic when money gets serious. Life often transforms through shared resources, an unexpected inheritance, a settlement after a breakup, a loan that changes everything. Trust around money is total or absent, with very little in between. Given openness instead of suspicion, you are a formidable guardian of what two people build together.",
    "sagittarius": "Optimism runs through the way you handle shared money. You are ready to back a partner's business, invest in a venture abroad or borrow to fund a course that could change everything, trusting that it will all work out. Often it does, and your faith opens doors that more cautious people never walk through. Details are another matter: loan terms skimmed, tax deadlines forgotten, the joint account left for a partner to reconcile. You can be generous to the point of carelessness, lending money to friends and never asking for it back. Honesty matters enormously, and you would rather hear the uncomfortable truth about a debt than be protected from it. Your financial life grows with a partner who enjoys the planning you skip.",
    "capricorn": "In your hands, shared money is serious business. You want joint finances documented, agreed and built for the long haul, with every obligation planned for and every agreement clear. Borrowing without a clear plan makes you uneasy, and debt is something you manage steadily rather than ignore. Family money often comes with duty attached, and you may end up as the one handling the practical side of loss while everyone else grieves. Financial trust is earned over years, never handed out on charm. The drawback is control: you can hold the reins so tightly that a partner feels like a junior employee in their own household. Whatever you build with someone financially is solid, slow and remarkably durable.",
    "aquarius": "Independence matters to you even when money is shared. You often prefer a joint account for the bills alongside separate accounts that stay entirely your own, and any arrangement that feels controlling makes you bristle. You are open to unusual investments, from new technology to a friend's start up or a community housing scheme, and you think about money in terms of principles as much as returns. Shared resources can arrive in unexpected ways, through friends, collectives or a sudden change of circumstance. Money arguments leave you cool and analytical, which can feel detached to a partner who is upset. Sudden changes of plan can unsettle a joint budget. Shared wealth flourishes for you under clear rules with freedom built into them.",
    "pisces": "Finances you share with others can feel foggy to you. You trust partners with the finances easily, sometimes too easily, and statements go unopened while you assume someone else has it in hand. Generosity comes naturally: you lend to people who are struggling, cover costs that are not yours or give away more than the budget allows without keeping score. Inheritances and joint resources can arrive in mysterious ways or slip away just as mysteriously. Intuition sometimes guides you well with investments, a feeling about a place or a person that proves right. The difficulty is follow through, the loan terms never read, the paperwork left for later, and betrayal around money wounds you badly. A practical partner keeping the books turns your open hand into a blessing."
  },
  "career:house6": {
    "aries": "Your working day runs on starts. You like to spot the most urgent fire and put it out before anyone else has finished talking about it. Colleagues learn that handing you the task nobody wants to begin is the quickest way to get it moving, and you enjoy being that person. Slow approvals, long queues and a manager who wants three drafts before anything happens wear you down faster than hard work ever could. Impatience shows as snapping at the person still explaining a problem you solved in your head, or dropping a half finished job the moment a fresher one lands. Clear ownership, short deadlines and a little friendly competition bring out your best, and a job with physical energy in it keeps you keen for years.",
    "taurus": "Steady output is your trademark at work. You settle into a routine and a way of working you trust, and from there you produce the same reliable quality week after week while others lurch between bursts and slumps. Colleagues come to you because you finish what you promised and you do not panic when the deadline moves. A sudden reorganisation, a new system forced on the team overnight or a manager who changes priorities by the hour unsettles you more than you let on, and you dig in, doing it the old way until someone notices. Pleasant surroundings matter, and physical comfort while you work makes a real difference to what you produce. Tangible work, fairly paid and allowed to unfold at a sensible pace, draws out a patience the whole team ends up leaning on.",
    "gemini": "Variety keeps you working. On a good day you juggle several tasks and conversations at once and somehow keep every thread alive, and you are the colleague who knows what is happening everywhere. Tasks get organised in systems of your own that make sense only to you. Repetition is the enemy: a job that asks for the same eight hours every day drains you until your attention wanders and small errors creep in. Too many open threads can also leave several jobs ninety per cent done and none shipped. Writing, coordinating, teaching or moving information between people fits you well. With lively colleagues and something new each week, your quick mind earns its keep many times over.",
    "cancer": "The team matters to you as much as the task. You notice who is struggling, keep spirits up, remember what matters to people and become the person newcomers come to when they are lost. A workplace feels right when it feels a little like home, with familiar faces and a sense that people look after each other. Criticism of your work lands personally, and a cold manager or a tense office can put you off a job you otherwise love. Moods leak into productivity, so some days you fly and others you guard your corner and do the minimum. Caring, feeding, housing or protecting people suits you. Wherever loyalty is rewarded, you give years of devoted, careful service that holds the place together without fanfare.",
    "leo": "Pride shows in the way you do your job. Even routine work gets your personal stamp, and you want it done well enough that people notice the care and polish you bring to it. You bring energy into a room, and colleagues often look to you to lift morale when everyone is flagging. Being overlooked is hard: when credit goes elsewhere or your effort vanishes into a faceless system, your motivation drops sharply. Drudgery without recognition makes you restless and a little dramatic behind the scenes. Visible roles suit you, leading a small team or serving with some flair. A sincere thank you from the right person can keep you glowing through months of ordinary effort.",
    "virgo": "Order is how you care for your work. You build systems, checklists and routines that make a chaotic day manageable, and you spot the typo, the missing figure or the step everyone else skipped. Colleagues trust you with detail because they know you will check it twice. Being useful satisfies you more than being applauded. The flip side is worry, with evenings spent replaying a small mistake and a habit of redoing other people's work because it was not quite right. Perfectionism can slow you to a crawl on a job that only needed to be good enough. Editing, analysis, health, craft and administration all reward the careful mind you bring to every shift.",
    "libra": "Harmony at work is what lets you function. You are the colleague who smooths over a tense meeting, finds wording both sides can accept and keeps the team on speaking terms. Your sharpest thinking happens in partnership: bouncing ideas off someone, sharing a project, having a reliable second pair of eyes. A shabby workspace or rude behaviour bothers you more than a heavy workload, and you put effort into making things look and feel right. Decisions can drag, since you weigh every option and want everyone content before committing. A clash with a colleague can occupy your thoughts for days while you stay politely pleasant on the surface. Design, negotiation, client work and anything built on fairness make good use of your tact.",
    "scorpio": "Intensity runs through your working day. When a task grips you, you dig until you reach the bottom of it, staying late to trace a problem back to its root while others have gone home. You notice the office politics, the unspoken rivalries and who holds power, and you rarely reveal how much you have seen. Colleagues sense you are not someone to cross, and your trust is earned slowly. Shallow tasks and micromanagement irritate you, and feeling controlled can turn into quiet resistance or a grudge that lasts years. Research, investigation, crisis work and finance draw you in. Wherever hidden mechanics need uncovering, your stamina and focus make you formidable in a way people remember long after you move on.",
    "sagittarius": "Freedom and meaning are what you need from a job. You work best when you understand why the task matters, and a role with room to travel, learn or move between projects keeps your spirits high. Colleagues enjoy your humour, and you are often the one who reminds the team of the bigger picture when everyone is buried in detail. Routine paperwork is another matter: it gets postponed, rushed or forgotten. You can overpromise, saying yes to three things because they all sound exciting and then scrambling to deliver. Micromanagement feels like a cage. Teaching, publishing, travel and outdoor work all fit, and an employer who trusts you with a long leash gets your most generous effort.",
    "capricorn": "You treat work as a long game. Each day is organised around goals, priorities and what needs doing to reach the next level, and you carry more responsibility than your job title suggests. Colleagues see you as the dependable one who meets deadlines and keeps standards up when others let them slip. Workload is rarely the problem, since you would rather take on too much than be seen as unreliable, and that can mean long hours with very little praise. Criticism of your competence cuts deep. Rest feels like something to be earned. Structured roles with clear progression suit you, because your effort compounds year on year into an authority that arrives slowly and then stays.",
    "aquarius": "Your way of working rarely matches the manual. You spot the inefficient process everyone else accepts and redesign it, often with a tool or shortcut nobody asked for. Colleagues value your fairness and your refusal to play favourites, and you often end up as the team's unofficial voice when something is unjust. Rigid hours and pointless rules drain you quickly, and you work best with flexibility, remote days or at least the freedom to organise tasks your own way. Emotional office drama leaves you cool and a little detached, which some people read as aloofness. Technology, science and community projects appeal. A team that shares a purpose earns your loyalty far more reliably than any pay rise.",
    "pisces": "Intuition guides the way you work. You sense what a colleague needs before they say it and often absorb the mood of everyone around you, which makes you kind company and a natural helper. Structure is harder: deadlines blur, loose ends pile up, and your surroundings may reflect a mind that is somewhere more interesting. Boundaries are the test, since you say yes to extra tasks out of sympathy and end up quietly overloaded. Harsh, cutthroat workplaces exhaust you, and you do better where compassion or creativity is part of the job. Music, art, healing and care work all call to you. When the work feels meaningful, you give it a devotion that surprises everyone, yourself included."
  },
  "health:house6": {
    "aries": "Your body runs hot and fast. Energy arrives in bursts, and you feel best after something vigorous that gets your heart pounding and leaves you breathless. Sitting still through long days makes you irritable, and pent up frustration shows as tension around the head, jaw and shoulders. You push through tiredness until you crash, and the bumps and scrapes you collect come from rushing rather than bad luck. Routines last only when they feel like a challenge, so a target to beat keeps you exercising where a gentle plan would not. Rest is the part you skip. Your stamina rebounds quickly, which is why cooling down deserves the same seriousness you give to warming up.",
    "taurus": "Steadiness keeps your body well. You thrive on regular meals, a good night's sleep and routines that barely change from week to week, and your stamina is deep once you get going. Comfort matters: good food, rest and physical ease are not luxuries to you but part of feeling right. The same love of comfort can make exercise hard to start, and one lazy evening can quietly become a lazy month. Stress often settles in the throat, neck and shoulders, or in eating for reassurance. Gentle, rhythmic and pleasurable movement agrees with you far more than punishing drills. Once a healthy habit is established you keep it for years, so the first few weeks decide everything.",
    "gemini": "Your nerves and your energy are closely wired. You feel lively when your mind is busy and flat when bored, and your body follows your thoughts more than most. Restlessness shows in fidgeting, shallow breathing, a racing mind at bedtime and too many hours on a screen. Routines rarely survive in one fixed form, so plenty of variety keeps you moving where a single regime would lose you. Irregular meals and eating on the go are familiar habits. Talking, writing and laughter lower your stress. Sleep and breath repay attention more than anything, since a calmer nervous system gives your quick mind a body that can keep pace with it.",
    "cancer": "Feelings and digestion are closely linked for you. When something upsets you, your stomach often knows before you do, and a tense week can show in appetite, sleep or a heavy tiredness. Home cooking and familiar routines are restorative, and a warm meal and a quiet evening in your own space make a visible difference. Comfort eating and staying in when low are recognisable patterns. Your energy rises and falls in tides rather than holding steady, so rigid fitness plans often break down after a few weeks. Gentle, familiar movement in company you trust works well. Caring for others can leave little for your own body, which recovers best when you nurture it as generously as you nurture them.",
    "leo": "Vitality is your natural state. When life feels joyful you have energy to burn, and warmth, fun and good company lift you physically as well as emotionally. Your heart, circulation and back take the strain of stress, and pride can stop you admitting you are exhausted. Routines stick when they are fun and a little social, with energy, company and a challenge you can share. Dull, solitary regimes are abandoned quickly. You can overdo it, playing hard and resting little, then feeling flat for days. Appreciation feeds your wellbeing more than people realise, and a life with room for creative play keeps both body and spirits strong.",
    "virgo": "Health is an area you think about carefully. You notice small changes in your body, read labels, track steps and often know more about nutrition than your friends. A tidy schedule of meals, sleep and exercise helps you feel in control. Worry is the main drain on your energy, and stress settles in the gut, with fussiness around food or sleepless nights spent running through lists. Too much attention can turn into anxious checking of every twinge. Gentle, regular practices such as walking, stretching or yoga agree with your system far better than extremes. When your mind is calm your body is remarkably efficient, and your habits become a quiet foundation that keeps you well for decades.",
    "libra": "Balance is what your body asks for. You feel good when life is harmonious, and conflict, rushing or an ugly environment drains your energy surprisingly quickly. Rich food, late nights and sweet treats can tip you off course, especially when you are being sociable and going along with others. Exercise works best with a partner or in a pleasant setting, where movement feels graceful rather than grim. Solo slogs rarely last. Stress often shows in the lower back, the skin or a general sense of being out of sorts rather than one clear symptom. With a gentle rhythm of activity and rest and peaceful relationships around you, your wellbeing steadies and your natural grace returns.",
    "scorpio": "Your body keeps your secrets. Stress you do not talk about gets stored somewhere, and you often only notice how tense you have been when it lets go. Stamina is deep: you can push through remarkable demands, and you are drawn to intense exercise that burns off anger or pressure and takes you to your limit. All or nothing is a familiar pattern, with strict regimes followed by stretches of complete neglect. You recover fully once you let yourself stop. After a hard period your body has an uncanny way of rebuilding itself stronger than before.",
    "sagittarius": "Movement and freedom keep you healthy. You feel best outdoors, on the move, with a sense of adventure, and open space and new surroundings restore you more than any fixed routine. Routines feel restrictive, so you start plans enthusiastically and drop them when they become repetitive. Excess is your weak spot: generous portions, one more indulgence, overdoing it whenever you are enjoying yourself. Your hips, thighs and liver tend to feel the effects when you overdo it. Optimism keeps you resilient, and you bounce back quickly from setbacks. A goal worth training for keeps your body engaged far longer than discipline alone.",
    "capricorn": "Discipline shapes your health. Once you commit to a routine you stick to it, and your stamina grows steadily with age rather than fading. Work often comes first, though, and you run on reserves, skipping meals or sleep while you finish something important. Tension collects in the bones, knees, teeth and shoulders, and you carry responsibility physically in a stiff neck or a set jaw. Admitting you are tired can feel like weakness, so early signals get ignored. Steady, strength-building movement gives your body the framework it likes. You tend to grow healthier as you get older, once rest becomes part of the plan rather than a reward.",
    "aquarius": "Your body responds to freedom and novelty. You feel energetic when life is stimulating and rebel against any routine that feels imposed, so a fixed exercise schedule tends to last only a few weeks. Unusual approaches appeal, and anything new or experimental holds your interest where the familiar would not. Circulation, ankles and your nervous system register stress, and irregular sleep patterns are common. You can live in your head and forget your body until it demands attention. Moving alongside other people keeps you engaged better than training alone. Built around your own rhythm rather than someone else's rules, your health becomes one of your most inventive projects.",
    "pisces": "Sensitivity is the key to your health. You absorb the atmosphere around you, and a stressful environment or a difficult person can leave you drained without any clear reason. Sleep and dreams matter enormously, and a disrupted night affects you more than most. Your feet, immunity and energy levels often mirror your emotional state. Escapes such as too much screen time, sugar or alcohol creep in when life feels heavy. Water in any form is healing, and calm, flowing surroundings restore you quickly. Flowing, gentle movement sits more kindly with you than harsh regimes, and quiet time away from the crowd is when your energy refills."
  },
  "spirit:house12": {
    "aries": "Your inner life is more restless than people guess. Solitude does not come easily, and when you do withdraw you often find a fierce, private drive underneath, a warrior fighting battles nobody else sees. Anger can be the hidden emotion, turned inward as frustration with yourself rather than expressed. Dreams are vivid and active, full of chases, contests and urgent journeys. A secret courage appears when you are alone with a crisis and nobody is there to watch. Stillness comes most easily through movement, and your mind quietens once your body has had a chance to spend itself. Faith, for you, is something to act on rather than contemplate, and the paths that call you ask for bravery and direct experience.",
    "taurus": "Stillness and the senses shape your inner world. You retreat into comfort and familiarity, and find something close to prayer in the simple physical pleasures that ground you. Private worries often concern security, with fears about money or losing what you have built that you seldom share. Dreams can be earthy and sensual, full of food, nature and familiar places. A deep inner patience helps you endure hard times with quiet strength. Your spirituality trusts what the body feels rather than abstract ideas, and nature is your cathedral. Stubborn attachments can keep you stuck, yet letting go of an old possession or habit often opens a peace you never expected.",
    "gemini": "Your mind rarely switches off, even in solitude. Alone at night you replay conversations, invent imaginary dialogues and chase ideas through half remembered books, and your dreams are often chatty, busy and full of messages. Many thoughts stay private, along with a hidden nervousness or a sense that no one quite hears what you mean. Words are your natural form of retreat, and putting your thoughts in order helps you settle. Intuition arrives as a sudden phrase or a coincidence that answers something you had been turning over for days. You collect teachings from many paths rather than following one. Stillness of mind is hard won, and when it comes it brings insight that surprises even you.",
    "cancer": "Memory and feeling fill your private world. Solitude often takes you back to childhood, family and the past, and old feelings surface when you are alone. Dreams can be vivid and nostalgic, featuring houses, water, mothers and places you once lived. Fears of abandonment or of being left without shelter sit underneath, and you may nurture others while keeping your own needs out of view. Retreat means home, comfort and simple nourishment, close to people you trust completely. Your intuition is almost physical, felt in the stomach before it becomes a thought. The sacred shows up for you in care and belonging, and in the slow healing of old family patterns.",
    "leo": "Beneath your outer self sits a private need to be seen, which you may feel shy about admitting. Alone, you can be your own harshest audience, and fears of being ordinary or unloved run underneath a confident manner. Your dreams are often theatrical, with performances, stages and moments of recognition. Creative expression done privately, for no one but yourself, is one of your truest forms of retreat. A generous heart works behind the scenes, and anonymous kindness can bring you more joy than any applause. There is an inner light in you that needs no audience, and discovering that your worth does not depend on anyone watching is freeing.",
    "virgo": "Order and service shape your inner life. In solitude you tidy, sort and plan, and quiet routines feel almost sacred. Worry is the familiar companion, a private voice that checks, doubts and criticises long after everyone else has moved on. Dreams can be detailed and practical, sometimes filled with lists, tasks or unfinished work. Your hidden strength is devotion: you help others behind the scenes without needing thanks, and that anonymous service brings peace. Useful work with your hands or a disciplined practice settles you more than idle rest. Humility and daily ritual carry spiritual meaning for you, and forgiving your own imperfections turns out to be one of the most healing things you ever do.",
    "libra": "Harmony is what your inner self keeps seeking. Alone, you often reflect on relationships, weighing what was said and whether you were fair, and resentments stay hidden to keep the peace outwardly. Loneliness and conflict are the quiet fears, and you may struggle to know what you want apart from others. Your dreams are often filled with beautiful places, partners and scenes of reconciliation. Art, music and beauty restore you, and harmony in your surroundings works on you like a retreat. Intuition comes through a sense of balance, a feeling when something is off. Love, justice and grace are the paths that speak to you, and making peace within yourself brings the calm you keep creating for others.",
    "scorpio": "Deep water runs beneath your calm surface. You keep your truest feelings hidden, and solitude is where you process grief, desire and rage that others never glimpse. Dreams can be powerful, sometimes dark, full of transformation, secrets and symbols that stay with you for days. Betrayal and loss of control are the fears you guard against, often without realising how much you carry. Your intuition is formidable: you sense undercurrents, hidden motives and unspoken truths. Retreat for you is a kind of rebirth, a going underground before emerging changed. Mystery, psychology and anything that looks directly at life and death fascinate you, and your greatest resource is the capacity to heal from within.",
    "sagittarius": "Somewhere inside you a traveller is always searching. In solitude you think about meaning, faith and the big questions, and you often feel a private sense of being guided or protected. Dreams can be expansive and adventurous, featuring travel, foreign places, teachers and flights. A hidden restlessness is common, a feeling that something more is waiting and that ordinary life is not quite enough. Optimism is a secret strength that carries you through dark periods more reliably than you expect. Nature, pilgrimage and places far from home all make good sanctuaries. As a seeker drawn to philosophy and wisdom traditions, your deepest growth comes from turning the quest inward instead of always looking over the horizon.",
    "capricorn": "Your inner life is serious and self reliant. In private you carry responsibilities and fears that you rarely admit, particularly fears of failure, inadequacy or being unprepared. Solitude can bring a heavy sense of duty, yet it is also where you build quiet resilience. Dreams may involve structures, mountains, exams or authority figures. You are wiser than you let on, with a hidden maturity others lean on without knowing its cost. Structure, quiet and a sense of continuity with the past settle you better than unplanned idleness. Tradition, ancestors and patience hold spiritual weight for you, and loosening your grip on control reveals a faith that grows stronger with the years.",
    "aquarius": "Detachment and vision colour your inner world. Alone, you think about humanity, the future and ideas far larger than yourself, and your mind often feels like it belongs somewhere else. Feelings of being an outsider or misunderstood can run beneath your friendly manner. Dreams are often strange, futuristic or full of flashes of insight that arrive without warning. Intuition works like a lightning bolt, sudden and certain. Wide open space and a small circle of fellow thinkers restore you. Unconventional paths appeal, science and mysticism alike, and the part of you that feels different turns out to be what connects you to the whole.",
    "pisces": "Boundless and porous, your inner life has few walls. Solitude feels natural, even necessary, because the world overwhelms you, and regular retreat is how you recover your sense of self. Dreams are vivid, symbolic and sometimes uncannily accurate, and you may remember them in rich detail. Your intuition picks up moods and hidden currents others miss entirely. Being lost or overwhelmed is the quiet fear, and escapism tempts you when life gets heavy. Music, water, art and meditation are natural sanctuaries. Compassion and surrender come easily to you, and your greatest peace arrives when you stop fighting the current and trust the tide of life."
  },
  "mind:house3": {
    "aries": "Your everyday mind runs hot and fast. With Aries on the 3rd house cusp, you answer before the question is finished, jump into a debate without warming up and learn by doing rather than reading about it first. Words come out direct, sometimes blunt, and people always know where they stand after a chat with you. Siblings may have been rivals as much as allies, the people you competed with hardest and argued with most freely. Your quick tongue can land harder than you meant, and a half heard point sometimes becomes a fight you did not need. Short bursts of focused learning suit you far better than long courses, and you are drawn to neighbourhoods and conversations with a bit of energy in them.",
    "taurus": "Thinking, for you, is a slow and thorough business. Taurus on the cusp of the 3rd means you check everything twice, let a new idea settle until it feels solid and remember what you learned years later because you took it in so carefully. Your speaking voice is calm and pleasant, and people find your way of communicating reassuringly unhurried. You like familiar places, familiar routes and people nearby whom you have known for years. Siblings are often a steady presence, someone you can turn to about practical things without fuss. Stubbornness is the snag: once you have made up your mind, a clever counterargument only makes you dig in. What you learn best is anything you can touch, taste, build or use with your own hands, slowly, until it becomes second nature.",
    "gemini": "Gemini sits naturally on the 3rd house, so your mind is quick, curious and rarely quiet. Your attention runs on several tracks at once, with several interests always half explored, and you can strike up an easy, lively conversation with almost anyone you happen to meet. Words come easily, and you can say exactly what you mean in writing as readily as out loud. Brothers, sisters or cousins were often your first sparring partners in wordplay and teasing. Scattering is the price of all this: you know a little about a great deal and can struggle to finish the one thing you committed to learning. Your mind wants variety, fresh information and people to swap it with, and lively surroundings suit you far better than silent ones.",
    "cancer": "With Cancer on the 3rd house, feelings and thoughts arrive together. You remember what someone said by how it made you feel, and you can replay an awkward conversation in your head for days. Your way of talking is warm and protective; you check that everyone is all right before you get to the point. Siblings carry emotional weight in your story, and the old family roles return the moment you are all together again, however grown up you have become. Your local world matters too: you notice who nearby needs looking after, and you feel most at home where people know your name. Moods colour your judgement, so on a bad day an ordinary remark can sound like criticism. Learning sticks when it feels safe and personal, taught by someone who cares.",
    "leo": "You speak as though there is an audience, even when there is only one friend across the table. Leo on the 3rd house cusp gives your everyday talk warmth, colour and a natural sense of storytelling, so the most ordinary moment becomes an anecdote people ask you to repeat. Writing carries your personality, and a plain message from you rarely stays plain for long. With siblings there may have been a quiet contest over who was the favourite or the funniest. You learn best when you can shine, answer the question aloud or teach what you have just discovered. Pride is the sticking point: being corrected in front of others stings, and you can hold on to a position to save face. Generous encouragement from you lifts everyone in the room.",
    "virgo": "Your mind notices the small error, the missing step and the detail everyone else has overlooked. Virgo on the 3rd house cusp makes everyday thinking precise, analytical and useful, and you are the one who reads the instructions and then explains them to everyone else. You communicate carefully, improve other people's work without being asked and keep your week in meticulous order. Siblings may have relied on you as the sensible one, or you may have sharpened your wit on their mistakes. Local life runs to order: you know how your surroundings work, where to find what you need and exactly whom to ask. Worry is the catch, since an overactive mind turns a small comment into hours of analysis. You learn beautifully through practice, detail and a skill you can refine.",
    "libra": "Conversation, for you, is a kind of dance. With Libra on the 3rd house cusp you choose your words gracefully, soften bad news and instinctively see both sides of every argument you hear. People come to you to mediate, because you can calm a quarrel without anyone feeling they have lost face. You think best in dialogue, turning an idea over with someone rather than alone at a desk. Your writing has polish and tact, and you care how your words will land long before you share them. Indecision is the cost: you can weigh two options so fairly that you never pick one, and you sometimes agree aloud while disagreeing silently. Learning goes well in pairs or pleasant surroundings, and a touch of beauty around you helps you concentrate.",
    "scorpio": "Nothing said in passing escapes you. Scorpio on the 3rd house cusp gives your everyday mind a detective's edge: you read between the lines of every exchange, notice what was left out of the story and remember the exact wording of an argument years later. You speak sparingly but with weight, and one sentence from you can end a debate. Siblings may have been the source of deep loyalty, fierce rivalry or secrets kept for decades. You prefer to know the people around you slowly and privately rather than share your business with everyone. Suspicion is the trap, because a mind that looks for hidden motives will usually find one, there or not. Learning, for you, means going deep, researching a subject until you understand what drives it, and a half explained answer never satisfies you.",
    "sagittarius": "Your everyday thinking is broad, cheerful and prone to wandering off the subject. With Sagittarius on the 3rd house cusp, a quick chat about the weather turns into a conversation about philosophy, and you would rather grasp the big picture than memorise the details. You talk with enthusiasm and humour, and your honesty can be startlingly frank. Siblings might live far away, come from different cultures or have been your partners in childhood adventure. Local trips rarely stay local, and even a short errand turns into a detour towards something you have never tried. Restlessness makes routine study hard, and you can promise a reply, a lesson or a visit you never quite deliver. Lessons stick when they are lively, practical and connected to something that matters to you.",
    "capricorn": "Like a well run office, your head keeps everything filed. Capricorn on the 3rd house cusp makes everyday thinking serious, structured and focused on what is useful, so you plan ahead without being asked and say what you mean in as few words as possible. People trust what you say because you rarely say it lightly. As a child you may have felt older than your years, perhaps responsible for siblings or quieter than the chatty ones around you. Learning came with effort rather than ease, and what you learned stays because you worked for it. Pessimism is the undertow, a habit of assuming the worst or dismissing your own ideas before sharing them. With age your voice gains authority, and the people around you often come to you for sensible advice.",
    "aquarius": "Your thoughts arrive from unexpected angles. With Aquarius on the 3rd house cusp you question the obvious, spot the flaw in the accepted method and enjoy a conversation most when it goes somewhere unusual. Ideas arrive with an urgency that cannot wait to be shared, and you tend to hear about the next new thing long before everyone else does. Siblings may feel more like friends, or the relationship may be marked by distance and independence. You are good at bringing neighbours together for a cause, yet you keep a certain detachment from the daily gossip. Stubbornness in thinking is the paradox: the rebel mind can cling to its own contrary view as fiercely as anyone. You learn best by experimenting, online or among like minded people who let you think out loud.",
    "pisces": "Your mind moves like water, picking up moods and images as easily as facts. Pisces on the 3rd house cusp means you think in pictures and feelings, remember the atmosphere of a conversation better than its content and often know what someone means before they have found the words. Your writing can be poetic, and you express yourself beautifully in music, images or a heartfelt message. Siblings may be tender, elusive or in need of your compassion. You move through everyday life half in a daydream, noticing beauty in small things and losing track of where you were going. Vagueness is the price: details slip, appointments blur and a promise to reply gets lost. You learn by absorbing, through stories, music and teachers who inspire you rather than drill you."
  },
  "mind:house9": {
    "aries": "Higher learning, for you, is something to charge at. Aries on the 9th house cusp gives you a pioneering intellect that wants to be first to a new theory, quick to challenge authority and far too eager to wait for permission to think. You gravitate towards subjects that feel like a challenge or a cause, and you can defend a big idea with fire. Teaching others lights you up when you can inspire rather than repeat. Impatience is the catch: long degrees, slow research and peer review test your nerves, and you may abandon a course once the excitement fades. Short, intense bursts of study suit you best, and you are willing to publish bold ideas others are too cautious to put their name to.",
    "taurus": "You build knowledge the way you would build a house, brick by brick. Taurus on the 9th house cusp gives a mind for higher learning that is patient, practical and sceptical of theories that cannot be applied. You would rather master one field thoroughly than skim five, and patient, quiet study is a genuine pleasure. Subjects linked to the earth, money, art, food or the body hold your attention longest. Once you trust a school of thought you stay loyal to it, and your teaching is clear and grounded. The difficulty is inflexibility, since a new paradigm can feel like an attack on what you worked hard to learn. Finished work from you is solid, lasting and worth publishing, even if it takes years to arrive.",
    "gemini": "Ideas pull you in several directions at once. Gemini on the 9th house cusp gives higher learning a restless, versatile feel: you might change your degree subject, study two languages at the same time or collect short courses the way others collect souvenirs. You love debate, lectures and discussion, and you absorb a surprising amount from conversation alone. Writing and publishing are natural outlets, and years of scattered notes have a way of becoming something substantial. You teach with wit and can translate a dense theory into plain language. Scattered commitment is the cost, with brilliant starts outnumbering finished projects. Your mind is at home in the marketplace of ideas, trading, comparing and connecting thinkers who would never otherwise meet.",
    "cancer": "Your big ideas start at home. With Cancer on the 9th house cusp, higher learning is coloured by feeling, family and memory, and you are drawn to history, psychology, heritage or anything that explains where people come from. The best teacher in your life probably felt like a parent, and you study best in a place that feels safe and familiar. You may teach in a nurturing way, remembering every student's name and worrying about the quiet ones. Beliefs inherited from family weigh heavily on your thinking, and questioning them, even privately, can feel like disloyalty. Moods also make study inconsistent. Writing from personal experience gives your work its power, and the story of where you come from often feels like one you are meant to tell.",
    "leo": "Learning is a stage for you, and knowledge is something you want to share with flair. Leo on the 9th house cusp gives you a big, generous intellect that loves to hold a room, and you share the ideas that changed your life with infectious warmth and conviction. You are drawn to the arts, drama, leadership or any subject with a touch of grandeur. Recognition matters: seeing what you know acknowledged, with your name attached, means more to you than you admit. Pride can make it hard to be a beginner, and you may avoid courses where you cannot shine quickly. A natural talent for inspiring students makes teaching and public speaking rewarding.",
    "virgo": "Higher education, for you, is about getting it right. Virgo on the 9th house cusp gives a scholarly mind that loves methodology, footnotes and the satisfaction of a properly referenced argument. You organise knowledge meticulously, and you are the one who spots the flaw in someone else's reasoning at once. Practical fields draw you, such as health, science, editing, analysis or any discipline that improves how things work. Teaching suits you when you can break a subject into clear steps and watch someone master them. Perfectionism is what holds you back: you may keep revising a thesis or manuscript long after it is ready and hesitate to publish anything with a possible error in it. Knowledge that serves people is what excites you most.",
    "libra": "Justice, beauty and fairness are the big questions that pull you into study. Libra on the 9th house cusp makes higher learning sociable and balanced: you think best in discussion and partnership, and you love comparing philosophies side by side. Law, art, design, diplomacy and the study of relationships can all suit you. You write elegantly and teach with tact, making even hard ideas feel reasonable to a sceptical room. Indecisiveness is the stumbling block, since you can see merit in every school of thought and struggle to commit to one argument or even one course. A big piece of work can stall while you weigh one more perspective. Your mind is at its most brilliant when it builds bridges between opposing views.",
    "scorpio": "You want to know what lies beneath. Scorpio on the 9th house cusp gives higher learning an investigative intensity: you are drawn to psychology, forensics, the occult, economics, medicine or anything that reveals hidden forces. A single subject can absorb you for years, and your research goes to the bottom of every source, including the footnotes nobody else reads. You teach with depth and magnetism, and students remember you long after. Publishing can feel exposing, so you may hold your best ideas back until they are bulletproof. Obsession is the danger, along with a tendency to dismiss teachers or ideas you see as shallow. When you do share your thinking, it has a way of changing the people who hear it.",
    "sagittarius": "Sagittarius is at home on the 9th house cusp, and your mind is built for big ideas. You love philosophy, languages, law, comparative religion, travel writing and any subject that widens the map of what is possible. Places of learning can feel like playgrounds, and your mind happily runs several subjects at once without tiring. Teaching comes easily because your enthusiasm is contagious and you connect facts to meaning. Publishing and broadcasting also call to you, and you can hold an audience with a sweeping argument. The weak spot is detail and follow through, since you grow bored once the grand concept is grasped, and your certainty can tip into lecturing. You are always one lecture away from a new passion.",
    "capricorn": "You take higher learning seriously, as an investment in your future standing. Capricorn on the 9th house cusp gives a disciplined, ambitious intellect that respects qualifications, traditions and people who have earned their authority. You may start your studies later in life, or take the hard route of learning alongside work, and finish what others abandon. Subjects with structure and a practical payoff appeal: business, law, history, architecture or management. As a teacher or author you are thorough and authoritative, and nothing you put your name to is ever sloppy. Rigidity is the risk, a scepticism towards unconventional ideas and a fear that your work is not yet good enough to publish. With age your expertise becomes an asset that others seek out.",
    "aquarius": "Your mind reaches for the future. Aquarius on the 9th house cusp draws you to science, technology, sociology, astrology or any discipline that challenges the way things have always been taught. You may learn online, in unconventional schools or entirely by your own methods, and you have little patience for rote memorisation. Big ideas excite you most when they could change society. You teach as a peer rather than an authority, and your writing is original and sometimes ahead of its time. Detachment is the difficulty: you can argue from principle so coolly that you overlook the human side, and you may reject a tradition before understanding it. Networks of fellow thinkers, forums and research groups feed your intellectual life more than any single professor.",
    "pisces": "Imagination shapes the way you study. Pisces on the 9th house cusp draws your mind towards poetry, music, film, psychology, spirituality and the stories that explain how people feel. You absorb ideas from atmosphere and intuition, and you may understand a text intimately without being able to quote a line of it. Structured courses can feel confining, and deadlines slip away as you follow a thread that interests you more. Teaching flows when you can inspire and empathise, and your writing often has a dreamy, lyrical quality. Confusion is the pitfall, along with a habit of idealising teachers or theories without testing them. Your best work arrives when inspiration is paired with a little structure and a firm hand on the deadline."
  },
  "growth:house9": {
    "aries": "Your search for meaning begins with a leap. Aries on the 9th house cusp makes faith something you act on rather than contemplate: you leap before you look and discover what you believe by testing it against daily life. Adventure is a need, and you feel most alive when you are somewhere new and slightly out of your depth. Your convictions are passionate, and you will fight for a cause you believe in. The shadow is zealotry, a habit of treating your current truth as the only truth, and of burning through a new belief as quickly as you picked it up. Courage grows your spirit, above all the courage to walk where no one has shown you the way.",
    "taurus": "Meaning, for you, has to be felt in the body and the senses. Taurus on the 9th house cusp gives a faith that grows slowly, rooted in nature, beauty and the steady rituals of daily life. You would rather know one place deeply than rush through many, and you measure any journey by how it feels in your body and senses. Your beliefs are sturdy and practical; you trust what has proved itself through experience. Resistance to new perspectives is the danger, because a comfortable worldview can harden into a fixed one. Spiritual growth comes through unhurried experience, time in nature and a spirituality that honours the physical world rather than trying to escape it.",
    "gemini": "Your spiritual life stays curious and on the move. Gemini on the 9th house cusp makes you a seeker who collects perspectives, dipping into several teachings and their critics at once. Travel appeals when it is varied and frequent, full of conversation and detours. A single conversation can change your outlook more than any sermon. You can hold two beliefs at once without much discomfort, and you enjoy the tension between them. Restlessness is the snag, as you can sample meaning endlessly without committing to a path deep enough to hold you in hard times. Growth arrives when your curiosity settles on something worth staying with.",
    "cancer": "Faith, for you, feels like home. Cancer on the 9th house cusp ties your search for meaning to family, ancestry and belonging, and you may keep the traditions and rituals you grew up with long after you stopped calling yourself religious. Travel often has an emotional purpose, drawing you towards your roots or towards places that instantly feel familiar. Your beliefs protect and comfort you when life turns stormy. Clinging is the trouble, holding on to the faith you were raised in out of loyalty or fear rather than conviction. Homesickness can also cut your adventures short. Your spirit grows when you allow a new place or a new belief to become a second home.",
    "leo": "You travel and believe with a big, open heart. Leo on the 9th house cusp gives your search for meaning a joyful, dramatic quality: you want adventures worth telling, full of colour, celebration and grandeur. Faith for you is about celebration and creativity rather than solemn duty, and you are drawn to teachers and traditions with charisma. You can inspire others with the warmth of your convictions. Pride is the pitfall, since your beliefs become part of your identity so that doubt feels like humiliation, and you may prefer the spotlight of a cause to its quiet work. A generous faith, one that makes room for other people's light as well as your own, is where you grow.",
    "virgo": "Meaning, for you, is found in useful devotion. Virgo on the 9th house cusp gives a practical spirituality: rituals of health, service and daily practice matter more to you than grand theology. You plan journeys meticulously, leaving little to chance, and you often travel to learn a skill or to help others. Your beliefs are examined and refined, never swallowed whole. Scepticism is healthy in you until it becomes nitpicking cynicism, and anxiety over details can keep you from enjoying the journey itself. Useful service, structured learning and a faith lived through small daily acts help your spirit grow steadily, one careful practice at a time.",
    "libra": "Your faith looks for harmony. Libra on the 9th house cusp makes beauty, fairness and relationships the doors through which meaning enters your life: a moment of harmony or a friendship with someone from another culture can move you profoundly. Experiences shared with someone close mean more to you, and adventures shared feel richer than those taken alone. Your beliefs lean towards justice and balance, and you are drawn to philosophies of peace. Leaning on others for your convictions is the weak point, adopting a partner's worldview instead of forming your own. Growth comes as you find a personal faith graceful enough to stand on its own, one you can hold with the same care you give the people you love.",
    "scorpio": "You seek truth that goes down to the roots. Scorpio on the 9th house cusp makes your search for meaning intense and transformative: you are drawn to mystery traditions, rebirth, death and the hidden laws of life. Travel may draw you to places with a powerful or haunted atmosphere, and one journey can change you permanently. Your faith is forged through crisis, and you may lose and rebuild your beliefs more than once in a lifetime. Fanaticism and bitter cynicism are the two extremes you can swing between. Facing what frightens you is the path, and you emerge with a faith that has survived something, quieter than before and far harder to shake.",
    "sagittarius": "The world is your temple. Sagittarius on the 9th house cusp makes you a natural pilgrim and optimist: part of you is always ready to go, the next horizon already in sight and your faith in life's goodness unusually robust. You find meaning in open roads, foreign cultures and the thrill of an unknown horizon. Your beliefs are expansive, generous and often eclectic, drawing on many traditions at once. Overreach is the danger: promising too much, trusting luck too far or preaching your truth to people who never asked for it. Adventure feeds your soul, and you grow whenever you let a new culture humble you and enlarge you, returning home with fewer certainties and a wider heart.",
    "capricorn": "Your faith is built slowly and tested by time. Capricorn on the 9th house cusp gives a sober, disciplined spirituality: you respect tradition, structure and teachers who have earned their place, and you may come to belief later in life after years of scepticism. Travel is usually purposeful, planned with care and taken for a reason rather than on a whim. Cynicism is the heaviness here, a sense that life's big questions are for other people, or a rigid moral code applied harshly to yourself. Maturity brings a grounded, reliable faith and the late blooming joy of adventures you allow yourself to take.",
    "aquarius": "Your search for meaning refuses to follow the crowd. Aquarius on the 9th house cusp gives unconventional beliefs: you may blend reason with spirituality or build a faith of your own design, and you question every dogma handed to you. Travel appeals when it is unusual, taking you where few people go or among people with a vision for a better world. You find meaning in ideals and collective progress. Aloofness is the risk, holding faith at arm's length as an intellectual exercise rather than letting it touch your heart. Growth comes through circles of fellow seekers and beliefs that serve humanity rather than only yourself.",
    "pisces": "Faith comes to you like weather, felt more than understood. Pisces on the 9th house cusp gives a mystical, compassionate spirituality: you are moved by beauty, stillness and coincidences that feel like messages. Travel draws you towards places with a spiritual atmosphere, and you often return from a journey changed in ways you cannot explain. Your beliefs are inclusive and gentle, with room for every lost soul. The shadow is escapism, using spirituality or travel to avoid daily life, or following a guru too trustingly. Your spirit grows when devotion is paired with discernment and your compassion reaches the people right beside you as well as the whole world."
  },
  "money:house2": {
    "aries": "Money comes to you through action. You earn best when you can go after something directly: pitching yourself, taking on work paid by results, starting a venture of your own with nothing but nerve. Waiting a year for a pay review feels like a slow insult, and a raise that never comes is reason enough for you to move on. Spending moves just as fast, and whatever catches your eye tends to be bought within minutes of wanting it. Your self-worth climbs with every bold move that pays off, and it sags when income ticks over without any effort from you. Lean spells rarely frighten you, because you trust yourself to go out and win it back. The savings that survive are the ones kept just out of your own impulsive reach.",
    "taurus": "Security is something you build brick by brick, and you feel it in your body when the account is healthy. You earn steadily rather than spectacularly, and you like income that arrives on the same date every month. Quality matters more than quantity, and you would rather own a few lasting things you love than many you will soon replace. Friends notice that you rarely panic about money, and that you somehow always have a little set aside. Possessions carry meaning for you, and parting with a well loved object can feel like losing part of yourself. The difficulty is a stubborn attachment to what you already have, which can keep you in a secure but underpaid role for years. Your worth grows slowly and roots deeply, much like your savings.",
    "gemini": "Two or three streams of income suit you far better than one. You earn through words, ideas, contacts and quick thinking. Money moves through your hands quickly, spent on whatever feeds your curiosity, and small costs slip past you unnoticed. You can talk your way into a better rate and you enjoy the bargaining itself. Your sense of worth is tied to feeling clever and useful, so a job that bores your mind feels poorly paid whatever the salary. Scattered finances are the hazard, with small leaks in many places quietly adding up. Variety keeps you earning, and a single clear overview keeps you solvent.",
    "cancer": "For you, money is about feeling safe and keeping your people fed. You earn well in work that nurtures or protects, and you often end up running the household budget without anyone asking. You like knowing there is a cushion tucked away somewhere, however small, because a reserve lets you breathe more easily. Spending goes on the home and on the people you care for, and making them comfortable feels like money well spent. Your self-worth rises and falls with mood, and a sense of being unappreciated at work can make even a good salary feel thin. Holding on too tightly out of fear is a familiar habit, as is lending to relatives you cannot refuse. Financial peace, for you, looks like plenty at home and a quiet mind.",
    "leo": "Earning is bound up with recognition for you, and you want to be paid for being yourself. Work where your talent is visible, whether performing, leading, creating or presenting, tends to bring the best money. You spend generously and with style, and you love giving in a way that makes people feel truly special. Looking less than your best bothers you more than you admit, because appearance and self-respect are tightly linked in your mind. Your confidence swells when your income reflects your worth and sinks hard when it does not. Pride can keep you spending to keep up an image during a lean month. Wealth, for you, grows from backing your own creative gifts and asking to be paid fairly for them.",
    "virgo": "Precision runs through your finances. You know roughly what is in your account at any moment, you notice when a regular cost creeps up by a few dollars, and you keep careful track of everything that goes out. Income comes most reliably through skill, service and doing a job properly, and colleagues often come to rely on your exactness. Spending is careful and practical: you research a purchase thoroughly and choose what works best rather than what looks prettiest. Self-worth is tied to being useful, which can make you undercharge and overdeliver for years. Worry is the hidden cost, since no amount of saving ever quite feels like enough. Your competence is worth more than you let yourself bill for.",
    "libra": "Money for you is closely tied to people and beauty. You earn well through partnership, negotiation, design, diplomacy or any work where charm and a sense of fairness count. Joint accounts, shared ventures and a partner's income often shape your finances more than you expected. Spending leans towards the lovely, and you would rather own one beautiful thing than several ordinary ones. You hate haggling in a crude way yet excel at finding the price that satisfies everyone. Indecision is costly, with a purchase put off for weeks or an investment postponed while you weigh both sides. Your self-worth grows when your taste is appreciated and your contribution to a shared effort is recognised.",
    "scorpio": "Money is serious business for you, and you rarely talk about it openly. You keep your finances private, sometimes even from a partner, and you prefer to hold the numbers close. Earning often comes through depth: research, investigation, therapy, finance, crisis work or anything others avoid. You understand leverage, debt and shared resources instinctively, and you notice who holds the purse strings in any room. Spending swings between strict control and sudden total commitment to something you want badly. There are likely to be times when you lose a great deal and rebuild from almost nothing, and each rebuild leaves you stronger. Self-worth is intensely tied to never being at anyone's mercy, which gives you remarkable financial resilience.",
    "sagittarius": "Optimism shapes your whole relationship with money. You trust that something will turn up, and remarkably often it does, through luck, good timing or a connection you never expected. Income comes well through teaching, travel, publishing, law, sales or anything with a sense of adventure and meaning. You spend on experiences far more than things, saying yes before checking the balance and paying for whatever promises to change your outlook. A tight budget feels like a cage, and you can be casual about bills until they become urgent. Your self-worth is bound up with freedom and growth, never only with how much is in the bank. Generosity flows easily from you, sometimes faster than the money itself.",
    "capricorn": "You take money seriously from an early age. You learned the value of money early, often through responsibility that arrived before its time or through seeing how hard it was to come by. Income grows slowly and steadily through hard work, qualifications and patient climbing, and you are rarely a lottery winner type. Spending is measured: you buy once and buy well, and you feel a quiet pleasure watching your savings creep upwards. Status matters, and the things you own often signal competence and seriousness. Frugality can harden into anxiety, with you refusing a small treat long after you can easily afford it. Your self-worth is tied to what you have achieved on your own, and later life often brings the most solid rewards.",
    "aquarius": "Conventional ideas about money leave you cold. You earn through technology, networks, innovation or unusual work that barely existed when you were at school, and your career path looks odd on paper. Income can arrive in unpredictable bursts, a windfall one quarter and nothing the next. You are usually among the first to try a new financial idea, long before it becomes ordinary for everyone else. Spending goes on technology, causes, friends and freedom, rarely on status symbols you find faintly ridiculous. Detachment helps you stay calm in a crisis, yet can make you vague about practical details like tax deadlines. Your worth grows when your originality pays, and you value independence far above a large but stifling salary.",
    "pisces": "Money slips through your fingers in a way that can puzzle even you. You give generously, lend without keeping a record and pay for others without a second thought. Earning comes well through creative, caring, healing or spiritual work, and you often do your best work for love rather than the invoice. Bank statements can feel like something to avoid, and money matters left unexamined have a way of surprising you later. You spend on beauty, music, escape and anything that soothes the mood. Clear boundaries are hard, and people with a sad story can drain your resources. Your self-worth is tied to compassion and imagination, and when you trust that your gifts deserve payment, money flows back in unexpected ways."
  },
  "home:house4": {
    "aries": "The house you grew up in rarely sat still. There were raised voices, heated moments, or a parent who expected you to stand on your own feet long before other children did. You were probably the child who learned early to fight your own battles. As an adult you want a place you can shape with your own hands, and you start making a new space yours almost as soon as you arrive. Domestic life with you is lively and a little combustible: a small irritation can start a row that is forgotten within the hour. Restlessness can push you to move more often than your friends do. A front door that is entirely yours, with no one telling you how to live behind it, is where you recharge.",
    "taurus": "Your roots go down deep, and you want a home that stays put. Memory for you is sensory: smells, textures and tastes carry you straight back to where you came from. A settled childhood gave you your first sense of safety, or its absence left you hungry for one. You nest with pleasure, investing in comfort, abundance and a corner of home that is entirely yours. Moving house unsettles you more than almost any other change, and you would rather improve where you are than start again elsewhere. Family habits can harden into rules nobody questions, and you hold on to familiar things long after they have worn thin. Having a place of your own and tending it brings a contentment little else matches.",
    "gemini": "Talk filled your early home. Your early home hummed with voices, comings and goings, and you learned young that change, movement and new faces were simply part of growing up. You learned to adapt quickly and make friends on any street. As an adult you fill your home with ideas, conversation and a constant low hum of activity, and life happens wherever people gather. A change of scene, even a small one at home, is your idea of a fresh start. Family bonds can feel chatty yet oddly light, with plenty said and less shared. Silence and isolation sound romantic only until they arrive, because home works for you as a lively crossroads rather than a fortress.",
    "cancer": "Everything in your life circles back to home and family. Childhood lives on in you with unusual vividness: the sounds, smells and small rituals of your early home stay with you for life. You are often the one who keeps the family connected, remembering what matters and gathering everyone together whether or not anyone asked. The home you make is soft, well fed and full of memories, a place where visitors relax within minutes. Old family hurts can surface without warning, and a single remark from a parent can undo you for days. Letting go of the past, or of grown children, comes slowly. Beneath all the caretaking lies a need to be mothered in return.",
    "leo": "A big personality stood at the heart of your childhood home: perhaps a proud, warm or theatrical parent whose approval felt like sunshine, or someone so bright that you grew up slightly in their shadow. You may have been the child performing for the family, waiting for applause. The home you create now has presence, warmth and a generosity that makes room for everyone you love. You love to host, and you glow when everyone is gathered under your roof. Pride can make you hide domestic trouble behind a cheerful face at the door. Family loyalty runs fierce in you, and a slight against one of yours lands as a slight against you. Your home is stage and sanctuary at once.",
    "virgo": "Order and usefulness shaped the house you grew up in, through a careful or anxious parent, worries about health or a firm sense that everyone pulled their weight. You learned early to notice what needed doing and do it without being asked. Your own home runs on systems, with a place for everything and a rhythm others find slightly intense. A small mess can keep you from sitting down until it is dealt with. Criticism absorbed in childhood can echo in your own inner voice whenever the house falls short. Care in your family shows up as practical acts far more than words. A clean, calm space lets your busy mind unclench.",
    "libra": "Keeping the peace was a skill you picked up at home, perhaps from a gracious, sociable parent, or from a family that kept a pleasant surface so that nobody had to face a row. You learned to read the atmosphere the moment you walked through the door. The home you make is beautiful and balanced, arranged with care so that it feels welcoming the moment anyone arrives. Sharing that home with a partner feels central to belonging, and living alone can feel strangely incomplete. Arguments under your own roof upset you badly, so you sometimes swallow a grievance to keep the evening nice. Fairness matters right down to who does which chore. A home that is lovely to look at and fair to live in lets you rest.",
    "scorpio": "Strong currents ran beneath the surface of your early home: a family secret, a loss that was never discussed, a powerful parent, or feelings that ran high but went unspoken. You sensed the undertow before anyone explained it, and you still read tension in a room instantly. Your own home is private and guarded, and few people are ever let very far into it. You want deep loyalty from family, and betrayal inside it can end a relationship for good. Old patterns repeat until you dig them up and look at them squarely. Leaving a home or closing a chapter of family life can feel like a complete death and rebirth. Home is your fortress and your place of renewal.",
    "sagittarius": "Your roots were never tied to a single place or a single view, and movement, mixed influences or strongly held beliefs coloured the home you grew up in. A parent was often adventurous, philosophical or away on some journey. The home you create has space and light, room for ideas and a welcome always ready for friends from far away. You may well end up living far from where you started, or keep part of yourself always ready to leave. Feeling hemmed in by family expectations or by four walls makes you restless and short tempered. Belonging for you comes from meaning more than bricks. Wherever a window opens onto a wide view, you feel at home.",
    "capricorn": "Responsibility came early in your family story, through a strict or distant parent, tight money, or being the sensible one who looked after younger siblings. Duty and rules often shaped the atmosphere more than open affection did. As an adult you build a solid base through steady effort, and owning property matters to you more than you usually admit. You are the one who keeps the practical side of home in order and plans for everyone's future. Warmth can be harder to show than practical care, and a chill from childhood can linger in your own household. Your home grows more comfortable and more loving with each decade. Later life often brings the secure base you always wanted.",
    "aquarius": "Something about your early home was unusual: an unconventional family set up, sudden change, a parent with radical ideas, or a lingering sense that you were the odd one out in your own family. Friends often felt more like family than relatives did. You create a home that follows your own logic, arranged to suit you rather than anyone else's idea of normal. Space and freedom within family ties are essential, and you bristle at being told how a household ought to be run. Emotional distance can make closeness tricky, and your living arrangements change abruptly more than once. Chosen family often becomes your truest one. Home is wherever you are free to be entirely yourself.",
    "pisces": "Your early home had a soft, dreamy or confusing quality, with a sensitive or artistic parent, an absent one, or boundaries that blurred in ways you only understood years later. You absorbed the feelings of the household like a sponge, often knowing a parent was sad before they did. The home you create is a refuge, soft and soothing, with somewhere quiet to disappear into. Lost souls and people in need find their way to your door. Idealising family can bring disappointment, and practical chaos creeps in while the bills sit unopened. Compassion lives in every room you inhabit. Home becomes a sanctuary where imagination and tenderness feel safe."
  },
  "love:house7": {
    "aries": "Partners with fire in them catch your eye. The one who argues back, who kisses you first, who dares you into something reckless: that is the person you remember, while agreeable types who defer to you on everything bore you within a week. In a committed relationship you want a teammate and a sparring partner in one, someone who keeps you sharp. Things move fast, and you might have moved in together or got engaged before friends had even met them. Rows are loud and frequent, yet usually forgiven almost as fast as they flare. Sharing the lead rather than battling for it becomes the work of a lasting bond. Courage is the quality you seek in a partner, and the one partnership asks of you.",
    "taurus": "Steadiness is what you look for in someone to share a life with. You are drawn to a calm, sensual, dependable person, the one who does what they said they would and shows care in practical ways. Flashy charm makes you suspicious; loyalty, physical warmth and a good meal win you over. Commitment builds slowly for you, often out of a long friendship or an unhurried courtship, and once you settle you intend it to last decades. A shared home, joint savings and comforting rituals you keep together form the spine of the relationship. Possessiveness and resistance to change can creep in unnoticed. Loyal to the bone yourself, you expect nothing less, and the right partner feels like solid ground underfoot.",
    "gemini": "Conversation is where attraction begins for you. The partner who makes you laugh, shares every interesting thing they find and happily argues with you for hours is the one who wins you. You want someone curious, quick and a little restless, who never lets the relationship go stale. Shared interests and endless talk keep a committed bond alive far more than grand gestures do. More than one serious relationship across a lifetime is common for you, or a partner who seems like two different people depending on the day. Mixed signals, and hiding deep feelings behind a clever remark, are the hazards. Your best partnerships feel like the longest and most enjoyable conversation of your life.",
    "cancer": "Emotional safety is the thing you seek most in a partner. You are drawn to someone protective and family minded, the person who notices you had a hard week and takes care of you without being asked. Partnership often feels like coming home, and you might even choose someone with an echo of a parent in them. In commitment you give tender care and loyalty, and you need that tenderness returned rather than simply received. Moods ripple through the relationship, and an old hurt can surface in the middle of an ordinary evening. Fear of losing someone can make you cling, or retreat into your shell. Your truest partnerships grow into a family of their own, a warm nest built by two people.",
    "leo": "People who shine draw you in: confidence, warmth and a certain star quality catch your eye, and you like being seen beside someone impressive. You want romance with a flourish: grand gestures, open declarations, the anniversary never forgotten. Committed partnership brings out your loyalty and generosity, and you give fiercely to someone who adores you. Jealousy and wounded pride flare when you feel overlooked, even for an evening. Two strong personalities can end up competing for the spotlight, even in private. Your happiest relationships are playful, proud and openly affectionate, with each person cheering the other on. Both of you need to be the hero sometimes.",
    "virgo": "Competence and quiet kindness attract you in a partner. You notice the person who helps without being asked, who looks after you when you are worn out, who remembers your small preferences. Flashy romance matters less than daily reliability, and you show love through service, feeling most cherished by a partner who does the same small practical things. Your standards run high, and criticism can slip into the relationship through a passing remark about how something was done. Choosing someone who needs fixing is a familiar trap. Healthy routines, honest talk and shared daily rhythms hold your partnerships together. You thrive beside someone who notices your care and returns it.",
    "libra": "Partnership feels natural to you, and you often understand yourself best through another person. You are drawn to someone graceful, fair minded and attractive, a person who turns an ordinary evening into something elegant. Good manners, harmony and shared taste matter enormously; you notice how a date treats everyone around them. In commitment you seek equality, and you work hard to keep the atmosphere pleasant. Avoiding conflict can let resentments pile up until one small thing tips the scales. Feeling whole outside a relationship can be a struggle, and you may have gone from one partnership straight into the next. Mutual respect is what makes your partnerships last, a true meeting of equals.",
    "scorpio": "Intensity is what pulls you towards a partner. Magnetic, private, emotionally deep people draw you in, and you would rather have one love that shakes you than several pleasant ones. Trust takes a long time to win, but once given it binds you completely. In commitment you want absolute honesty, and you sense instantly when something is being hidden, down to the smallest change in tone. Jealousy and power struggles surface whenever trust wobbles. Relationships transform you, and a breakup can feel like a death followed by a slow rebirth. A bond that lasts is one where both of you are fully seen, darker corners included, and still choose each other.",
    "sagittarius": "Freedom and adventure attract you in a partner. You are drawn to someone optimistic, worldly and funny, the person who suggests something spontaneous or opens your mind to a new way of seeing. Partners from other cultures or countries cross your path more often than chance would suggest. Commitment needs room to grow, a shared sense of meaning and honesty, even when it arrives blunt. Feeling trapped or bored makes you restless, and the idea of forever can feel daunting at first. The partnerships that last feel like an ongoing journey, full of learning and laughter. Two explorers with a shared map suit you far better than a quiet harbour.",
    "capricorn": "Maturity and reliability attract you in a partner. You are drawn to someone responsible, ambitious and grounded, often older or more established than you. Knowing where things are heading matters more than flirtation, and you have probably assessed a date's prospects before the evening was over. You take vows seriously and build something solid over years: shared security, a long plan, a life built together. Emotional warmth can be slow to show, and the relationship might sometimes feel more like a well run company. Marriage often comes later in life and improves with age, held steady by shared goals and respect for each other's work. Commitment is a long investment that pays out richly in later years.",
    "aquarius": "Originality draws you to a partner. You are attracted to someone independent, unconventional and intellectually alive, someone who was a friend before anything else. Traditional relationship scripts, the ring by a certain age and the joint everything, can feel stifling. In commitment you need plenty of space, shared ideals and firm respect for each other's freedom; separate hobbies and even separate bedrooms do not alarm you. Emotional detachment can make intimacy harder than you expected. Sudden changes or unusual arrangements are common in your love life, and friends are sometimes surprised by who you choose. Friendship and freedom sit at the heart of every partnership that lasts.",
    "pisces": "Compassion and romance pull you towards a partner. You are drawn to someone sensitive, artistic or spiritual, and you can fall headlong in love with who a person could become. Commitment feels like a soul connection, and you give selflessly, reading a partner's mood before they have said a word. Idealisation brings disappointment when daily life arrives with its laundry and bills. You might attract people who need rescuing, and boundaries blur until it is hard to see where you end and they begin. Seeing a partner clearly, flaws and all, is the quiet task of your love life. The partnerships that last rest on tenderness, shared dreams and forgiveness flowing both ways."
  },
  "career:house10": {
    "aries": "Your calling asks for a front line. You are built for work where you lead, launch or compete, and people see you as the one who gets things moving while everyone else is still in the meeting. Entrepreneurship, emergency work, sport, surgery, sales or any start up role can suit you, because the reward comes from being first. Your reputation grows fastest right after you take a risk others avoided. Bosses who move slowly or micromanage bring out your temper, and you may have walked out on one in a blaze of frustration. Impatience with the long middle stretch of a project can cost you. The career that fits gives you a mountain to charge and the freedom to charge it your way.",
    "taurus": "Your public life is built slowly and meant to last, and you are known as reliable, grounded and unflappable, the colleague trusted with what matters most and what takes years to finish. Careers in finance, property, food, design, craft, music or anything with tangible results and sensory pleasure suit you. You would rather climb steadily inside one solid organisation than chase every shiny opening. Recognition comes through consistency, and your reputation rests on the quality of what you produce. Authority earns your respect when it is fair and practical, and your stubborn silence when it is not. Comfort can keep you in a role long after it has stopped stretching you. A career that pays well and feels secure lets your talents ripen slowly.",
    "gemini": "Words and ideas are your public currency. You are seen as quick, articulate and well informed, the person who can explain anything and seems to know someone in every department. Journalism, teaching, marketing, media, sales, writing or any role built on communication and connection suits you. More than one career over a lifetime is almost a given, and perhaps two running at once. Managers who stifle questions frustrate you, and you are usually the one pushing for a better way of doing things. Scattered focus is the risk, starting projects with a burst of enthusiasm and drifting when the novelty fades. Your reputation grows once your versatility is seen as range rather than restlessness.",
    "cancer": "Caring for others shapes your public role. You are seen as protective, intuitive and supportive, the one at work who remembers what matters to people and notices when someone new is struggling in silence. Careers in care, education, hospitality, property, family business or anything that nurtures suit you well. A workplace that feels like a family brings out your best, and your fierce loyalty to a team means your reputation grows through emotional intelligence as much as skill. Authority can feel personal, with a harsh boss stirring up old feelings about a parent. Sensitivity to criticism can make your working life rise and fall like a tide. Work that lets you look after people, or build something lasting for your own family, fits best.",
    "leo": "You are made for visibility: your calling involves leadership, creativity or performance, and people remember you long after you leave the room. Careers in the arts, entertainment, management, teaching or any field where you can take centre stage suit you. Recognition matters deeply, and you work hardest when your contribution is seen and applauded. As a boss you tend to be warm and generous, the kind who celebrates the team and champions the quiet junior. Pride can clash with authority, sharpest when a superior takes credit for your idea. Being passed over for a promotion wounds you more than you let on. Roles that let you lead, create and be proudly yourself in public bring out a warmth nobody forgets.",
    "virgo": "Your reputation rests on skill and precision. You are known as the person who does the job properly, catches the mistake nobody else noticed and keeps the whole operation running. Careers in health, research, editing, accounting, analysis, craft or any service requiring expertise suit you. Recognition often comes slowly, earned through dependable competence rather than self promotion. You respect authority that is organised and fair, and every inefficiency in a disorganised boss irritates you like a stone in a shoe. Perfectionism can slow you down, and you might sit silently while someone louder takes the credit for your careful work. The career that fits lets you be useful, improve systems and master a craft until it becomes your signature.",
    "libra": "Diplomacy is the thread running through your public life. You are seen as charming, fair and easy to work with, the person who smooths over tension and wins the difficult client round with sheer charm. Careers in law, design, fashion, the arts, mediation, human resources or partnership based business suit you. Collaboration brings out your best work, and your career often advances through a handful of key relationships. You prefer authority that is reasonable and polite, and a shouting boss can unsettle you for days. Indecision can stall your progress, as can putting other people's approval above your own ambition. Work that combines beauty, fairness and teamwork, and lets your taste become part of the job, suits you best.",
    "scorpio": "Your calling runs deep. You are drawn to work involving power, research, investigation, healing or transformation, and colleagues see you as intense, capable and slightly unreadable. Careers in psychology, finance, medicine, detective work, crisis management or anything that uncovers what others hide suit you. You come into your own under pressure, and you are strongest on the day everything has fallen apart. Your reputation can go through dramatic changes, including a complete reinvention of your career at least once. Power struggles with authority are common, and you rarely forget a betrayal at work. You belong wherever you can dig beneath the surface and change something for good.",
    "sagittarius": "Meaning is what drives your career. You are drawn to work that widens horizons, whether teaching, publishing, travel, law, philosophy or anything international. People see you as optimistic, knowledgeable and inspiring, the colleague who reminds everyone why the project matters. A job that feels pointless or confining drains your enthusiasm within months, and the urge to walk away simply to feel free again runs strong in you. Narrow minded bosses frustrate you, and your honesty with authority can come out a little too bluntly. Overpromising and restlessness can scatter your efforts across too many plans. Your reputation grows as a teacher and guide, and the right path lets you keep learning and pass on what you find.",
    "capricorn": "Ambition is written into your public life. You were probably seen as serious and responsible from a young age, the person trusted with authority long before your peers. Careers in management, government, law, finance, engineering or any structured field with a clear ladder suit you. Success usually comes through patient effort, and your career often peaks later in life, with the best titles arriving in your forties and fifties. You respect authority and eventually become it. Working late into the evening feels normal to you, and fear of failure can cost you time with the people you love. The career that fits rewards discipline and lets you build something that outlasts you.",
    "aquarius": "Originality marks your public role. You are seen as innovative, independent and a little unusual, the person in the meeting with the idea nobody else would have dared suggest. Careers in technology, science, social causes, activism, invention or anything future focused suit you. Your path is rarely conventional, with sudden changes of direction that make your CV an interesting read. Authority grates when its rules make no sense, and you are likely to question them out loud. Office politics bores you, and your detachment can be mistaken for aloofness, so freelance or remote work often suits you better than a nine to five. Freedom, a sense of purpose and a chance to change the system from within are what keep you engaged.",
    "pisces": "Compassion and imagination shape your calling. You are drawn to work in the arts, healing, spirituality, charity, music, film or anything that serves others or touches the soul. People see you as gentle, intuitive and creative, though your public image can be hard to pin down. Your career path is rarely straight, and you might drift through several jobs before finding the work that feels like a vocation. Rigid hierarchies and cold managers disappoint you, and boundaries at work blur easily, so you can end up absorbing everyone's stress along with your own. Recognition often arrives for work you did because it moved you. Dreaming, creating and helping others all at once is when work stops feeling like work."
  },
};
// where each house ruler sits, read through the page
window.AstroDeep.areaRulers = {
  "love:house5": {
    "1": "Romance lives in your own body and manner, so people pick up on your capacity for fun before you say a word. You flirt by being yourself, with a warmth and laughter that turn heads and a way of lighting up when a conversation catches. Dating changes who you are, and each great crush leaves its mark on the way you see and present yourself. You are usually the one who makes the first move, and you enjoy being the lead in your own love story. The trap is treating a lover as an audience, someone whose delight mirrors you back. Love grows richest when the spotlight is shared and you let the other person surprise you.",
    "2": "Pleasure and security are tied together for you, and romance has to feel solid before it feels thrilling. You show interest through tangible things, choosing gifts and gestures with care and remembering exactly what someone admired. Dating is a sensory affair, slow, lingering and full of physical pleasure. Being desired lifts your sense of your own worth, so a warm romance makes you feel richer in every sense. Spending on love comes easily, sometimes more easily than it should. The quieter danger is measuring affection in gifts and effort, keeping an unspoken ledger of who gave what. You are loved best by someone who values the same simple, lasting comforts.",
    "3": "Flirting, for you, is a conversation that never quite ends. Crushes start in conversation, in the places you pass through every day or through someone who insists there is a person you simply have to meet. You fall for wit, and a clever reply can do more for you than any grand romantic gesture. Dating has a light, curious quality, full of movement, novelty and endless chatter. Keeping several light flirtations going at once feels harmless and natural to you. The weakness is that talk can replace feeling, and a romance stays charming but never lands. When someone matches your mind and still reaches your heart, you settle gladly.",
    "4": "Romance wants a home to live in. Your best dates feel homely and private, unhurried and tucked away from the rest of the world. Family shapes your love life more than you admit, and a parent's approval or an old attachment can linger in your choices. You fall hard for people who make you feel safe, and you start imagining a shared home surprisingly early. Pleasure for you is domestic and deep rather than flashy. The pull is to move a romance indoors so quickly that the playful stage is skipped altogether. When you let courtship breathe a little, the nest you build together is warmer for it.",
    "5": "Here the ruler sits at home, so romance is a concentrated force in your life. You know how to be delighted, and you treat falling in love as an art form: the build of anticipation, the perfect first kiss, the small rituals of a new affair. Creativity, play and love all feed each other, and you often meet lovers through the things you most enjoy doing. Children, of the body or of the imagination, carry the same joy. You rarely need anyone else's permission to have fun. What catches you out is chasing the high of a fresh crush and losing interest when ordinary life begins. Joy that survives ordinary days is the kind that belongs to you.",
    "6": "Love finds you in the daily round. You meet people through work and the familiar rhythms of your day, and romance grows out of routine rather than grand gestures. Your way of flirting is useful: helping out, looking after someone when they are unwell, remembering exactly how they like things. Dating fits into a busy life, and a relaxed evening together can mean more to you than any lavish occasion. You show love through care and attention to detail. The flat side is turning pleasure into another task, analysing a date instead of enjoying it. Romance flourishes when you let yourself be looked after in return.",
    "7": "Flirtation turns towards commitment almost at once. You rarely date casually for long, because every promising romance starts to feel like a possible partnership, and you notice yourself imagining the two of you as a unit by the third meeting. Friends set you up, introductions work well, and some of your most exciting romances start as collaborations. You are at your most playful in company with one special person. Pleasure means sharing, and a beautiful moment seen alone barely counts. You can rush past the light, silly stage of courtship because you are so eager for the lasting thing. A partnership that keeps its sense of romance, with dates and surprises long after the commitment is made, suits you perfectly.",
    "8": "Romance runs deep and dark for you, and light flirtation rarely holds your interest. You fall hard, with a physical intensity that can feel almost overwhelming, and a crush becomes an obsession that fills every quiet moment. Secrecy thrills you: the hidden glance, the affair nobody knows about yet, the late-night confession. Love changes you each time, and you come out of a big romance altered in some basic way. Sexual chemistry matters more than you let on. Jealousy and all-or-nothing tests are the price of this intensity. The romances worth having are the ones where both of you can survive being seen completely.",
    "9": "Adventure and romance are tangled together. You are drawn to people who open a door onto another world, whose ideas, background or way of life show you something you never knew. Some of your happiest memories are of love that felt like an adventure, far from everything familiar. Dating feels best when it involves learning something, and a lover who widens your view of life holds you longest. You fall for minds and horizons as much as faces. The trap is idealising what is far away and losing interest once the lover becomes familiar. Travel together, literal or in thought, is what keeps the spark alive for you.",
    "10": "Your love life has a public face. Romance often arrives through work or among people connected to your ambitions, and you are attracted to confidence, talent and a bit of status. Friends and colleagues tend to know who you are seeing, and a romance can shape your reputation for better or worse. Creative success and romantic happiness rise and fall together for you. You like a lover you are proud to be seen with. The danger lies in choosing someone because they look right on paper, or in letting career eat every evening. You are happiest when pleasure holds a place in your life as firm as any goal.",
    "11": "Friendship is the gateway to romance for you. Your crushes grow among friends of friends and in shared circles, often after a long stretch of easy conversation. You love a lover who is also a mate, someone you can laugh with in company and argue ideas with in private. Freedom matters, and a romance that tries to cage you loses its charm fast. The difficulty is getting stuck in the friend zone, too cool to admit how much you feel. When you let a friendship become openly romantic, the bond you build is unusually easy and honest.",
    "12": "Romance has a secret, dreamy quality for you. Some of your deepest crushes were never spoken aloud, and you can carry a flame for years for someone who barely knows you exist. Fantasy is part of your pleasure, and a whole relationship can unfold in your imagination before anything real happens. You fall for artists, wounded souls and people who are hard to reach. Compassion runs through your love, and you forgive a great deal. The danger is choosing the unavailable, the married or the far away, because a love that stays hidden cannot disappoint. Tenderness comes when you let the dream step into daylight."
  },
  "love:house7": {
    "1": "Partnership is written into your sense of who you are. You attract people who resemble you in striking ways, and friends sometimes joke that you and your partner look alike or finish each other's sentences. You often make the first move in love, taking the lead rather than waiting to be chosen. Relationships change you visibly, and you come out of each long one as a slightly different person. You bring the full force of your personality to a couple. The balancing act is between self and other: sometimes you lose yourself in a partner, sometimes you treat them as an extension of your own plans. Love works when two strong selves stand side by side.",
    "2": "Your partner is bound up with your sense of security and worth. You choose people who feel steady, often someone with practical sense or earning power, and you build a life together through shared resources and the slow gathering of good things. Love, for you, is shown in what is given and kept. A good partner raises your confidence and your standard of living alike. Money can become a quiet battleground: who pays, who saves, who spends on what. Possessiveness grows when you feel insecure. The best relationships you have are ones where values match as closely as tastes, so that building something together feels natural.",
    "3": "Conversation is the foundation of your partnerships. You often meet a partner close to your everyday life, through people you already know or through conversation you soon find yourself looking forward to. Your relationship feels like a long, lively chat, full of in-jokes, shared news and friendly debate. You choose people who are curious and quick. A partner who is also a best friend suits you well. The weakness is that talking can replace deeper feeling, and difficult emotions are discussed rather than felt. When words carry tenderness, your bond is one of the most companionable around.",
    "4": "Partnership, for you, is about building a home. You choose someone who feels like family, and often the relationship starts with a sense of homecoming, as if you had known them for years. Your partner can remind you of a parent in ways that are either comforting or complicated. Much of your love life takes place at home, in the spaces you create and care for together. Family members have strong opinions about who you marry. Repeating your parents' patterns without noticing is the pitfall. At its richest, your partnership becomes the root system for a whole life, a place both of you return to.",
    "5": "You want a partner who is also your playmate. Romance stays at the centre of your committed relationships, and you expect dates, surprises and laughter long after the honeymoon. You are drawn to charismatic, creative people who make life feel like a celebration, and you enjoy being admired by the person you chose. Children often arrive as a joyful expression of the bond. The difficulty is that everyday life cannot always sparkle, and you can mistake quiet stretches for the end of love. A partner who keeps playing with you through the dull patches is the one you keep.",
    "6": "Partnership shows itself in daily care. You often meet a partner through work or routine, and the relationship grows out of shared tasks and practical support rather than dramatic declarations. You choose someone reliable, capable and useful to have around. Love, for you, looks like the person who quietly takes care of what you forgot and keeps daily life running without being asked. You work well together as a team. The shadow here is caretaking that becomes one-sided, or a habit of criticism that wears the romance thin. When service flows both ways, your partnership has a humble, durable strength that outlasts grander romances.",
    "7": "With the ruler in its own house, partnership is a central theme of your life. You know what you want in a partner and you tend to recognise it quickly, often committing with unusual clarity. Relationships are the arena where you learn most about yourself, and you pour energy into making them work. Coupledom can swallow your identity if you let it. Your deepest partnerships happen when both of you remain complete people who choose each other daily.",
    "8": "Your partnerships run deep. You choose someone with whom you merge completely, sharing money, secrets, bodies and fears, and a casual relationship never satisfies you for long. The people you are drawn to often have hidden depths or a past that marks them. Partnership transforms you: you are never quite the same person after a major relationship. Joint finances, inheritance and shared property matter in your committed life. Power struggles and jealousy can creep in when trust is shaken. The relationships that serve you best allow full honesty, so that intimacy becomes a source of strength rather than a battlefield.",
    "9": "Your partner opens the world for you. You often meet someone from a different country, culture or faith, or on a trip, at university, or in a class that changed your thinking. You choose people with big ideas, a sense of humour about life and a restless streak. A partnership, for you, is a shared adventure: exploring together, arguing happily about philosophy and always looking towards the next horizon. You grow through the person you love. Ordinary days can make you restless once the relationship settles. Learning side by side turns the long haul into an expedition you both enjoy.",
    "10": "Partnership is tied to your public life and ambitions. You often meet a partner through work or career circles, and you are drawn to someone with status, drive or a respected position. Your relationships are visible, and marriage can affect your reputation, open professional doors or shape how others see you. A partner is often your ally in the climb. You take commitment seriously and want a relationship you can be proud of. The danger is choosing a partner for what they represent rather than who they are. The partnerships that last are the ones where private affection runs as strong as public respect.",
    "11": "Your best partners start as friends. You often meet through groups, communities, shared causes or friends of friends, and the relationship grows out of companionship. You want equality above all: a partner who respects your independence and has a life of their own. Unconventional arrangements suit you, and you are happy for your relationship to look nothing like the ones you grew up around. Shared ideals hold you together. The difficulty is a certain emotional distance, a tendency to keep the heart at arm's length. When friendship deepens into intimacy, your partnership is refreshingly free and honest.",
    "12": "Partnership has a hidden, spiritual quality for you. Some of your relationships begin in secret, or with someone who needs rescuing, or in circumstances you would rather not explain. You are drawn to sensitive, artistic or wounded people, and you give generously, often sacrificing your own needs for theirs. A partner can feel like a soulmate from another life. You can idealise someone and miss clear warning signs, or stay in a relationship out of pity or guilt. Blind spots are common here. The partnerships that heal you are built on honesty and compassion, where both of you are seen plainly and loved anyway."
  },
  "love:house8": {
    "1": "Intimacy shows in you whether you like it or not. People sense a magnetic intensity in your presence, a steadiness in your gaze that makes them either lean in or feel slightly unnerved. Desire lives close to the surface of your body, and a lover can read your interest in the set of your shoulders before you have decided anything. Trust is personal for you, so a betrayal lands as an attack on who you are, not just on the relationship. Nothing about your closeness is half-hearted. Guardedness can read as coldness, and your need to stay in control sometimes pushes away the very person you want. Letting someone see the depth behind your eyes gives you the powerful, lasting bond you secretly want.",
    "2": "Closeness grows slowly for you and needs solid ground under it. Trust is built through touch, consistency and the plain proof that someone turns up when they said they would. You are richly sensual, and warmth, touch and unhurried time together matter more to you than any clever technique. Money and intimacy get tangled in your life, and a partner's spending, debts or generosity changes how close you feel to them. Possessiveness surfaces when you fear losing what you treasure, and you can cling to a lover the way you cling to savings. Your body knows when it is safe long before your mind agrees. Once that safety is earned, you are loyal, generous and physically devoted for years.",
    "3": "Words open the door to your deepest intimacy. Words that say what nobody else has dared to say reach you more than any gift ever could, and you remember every revealing sentence a lover has spoken. You need to name a feeling before you can fully feel it, so you talk your way into trust. Secrets are traded in conversation, which makes you a wonderful confidant. The weak spot is that describing intimacy can stand in for living it, and private matters sometimes slip into a chat with a friend. Closeness arrives once your words and your body say the same thing.",
    "4": "Intimacy needs home ground. You open up fully only where you feel safe, in private and familiar surroundings, with someone who has started to feel like family. The way your family handled secrets and affection shaped how you learned to trust, and old patterns about closeness surface in your adult bedroom whether you invite them or not. Privacy matters enormously, and the slightest sense of being overheard or intruded upon can shut you down for days. Letting a lover in is a slow homecoming rather than a sudden leap. Childhood hurts tend to rise in the most vulnerable moments. With a partner who makes you feel at home, your tenderness is profound and nurturing.",
    "5": "Intimacy and play are intertwined for you. You love closeness that is fun, creative and a little theatrical, and a lover who can laugh with you in bed wins your trust faster than any solemn declaration. Intense romances light you up, and you throw yourself into passion with your whole heart, full of playfulness, flair and generous gestures. Pleasure is serious business to you, though you keep it joyful. The flip side is drama: affairs that burn hot and fast, jealousy that turns into a scene, or mistaking a thrill for depth. A bond that keeps both its spark and its depth gives you the richest intimacy you can imagine.",
    "6": "Intimacy lives in small daily rituals. Small acts of care, a comforting touch after a hard day, a partner who reads your mood without being told: these build trust more than any dramatic confession. You are attentive to bodies, your own and your lover's, noticing tension, tiredness and small changes others would miss. Closeness becomes part of a healthy rhythm, reliable and sustaining rather than wild. Nerves can creep in, though, and you sometimes turn sex into another task to perform well or worry over afterwards. Health and stress show up quickly in your desire. Once you stop trying to get it right, your care makes you an unusually thoughtful lover.",
    "7": "Deep intimacy arrives through committed partnership. You rarely open up fully outside a serious relationship, and the person you commit to becomes the one who knows your bank balance, your fears and your most vulnerable self. Partners often bring intensity, depth or shared resources into your life, and a marriage can change your finances as much as your heart. Trust is built through the long commitment itself, through staying when things get hard. Struggles over control, money or loyalty can surface precisely because the stakes feel so high. A solid bond with one person becomes one of the deepest mergers you will know, and both of you grow inside it.",
    "8": "Here the ruler sits in its own house, and intimacy becomes a concentrated, serious theme. You know depth, and anything shallow leaves you cold within minutes. Trust is earned slowly and given totally, so a lover who breaks it rarely gets a second chance. Privacy is sacred: your sex life is nobody's business, and you notice instantly when someone probes too far. You have been changed by closeness more than once, and you understand the power of vulnerability better than most people you meet. All-or-nothing thinking and a watchfulness for betrayal can keep you on permanent guard. Your healing comes from the kind of intimacy where both people surrender without losing themselves.",
    "9": "Intimacy, for you, is a journey of discovery. You are curious about desire, spirituality and what closeness means in other cultures, and ideas about the sacred side of intimacy hold your attention completely. Lovers from different cultures or backgrounds fascinate you, and they tend to leave the deepest impression on you. Trust grows fastest with someone who shares your philosophy of life. You are more open-minded in private than you appear in public. Intellectualising can creep in, so that you discuss intimacy brilliantly and feel it less, or chase novelty to avoid depth. Exploration paired with tenderness turns your intimate life into a source of meaning.",
    "10": "Your private life and your public standing touch each other. Discretion matters a great deal: you choose carefully who knows what, and you would be mortified to hear your love life discussed at work. You are often drawn to people with power, authority or a serious reputation, and a little imbalance in status can sharpen desire. Intimate choices affect how the world sees you, for good or ill, and you know it. Trust is something you expect to be earned through conduct over time, like a promotion. A need to stay in charge can follow you into the bedroom. Allowing yourself to be vulnerable turns closeness into a strength that steadies your whole public life.",
    "11": "Intimacy grows out of friendship for you. You open up most to people you already trust as friends, and some of your deepest bonds began as years of easy companionship before anything physical happened. Frank conversation about desire comes easily, and you are comfortable with arrangements that would unsettle more conventional people. Trust, for you, rests on honesty and a mutual respect for freedom. Your circle of friends knows a surprising amount about your love life, and group settings shape who you end up close to. Emotional distance is your weak point, keeping lovers at a cool arm's length or treating intimacy as an idea. Friendship and passion merged fully give you something honest and liberating.",
    "12": "Intimacy has a private, almost sacred quality for you. You long for a union where boundaries dissolve and two people feel like one, and ordinary sex without that feeling can leave you strangely lonely. Secret longings, hidden crushes and vivid fantasies live inside you, sometimes for years. Being seen frightens you as much as it attracts you. Some of your most intense connections were never spoken of openly, and a few remain known only to you. Secrecy and escapism are the pitfalls, along with giving yourself to someone who is unavailable or not quite real. A partner who meets you with compassion makes closeness feel otherworldly and healing."
  },
  "money:house2": {
    "1": "Your income comes from you: your personality, your hands, your name, the way you walk into a room. You earn most when you are directly in charge, freelancing, running your own show or being the recognisable face behind the product. Clients book you because they want you specifically, not a firm. Self-worth and earning power are tightly knotted, and in weeks when you feel confident the invoices seem to pay themselves. You trust your instincts about money and act on them faster than most. The weak point is that income depends on your energy, so a tired month or an illness means a thin month. Building something that earns without you is the wisest move you can make.",
    "2": "With the ruler in its own house, money is a self-contained, steady theme. You know how to earn, save and grow your resources with little fuss, and you are the friend who always seems to have something put aside. Income comes straight from your own talents and possessions, and you have a clear, unsentimental sense of what your time is worth. You enjoy gathering good things slowly, from savings that grow to possessions built to last. Security matters deeply, and you build it brick by brick. Holding on too tightly is the pitfall, along with judging your worth only by what you own. Turning plain skill into lasting security is your gift.",
    "3": "Words, ideas and connections are your livelihood. Writing, teaching, sales, marketing, media, driving, local trade or anything that involves talking to people pays you well, and you can sell almost anything you believe in. Siblings, neighbours or your local area frequently play a part in how you earn, whether through a lead or a shared venture. You learn fast and adapt to new opportunities quicker than colleagues. Scattering yourself across too many small projects is the temptation. One well-chosen skill, pursued seriously, can outearn a dozen side hustles.",
    "4": "Money is tied to home, family and roots. You earn from property, a family business, working from home, or anything connected to food, care, housing or domestic life. Family shapes your finances in obvious and hidden ways: an inheritance, a loan from a parent, a sense that you must earn to look after everyone. The roof over your head is the main reason you work, and every pay rise becomes a better home. Bricks and mortar often prove your most reliable investment. Financial entanglement with relatives can become heavy around shared houses and wills. Owning your own foundations gives you both income and a deep sense of peace.",
    "5": "Creativity, pleasure and self-expression are where your money grows. Entertainment, the arts, design, working with children, sport, hospitality or anything that makes people happy can pay your bills. You earn best when you are enjoying yourself, and a hobby you started for fun has a habit of turning into paid work. Speculation appeals to you: backing a hunch, investing in a friend's venture, starting something new on impulse. You have a flair for making money out of play. Gambling, overspending on treats or chasing a thrill over a steady wage are the traps. Creativity paired with a little discipline turns your talents into wealth.",
    "6": "Earning, for you, rests on daily work, service and honed skill. You earn through steady employment, a craft you have practised for years, or work in health, care, administration, trades or anything that keeps other people's lives running. Colleagues rely on you, and you are the one who knows where every file lives. Competence is your financial strength, and you take quiet pride in a job done properly. Security grows through routine, month by month, payslip by payslip. Undervaluing yourself is the hazard: accepting less than you deserve, covering extra shifts, working through lunch for years. Asking plainly for what your skill is worth changes your finances more than any lucky break.",
    "7": "Other people are your route to money: partners, clients, the person across the negotiating table. Consulting, contracts, collaborations, agency work or a spouse's earnings often play a central part in your finances. You earn best alongside someone, whether a business partner, a loyal client list or a husband or wife whose salary lets you take risks. Negotiation is a strength, and you have a feel for a fair deal and a reasonable fee. Financial dependency can creep in, and you sometimes undersell yourself to keep a relationship smooth. Clear contracts, agreed in writing, protect you more than goodwill. Balanced partnerships multiply your income and open doors you could never push open alone.",
    "8": "Your earning power runs through shared money: the resources, debts and assets that pass between people. Investments, inheritance, commissions, banking, insurance, tax, lending or managing shared resources often feature in how you earn. You understand money at a deep level: the hidden flows, the fine print, the power it gives whoever controls it. A windfall, a settlement or a partner's assets can change your circumstances overnight. You spot value where others see only risk, and you are calm in a financial crisis. Debt and tangled joint finances are the darker side, along with quiet struggles for control over the purse. Handled with integrity, shared resources can grow your wealth remarkably.",
    "9": "Far horizons fill your purse. Teaching, publishing, law, travel, universities, international trade or anything built on big ideas can pay you well. Foreign clients, a job abroad or work that crosses borders often boosts your finances more than anything at home. You earn most when your work means something and stretches your understanding, and a dull, well-paid job rarely lasts long. Optimism lets you take financial leaps others avoid, and they often pay off. Restless spending on flights and experiences can drain the account, and overconfidence in a bold venture is a hazard. Guided by wisdom, your wide vision becomes a source of wealth.",
    "10": "Career and public standing set the level of what you earn. Status, promotion, recognition and a respected role drive your earnings, and your salary tends to climb in visible steps with each new title. Ambition is a financial asset for you, and you are willing to put in the long hours. The catch is that self-worth and job title can fuse, so a restructure or a missed promotion shakes your sense of value far more than your bank balance. Building a career you believe in brings money and meaning in together.",
    "11": "Networks, groups and new ideas bring money your way. Technology, online work, subscriptions, community projects or clients passed on by friends and former colleagues can all pay your bills. Your social circle is a financial asset, and a friendly conversation has a way of turning into paid work. You earn best when your work serves some bigger purpose you care about. Collaborations bring surprising gains, sometimes from people you barely know. Relying too heavily on others, or losing money on an unconventional scheme a friend championed, are the pitfalls. A solid base of your own within the network keeps your hopes and income pulling the same way.",
    "12": "Behind the scenes is where money finds you. Work in hospitals, charities, prisons, retreats, research, the arts or any quiet solitary setting often suits you, and royalties or anonymous work pay better than you expect. You earn without seeking the spotlight, and colleagues are sometimes surprised to learn how much you do. Compassion and intuition guide your financial choices, occasionally better than any spreadsheet. Vagueness is the weak spot: not checking the statement, lending money you never see again, undervaluing your gifts. Clear boundaries and a trusted adviser protect you. Trusting your quiet talents lets income arrive in ways that feel almost magical."
  },
  "money:house8": {
    "1": "Shared money runs straight through your sense of self. How you handle debt, joint accounts and other people's resources becomes part of how people see you: you are the one who understands how credit works, or the one quietly carrying an obligation nobody else knows about. You enter financial partnerships personally, and a bad deal lands like an injury rather than a paperwork problem. An inheritance, a partner's income or an investor's backing can visibly change the way you present yourself. There is a strong pull towards control, keeping the numbers close to your chest even with the people you love. Used well, this gives you nerve around money that is not strictly yours, and you negotiate terms face to face without flinching.",
    "2": "Other people's money feeds directly into your own security. A partner's salary, a family loan, an inheritance or a return on shares tends to land in your personal account and change what you can afford, and you feel that difference in your body as much as in your balance. You are careful with joint funds, usually the one who insists on a savings pot or a written agreement before anything is pooled. Debt unsettles you more than it unsettles most people because it blurs what is yours. Holding on too tightly is the trap: refusing to merge finances, or clinging to an asset long after it has stopped earning its keep. Handled patiently, shared resources become the ground you build steady, lasting wealth on.",
    "3": "Joint finances move through conversation, paperwork and the people living nearby. You read the small print on a loan properly, compare every option at length, and end up explaining finances to people close to you who have been avoiding them for months. Brothers, sisters, cousins or neighbours can be tied into an inheritance, a joint venture or a debt, for better or worse. Writing, teaching, brokering or selling information can bring in commissions, royalties and fees drawn from other people's resources. Restlessness is the snag, with too many small accounts and side investments until you lose the thread of what is owed where. Kept in order, your quick mind turns financial complexity into something you understand and can explain.",
    "4": "Shared money and family are knotted together for you. Property, a family home, an inheritance from parents or grandparents, or a loan from relatives tends to play a large part in your finances, sometimes a larger part than you would choose. You can end up living in a house partly paid for by someone else, or carrying the emotional weight of a parent's debts long after they are settled on paper. Conversations about wills, care costs and who gets the house stir up old family roles within minutes. Money borrowed inside the family never feels neutral, and you remember every favour. Bricks and mortar suit you because you think of wealth as something that shelters people. Separate the feelings from the figures and family resources become a foundation rather than an obligation.",
    "5": "Pleasure, creativity and risk pull at the money you share with others. An investment gives you the same buzz other people get from a night out, and backing a friend's start up, a speculative share or a creative project holds a charge for you. Finances with a lover tend to become entangled early, and romance and money blur in ways that are thrilling and occasionally expensive. Money spent on children, or money that arrives through them, can figure strongly in your story. Your own creative work attracts patrons, grants or investors when you pitch it with conviction. Gambling on a hunch with funds that are not only yours is the weak spot. Given some discipline, your appetite for risk becomes a flair for spotting what is worth backing.",
    "6": "Other people's money shows up in your working day. You could handle payroll, insurance claims, loans, accounts or tax for a living, or be the colleague everyone turns to when a pension form lands on the desk. Your own debts are managed through routine and careful tracking, with a regular check of the balance that you rarely skip. Worry about what you owe settles straight into your habits, and one alarming bill can put you off your food or your sleep for a week. Employer schemes, sick pay and workplace pensions matter more to you than to most people. Grinding through repayments without ever stopping to renegotiate is a familiar habit. Your steady eye for detail makes you trustworthy with money that belongs to others.",
    "7": "Shared money arrives through partnership. Marriage, a business partner or one significant contract tends to shape your finances heavily, and the person you commit to often brings resources, debts or a completely different money style into your life. You are skilled at negotiating terms, working out a fair split and reading what the other side needs from a deal. Resentment builds when the balance tips and one of you ends up funding the other without it ever being said aloud. Written agreements protect you far better than good intentions. Entered with open books, partnerships become the route to a kind of wealth you could never build on your own.",
    "8": "With this house's ruler at home in its own house, everything about shared resources becomes concentrated, intense and self-contained. Money that is not strictly yours, through inheritance, investment, a partner's income or debt, plays a decisive role, and you handle it with a seriousness other people find almost unnerving. You read contracts to the last clause, spot the hidden fee and know who owes whom. Financial crises come in waves, and you emerge from each one knowing more about power and trust. Secrecy is your instinct: few people ever learn what you are worth or what you owe. That discretion can harden into control. Your talent for managing other people's money, whether in finance, insurance, tax or estates, runs deep.",
    "9": "Debt, investment and inheritance are bound up with distant places, education and belief. Foreign investments, a partner from another country, funding for study abroad or an inheritance that crosses a border can all feature. An overseas property, a pension from a job abroad or a currency swing can prove surprisingly significant to your bottom line. Student loans, scholarships and grants for research or publishing often play their part. You approach finance with a philosophy, trusting a principle about risk rather than the day's headlines, and you can argue for it for hours. Overconfidence is the weak spot, betting big on a conviction without checking the figures. When the vision and the numbers line up, shared resources widen your world far beyond where you began.",
    "10": "Joint and borrowed money is bound up with your career and public standing. Banking, investment, insurance, tax, estates or any role that involves handling large sums belonging to others suits you, and your reputation rests on how you carry that trust. A partner's wealth or a family inheritance can visibly shape your professional path, funding a business or buying you time to train. Bonuses, shares, commission and a company pension often matter more than the base salary on your contract. When debt goes wrong it feels public and exposing, as if everyone you work with can see it. You are drawn to positions of financial authority, the signatory, the treasurer, the person who approves the budget. Handled with integrity, that stewardship earns you serious respect.",
    "11": "Shared money flows through friends, networks and groups. Pooled funds, shared ventures, a business started with friends or property held within your circle can shape your finances. Friends lend, borrow or invest alongside you, and money can complicate friendships you care about. Collective finance appeals to you: cooperatives, community energy schemes, ethical funds, anything that spreads wealth around rather than hoarding it. Your hopes for the future often depend on backing from others, a grant, a sponsor or an investor who shares your vision. Trouble starts when things stay vague between friends, the unrepaid loan that nobody mentions but everyone remembers. With clear agreements in place, your network turns into a source of financial support and opportunity.",
    "12": "Behind the scenes is where joint money does its work for you. Hidden debts, private trusts, an inheritance you knew nothing about or arrangements kept quiet from the rest of the family tend to feature. You can be hazy about what you owe or what is owed to you, and difficult news about money can sit unexamined for a long time because facing it feels overwhelming. Support can come through charities, hospitals, institutions or benefactors who prefer to stay anonymous. You give generously to people in trouble, often more than you can afford. Confusion and self-sacrifice around joint funds are the dangers, including being taken advantage of. Once the numbers are brought into daylight, your intuition about money and your compassion work beautifully together."
  },
  "career:house10": {
    "1": "Your career is written into who you are, and people identify you with your work almost from the first handshake. You carry your professional role in your posture, your clothes and the way you walk into a meeting, and you often find your calling by doing what comes naturally rather than following a set ladder. Self-employment, personal branding or any role where your own face is the product suits you. Criticism of your work stings as if it were criticism of you, and you replay a bad appraisal for days. Building an identity outside the job is the harder task, and it shows when a role ends or a business closes. At full strength, you lead by example, and your reputation grows straight out of your own presence.",
    "2": "Money, resources and personal values are where your vocation takes shape. Career and income are tightly linked for you: you judge a job partly by what it pays, and you feel most respected in the month the pay rise comes through. Finance, property, food, design, music or anything tangible and lasting can draw you in. You build a reputation slowly, like a savings account, and stay in a role long enough to see returns on the effort. A secure post can trap you in comfort long after your ambition has moved on. Colleagues and clients know you for your practicality, your taste or your eye for quality. Over the years, your professional standing becomes an asset as solid as any property.",
    "3": "Words, communication and the local world carry your vocation. Writing, teaching, sales, media, transport, admin or anything that keeps you talking and moving suits you. People know you for what you say, the messages you send and the introductions you make, and a whole career can grow from one well placed word or a chance conversation. Siblings or neighbours sometimes steer your path or even work alongside you. You juggle several roles at once: a day job and a side hustle, a newsletter and a short course. Spreading your energy across too many small things is the danger. Focused, your quick thinking makes you known as the person who gets information where it needs to go.",
    "4": "Professional success, for you, starts close to home. Working from home, running a family business, property, hospitality, care or anything connected with roots and belonging suits you. A parent's career or expectations shape yours strongly, whether you follow in their footsteps or deliberately walk the other way. Public and private life are hard to keep apart: a promotion changes the whole household's routine, and a family crisis shows on your face at work. Professional peaks often arrive later in life, once your foundations feel secure. Retreating when you ought to step forward is a familiar habit. Your reputation grows from the sense of safety you create, and colleagues treat you as the anchor of the team.",
    "5": "Creativity, play and self-expression are the stage for your ambitions. Performing, working with children, entertainment, sport, design or any job where you can put your personal stamp on the result suits you. You need to enjoy the work, and a role that bores you drains you faster than it would most people. Hobbies turn into careers, and something you once did purely for pleasure has a way of becoming your paid work. Recognition matters, and you shine when there is an audience or a stage of some kind. Treating a career as a game leads to risky moves, such as dropping a steady post for a passion that has not yet paid a bill. Pursued with commitment, your creativity becomes your professional signature.",
    "6": "Ambition, for you, is built in the details of daily work. Health, service, craft, administration, analysis or anything that improves how things run suits you. People know you as reliable, skilled and conscientious, the one who finishes the job and checks it twice. Your career builds through practical competence and steady refinement rather than grand leaps, and one well organised project often leads to the next promotion. Routines, workplace systems and colleagues matter enormously, and a good team can make an ordinary job feel meaningful. Overwork is the familiar trap: staying late, saying yes to extra, confusing busyness with progress. Your reputation rests on your usefulness, and people rely on you in a way that earns quiet, lasting respect.",
    "7": "Partnership is the engine of your public life. Business partners, clients, agents and collaborators shape your career more than you expect, and the big breaks usually arrive through one key relationship. Law, counselling, consulting, diplomacy, design or any work done one to one suits you. A spouse can influence or share your professional life, or your marriage becomes part of your public image. You think best out loud with someone across the table and struggle when left entirely alone at the top. Losing yourself in another person's ambitions is the risk, polishing their name while yours stays off the door. Chosen well, partners lift your standing and carry you to heights you could not climb by yourself.",
    "8": "Deep, intense or hidden territory is where your professional life finds its purpose. Finance, investment, psychology, research, medicine, crisis work, insurance or anything dealing with power, money or transformation suits you. Your career tends to move through dramatic endings and rebirths: a redundancy that opens a new direction, a crisis that reveals what you are made of. Other people's resources often fund your path, through investors, a partner or an inheritance. You work well behind closed doors and handle confidential matters with complete composure. Power struggles at work can grow heated, and you never forget who crossed you. Embraced, your willingness to go where others fear makes you formidable and widely trusted in your field.",
    "9": "Borders and big ideas define the reach of your career. Teaching, publishing, law, travel, academia, religion or international work suits you. Your career often involves foreign countries, overseas clients or a move abroad that changes everything, and distance has a way of opening doors for you. Higher education opens professional doors, and you gravitate towards roles that let you share a wider vision. You want your work to mean something and grow restless in jobs that feel small. Preaching rather than practising, or chasing the next horizon before finishing the current one, is the pitfall. Grounded, your breadth of outlook makes you known as someone who inspires others and widens the world around them.",
    "10": "Sitting in its own house, this ruler makes career a strong, self-directed and central theme. You know what you want to achieve and you are prepared to climb for it, steadily and with considerable determination, often mapping out the next five years before anyone asks. Your calling is visible and sharply defined, and people see you as a natural authority in your field. Management, leadership and public roles suit you well. The weak point is letting career swallow everything else, so that rest, friendships and family always come second and holidays get cancelled for deadlines. At full strength, you build a professional legacy that stands on its own and outlasts any single job title.",
    "11": "Networks, groups and ideals for the future drive your professional path. Technology, social causes, campaigning, large organisations, science or any collective effort suits you. Friends and contacts play a major part in your career, and a single conversation with the right person can open a door that stays open for years. You want your work to serve something bigger than yourself, and you come alive in teams that share a vision. Your reputation often grows through professional associations and communities rather than a single employer. Blending into the group so completely that your own contribution goes unseen is a risk. Leading from within, you become known as someone who connects the right people with the right ideas.",
    "12": "Your calling plays out behind the scenes. Hospitals, charities, prisons, retreats, research, the arts, spiritual work or any institution serving hidden needs suits you. You are often more influential than visible, the person who makes things happen while someone else takes the applause. Your career path can feel mysterious, guided by intuition, coincidence or a sense of vocation that is hard to explain on a CV. Uncertainty about direction and difficulty claiming public recognition are ongoing struggles. You work best with solitude and time to reflect, and open plan offices exhaust you. Trusted, your quiet dedication and compassion shape a career that heals and helps in ways few people ever see."
  },
  "career:house6": {
    "1": "Your working day is an extension of who you are. You approach every task personally, arriving with your own methods and standards, and colleagues can spot your work without seeing the name on it. How busy you are shapes how you feel about yourself: an empty to do list leaves you restless, while a productive morning puts a spring in your step for the rest of the day. You often set the pace for the whole team, whether you mean to or not. Taking every small mistake as a verdict on your character wears you down over a long week. Your body registers overwork quickly, in tight shoulders and short sleep. At its healthiest, your self-led way of working is something others copy.",
    "2": "Earning and making things last shape every working hour. You want daily effort to translate directly into income, and you notice quickly when a job asks too much for too little. Steady routines, a regular payslip and familiar surroundings help you settle into good work. Colleagues know you as the patient, practical one who builds things properly and makes them last. Being rushed makes you dig in, and you resist changing a method that already works, even when the new software arrives with great fanfare. Comfort can turn into inertia. Valued properly, you are the dependable one who turns ordinary days into solid, tangible results.",
    "3": "Messages, errands and conversations fill your working hours. Calls, emails, short trips, meetings and constant multitasking define your routine, and you feel most alive with several threads running at once. Colleagues rely on you to pass information along, explain the new system or draft the note everyone needs by lunchtime. Work can involve a lot of local travel, or it keeps you close to your neighbourhood, and siblings or neighbours sometimes play a part. Mental overload is the hazard: too many threads running at once and a mind still buzzing long after work ends. Short breaks and a change of scene reset you. Organised, your versatility makes you the linchpin of any team.",
    "4": "The workplace and the household overlap for you. You could work from home, in a family business, in property, care or hospitality, or you bring a homely, welcoming atmosphere into any workplace you join. Colleagues start to feel like family, and you look after them accordingly, remembering birthdays and noticing who looks tired. Household jobs and work tasks blur together, which is efficient right up until you can no longer switch off. Moods at home travel straight into your productivity. Firm boundaries between work time and home time protect you. With those in place, you build a work environment where people feel safe and cared for.",
    "5": "Daily work only flows for you when there is creativity and enjoyment in it. Routine work drains you unless you can turn it into a game, add your own flair or find something to play with. Jobs involving children, entertainment, the arts, sport or teaching often suit you. You bring warmth and fun to colleagues and are usually the one who turns an ordinary working week into something to celebrate. Pouring energy into the tasks you love while the dull ones pile up is the classic pattern, and the tedious admin sits untouched for weeks. When the balance is right, you turn daily work into a source of pleasure and pride.",
    "6": "Placed in its own house, this ruler concentrates everything about daily work into one self-contained theme. You have a natural relationship with routine, craft and service, and you usually know how to organise a working day better than anyone around you. Skills, habits and competence are your currency, and you keep a list of what needs fixing. You take pride in doing a job properly and notice every flaw, including ones nobody else has seen. Perfectionism and overwork are the obvious risks, along with worry that keeps work on your mind long after hours. Well directed, your devotion to good work makes you indispensable, the person every manager hopes to hire.",
    "7": "Partnership sits at the centre of your daily routine. You work best alongside someone, whether a trusted colleague, a client or a business partner, and much of your routine involves one to one meetings, negotiation or advising. A spouse or partner can work with you, or your relationships mirror your working habits in telling ways. You smooth over conflicts and keep the peace in the team, often acting as the unofficial mediator between departments. Quietly absorbing everyone else's workload to avoid friction is the trap. Choosing fair collaborators matters enormously, because a lopsided partnership eats your days. With the right people, work becomes an exchange, lighter and more productive than anything you manage alone.",
    "8": "Depth, intensity and other people's resources colour your daily workload. Money, research, crisis work, psychology, medicine or anything requiring focus and discretion can fill your hours. You handle heavy workloads and emotionally charged situations with steady nerves, the calm voice when everyone else is panicking. Colleagues trust you with secrets, and very little in office politics escapes your notice. Burnout arrives dramatically: you push until something breaks, then overhaul your entire way of working in one go. Control over your own tasks matters a great deal, and micromanagement makes you bristle. Embraced, your capacity to go deep turns an ordinary job into powerful and meaningful work.",
    "9": "Your working day stretches well beyond the local. Travel, foreign colleagues, teaching, publishing, law or anything connected with ideas and learning can fill your routine. You need meaning in daily tasks and feel stifled by work that seems small or endlessly repetitive. Colleagues from different backgrounds fascinate you, and you pick up phrases and habits from all of them. Promising more than a day can hold is a regular pattern, with ambitious lists and grand plans that never quite get done. Grounded, your enthusiasm for learning makes you a natural mentor and keeps your work fresh and expansive.",
    "10": "Each ordinary task at work feeds your ambition and public standing. You tend to rise through sheer competence, the person others notice because you deliver, every time. You can let the job define your entire life, answering to work even when you are meant to be resting.",
    "11": "Teams, networks and technology carry your daily work. You thrive in collaborative settings, group projects, remote work or organisations with a cause. Colleagues become friends, and friends sometimes become colleagues, so the line between working life and social life is thin. You like reinventing how work is done, suggesting new tools and systems before anyone else has noticed a problem. Rebelling against rigid routines, or drifting from task to task, can undermine your output. Your ideals matter in daily life, and a job that clashes with your values wears you out fast. Aligned with a purpose, your knack for connecting people and improving processes makes work feel forward looking.",
    "12": "Much of your daily work happens behind the scenes. You could work alone, in institutions, hospitals, charities, research, the arts or anywhere quiet and tucked away. You absorb colleagues' moods easily and need solitude to recover, and a day of back to back meetings leaves you drained in a way that is hard to explain. Workloads can feel overwhelming or oddly unclear, and you sometimes work hard without recognition. Escapism, avoiding tasks or losing track of time are constant risks. Gentle routines that include proper rest keep you steady. Supported, your compassion and intuition make you a healing presence at work, doing service that matters."
  },
  "home:house4": {
    "1": "Home and family sit at the centre of your identity. You carry your roots with you, and people sense your background in the way you speak, dress and carry yourself. Your sense of self grew directly out of your family story, whether you embrace it or fight against it. Your home bears your personal stamp so strongly that disorder there can make you feel exposed. Family matters feel intensely personal, and a parent's approval counts for more than you admit to friends. Pulling back into self-protection when hurt is a familiar reflex. As you mature, you become the emotional anchor of your family, the person everyone turns to first.",
    "2": "Money and security are woven into your sense of home. Owning property, building a comfortable nest and providing for your household matter enormously to you. Family resources, heirlooms or inherited property can play a big role, and you feel the history in whatever has been handed down. Physical comfort is a priority, and a home that feels warm, well stocked and inviting settles you. Your self-worth is often bound up with your family's values and approval. Clinging to possessions or old family patterns can hold you back. When you feel secure, you create a home that is a sanctuary, solid and generous to everyone who visits.",
    "3": "Conversation and the local neighbourhood give your home life its pulse. Siblings, cousins or neighbours feature strongly in your domestic life, and you often live close to relatives or pop round without warning. Your home is lively, full of ideas, conversation and people coming and going. Moving house often, or keeping two bases, suits your restless streak. Family talk and news carry emotional weight, and a sharp comment from someone close can colour your whole week. At its best, your home becomes a hub of ideas and connection that keeps the whole family in touch.",
    "4": "With this ruler in its own house, home and family form a strong, self-contained theme. Your roots run deep, and your sense of belonging is powerful. You invest heavily in your home and your people, and you know exactly what you need to feel safe: familiarity, warmth and small comforts that never change. Family traditions matter, and you often stay close to where you grew up or recreate it wherever you land. When hurt, you withdraw into your private world or become overprotective of loved ones. You create a secure base that nourishes everyone who walks through your door.",
    "5": "Creativity, children and joy fill the family home. Your home is a place for play, entertaining and self-expression, full of warmth and creative energy. Children often bring you back to your roots, or your family inspires your creative life. You love to fill your home with people, colour and celebration. Family drama can turn theatrical, with big scenes and bigger reconciliations. Needing constant attention from family, or chasing fun at the expense of stability, can unsettle the household. Balanced, your home becomes a warm, creative space filled with laughter and the sound of people who feel free to be themselves.",
    "6": "Work, routine and care organise your home life. You could work from home, or the household runs on tight routines and careful planning. Caring for family members, ageing parents above all, can become part of daily life, and you are often the one who keeps track of what everyone needs. You keep your home orderly and notice every small task that needs doing long before anyone else does. Wellbeing at home matters to you. Turning domestic life into endless chores is the trap, never sitting down until everyone else has. Balanced, your home becomes a place of practical care and quiet efficiency.",
    "7": "Partnership is the doorway to your sense of home. Your partner strongly shapes your home life, and a committed relationship often defines your sense of belonging. You could live with a partner's family, or build a home together as the central project of your relationship, shaping every corner of it together. Harmony at home matters enormously, and you smooth over tension before it has a chance to settle. Family patterns from childhood travel into your relationships, sometimes without you noticing. Now and then your own roots disappear into another person's world. Chosen well, partnership creates a home that feels shared, where both of you belong equally.",
    "8": "Intensity, secrets and transformation run through your family life. Family history contains hidden stories, inheritance issues or emotional complexity that surfaces whenever the family gathers. Your home can be a place of deep healing or a site of power struggles, and sometimes both in the same year. Shared resources, a partner's money or an inheritance often fund your home. You need privacy and emotional depth behind your own front door, and shallow visitors wear you out. Control or unresolved family pain can hold you back. Faced honestly, your family roots become a source of profound strength and renewal, and you often end up healing a pattern that ran for generations.",
    "9": "Distance and belief stretch your idea of home. You could live abroad, have family scattered in other countries, or have grown up surrounded by strong religious or philosophical values. Home is where you learn and grow, full of ideas, curiosity and lively debate. Relocating for study, faith or adventure can reshape your sense of belonging. You feel most at home when life feels expansive. Restlessness can make settling hard, with one eye always on the next move. Once you find the right balance, your home becomes a place of learning and wide horizons for everyone in it.",
    "10": "Home and family are tied to career and public standing. Your family's reputation, or a parent's career, shapes your own ambitions, sometimes more than you would like to admit. Working from home or running a family business are natural paths, and home often doubles as your headquarters. Balancing home and work is a lifelong juggling act, with work spilling into time that should be your own. Family expectations about achievement weigh heavily, and you still hear a parent's voice when you consider a job offer. Handled wisely, your home supports your ambitions, and your achievements honour the roots you came from.",
    "11": "Friends and community make up a large part of what home means to you. Your home is open to friends, and close friends feel like family, welcome to stay for as long as they need. Communal living, shared housing or an unconventional household arrangement can suit you. Your family itself is unusual in some way: blended, extended or deliberately chosen. Plans for the future often involve where and how you will live together with others. Detaching from your own roots, or keeping everyone at arm's length emotionally, is the risk. You create a home that welcomes your chosen family, a place where outsiders become insiders.",
    "12": "Mystery, sacrifice and spiritual depth surround your family story. Family history involves hidden stories, loss, illness or unspoken pain, and some things are simply never talked about. Your home is a sanctuary for retreat, and you guard your quiet hours fiercely. Caring for family members through illness or hardship can become part of your life. Boundaries blur at home, and you absorb the moods of everyone around you without realising. Escaping into solitude or feeling responsible for everyone's pain can drain you. As old wounds heal, your home becomes a peaceful and spiritual refuge, restoring you and the people you love."
  },
  "health:house6": {
    "1": "Your daily habits show on you quickly. A week of early nights and proper meals is visible in your face and posture, and so is a fortnight of skipped lunches and late screens. You carry your routine like a signature, and people know you by the habits you keep and the care you take with them. How you work and how you feel in your body are hard to separate, so a job that suits you leaves you looking well. Restlessness in your limbs is often the first signal that something in your schedule has gone wrong. Treating your body as a personal project, rather than a chore, is what keeps your energy steady.",
    "2": "Wellbeing and money sit close together for you. You know what looking after yourself costs, and you judge a habit partly by whether it feels like good value. Comfort matters to your body, and warmth, good food and a sense of ease steady you more than any strict plan. When money is tight, your routine is the first thing to slip, and you eat whatever is cheapest and quickest. Security helps your nerves settle, so a healthy savings balance can feel oddly like a health measure. Slow, sensual pleasures restore you more reliably than dramatic regimes, because your body settles through ease.",
    "3": "Your mind and your body run on the same wiring. A crowded mind, a tense exchange or a day of constant chatter shows up as tension in your body by evening. Movement helps you think, and you solve problems best when you are up and about rather than sitting still. You tend to read up on wellbeing and pass what you learn on to the people around you. Too much input overloads you, and taking in information late in the day costs you more than it costs most people. Short breaks, less noise and conversations that reach an end keep your energy even and your nerves calm.",
    "4": "Your health habits were learned early, in the home you grew up in. The way your family ate, rested and handled being unwell still shapes your routine, whether you copy it or do the opposite. Home is where you recover, and familiar surroundings and your own space do more for you than any luxury away from home. Unrest in the household lands in your body, so tension or chaos at home can leave you drained for days. Nourishing yourself properly, rather than eating on the run, has a steadying effect. A calm, well ordered home base is the foundation your energy is built on, and you feel it the moment it wobbles.",
    "5": "Pleasure is part of your health, not a break from it. You keep fit when fitness feels like play, and anything that feels like a grim chore is soon quietly abandoned. Creative work restores you too, and making something with your own hands leaves you lighter than a nap. Treats creep in when life turns dull, and a little indulgence can easily stretch into a habit. Romance and fun lift your energy visibly. Your body responds best to joy, so a routine built around what you love is the one that lasts.",
    "6": "Health is a theme you take seriously in its own right. Routine is a comfort, a steady rhythm of meals, movement and rest, and you notice at once when any piece of it slips. Your body is a sensitive instrument, reacting quickly to poor food, bad sleep or a stressful week at work. People know you as the organised, sensible one, and small daily practices carry you. Worry is the flip side: you can over-monitor, reading every twinge as a warning and tweaking your diet endlessly. Given sensible structure and a little room for imperfection, your habits become an unusual source of strength.",
    "7": "Other people have a direct effect on your wellbeing. You keep to a routine far more easily when someone shares it with you, and effort feels lighter when it is shared. A close relationship that runs smoothly leaves you energised, while a strained one shows up in your sleep and appetite within days. You often adjust your habits to fit a partner's schedule, eating when they eat and going to bed when they do. That can be healthy, and it can also mean your own needs fall off the list. Fair relationships, shared effort and time with people who look after you as well as you look after them keep you well.",
    "8": "Stress goes deep with you and stays there. You can hold your composure through a crisis and then feel it in your body weeks later, once the danger has passed. Shared burdens weigh on you, and other people's troubles, secrets and grief quietly become part of your own load. Your energy runs in cycles of intensity and depletion, and you recover best through complete rest rather than half measures. Periods of upheaval, such as a move or a loss, reset your habits entirely. Your capacity to rebuild is strong, and you often find your best routines after a hard season rather than before it.",
    "9": "Space and movement are good for you. Space, movement and the feeling of somewhere new around you restore your energy faster than any familiar routine. You like a philosophy of wellbeing, and you take up a new approach with enthusiasm and love explaining why it works. Routines that feel narrow or pointless do not last, so you need to understand why a habit matters before you commit. Excess is the trap, and your appetite for life can tip into too much of a good thing. Adventure, fresh air and a sense of purpose keep your body feeling alive and your spirits up.",
    "10": "Work and reputation have a strong hold on your health. A demanding job shapes your whole day, from when you eat to how much you sleep, and you are often still working long after everyone else has stopped. Achievement energises you, while feeling undervalued at work drains you more than long hours do. Responsibility settles in your shoulders and jaw, and you notice it most when a big project ends. When your career has a sustainable shape, your body follows, and people often admire how well you manage both.",
    "11": "Friends and groups are part of your wellbeing. You exercise more happily in company than alone, and a goal you share with others keeps you going far longer. Social life shapes your routine for better and worse: the friends who lift your energy, and the ones who keep you up far too late. New ideas about health catch your eye, and you enjoy trying them out and comparing notes with others. Irregular hours suit you in bursts but wear you down if they become the norm. Community and a sense of belonging steady your nerves more than any solitary plan.",
    "12": "Rest and solitude are essential to your health, not optional. You recharge through quiet time alone, away from every demand, with nothing and no one needing anything from you. Your body picks up on hidden stress, and you can feel run down without being able to name the cause until you stop. Crowded, noisy weeks drain you invisibly, so you often notice the cost only once things slow down. Sleep is your greatest ally, and your dreams and moods say a lot about how you are coping. Gentle, unhurried movement and quiet stillness suit you far better than anything harsh or competitive."
  },
  "mind:house3": {
    "1": "Your way of thinking is part of your identity. People meet your mind first: the quick remark, the question on the tip of your tongue, the running commentary on whatever is happening around you. You think out loud and form opinions on the spot, often surprising yourself with what comes out. Being seen as bright and well informed matters to you, and you notice when a conversation moves on without you. Mental restlessness spills into the body, so you fidget, gesture and pace while you talk. Your voice, in writing or in speech, is one of the clearest ways you have of being seen, and people remember how you put things.",
    "2": "Practical, value-driven thinking is where your mind goes first. You learn best when you can see what the knowledge is worth, and you remember prices, figures and small details other people forget. Talking and writing can become ways of earning, through sales, teaching or any work that rewards careful attention. You think steadily, preferring to settle a question once and for all rather than juggle ten ideas at once. Once you hold an opinion, you keep it, sometimes longer than is useful. Your thoughts feel secure when they rest on solid facts, and you trust what you can check for yourself, slowly and without pressure.",
    "3": "Your everyday mind is at home in its own territory. Curiosity is constant: you read whatever is in front of you, take an interest in every conversation within earshot and cannot resist something new to learn. Learning comes easily in short, lively bursts, and you pick up names, routes and local news without trying. Siblings, neighbours and nearby friends play a large part in how you think, and many of your best ideas come from a casual chat with someone close by. Scattered attention is the cost, with too many interests running at once and little ever quite finished. Given something to write, teach or talk about, this busy mind becomes an asset.",
    "4": "Your thinking is rooted in home and family. You learned to talk, argue and reason within your family, and its phrases and opinions still echo in your head. Much of your best thinking happens at home, in comfort and quiet, where your mind is free to wander. Memory is strong, and you can recall exact conversations from years ago along with the feeling in the room. Writing about the past, family history or where you come from often fascinates you, and a settled home clears your head like nothing else.",
    "5": "Your mind loves to play. You think best when an idea is fun, and you enjoy wordplay, stories and any exchange with a bit of performance in it. Learning sticks when it is creative, so a lesson with colour and play in it stays with you long after the dry version fades. An audience brings out your wit, and a lively exchange lights you up more than a quiet memo. Teaching, storytelling or any creative way of sharing ideas suits you, and people wait to hear how you will tell it. Boredom kills your attention quickly, and you drift off mid sentence when a subject feels dutiful. When thinking feels like self-expression rather than a task, your mind is at its brightest.",
    "6": "Your everyday mind is busy with the practical. You think in lists, schedules and procedures, and you are the person who spots the error, the missed step or the better way to do an everyday task. Work gives your thoughts a shape, and much of your mental energy goes on solving small daily problems efficiently. You learn by doing, and a skill makes sense once your hands have practised it a few times. Worry creeps in when there is nothing to fix, with your mind chewing on minor details late at night. Useful, precise thinking is your strength, and colleagues rely on your clear explanations and your notes from the meeting.",
    "7": "You think best in conversation with another person. Ideas take shape when you bounce them off a partner, a friend or a colleague, and you often only know your view once someone has challenged it. Seeing both sides is second nature, and people bring you their disagreements because you can explain each person to the other. Negotiation, mediation and one to one teaching suit you well. The drawback is leaning too heavily on others' opinions, or softening your own words to keep the peace. A close partnership full of searching conversation, the kind that runs on long after it should, is one of the most stimulating things in your life.",
    "8": "Beneath the surface is where your thinking wants to be. Small talk leaves you cold, while a conversation about secrets, motives or what happened keeps you up late. You notice what people avoid saying, and you read between the lines of every message. Research, investigation and subjects others find uncomfortable draw you in, from psychology to hidden history to the small print everyone else skips. Words carry weight for you, and a sharp remark can stay with you for years. You guard your own thoughts closely, sharing them only with people you trust completely. Given depth to work with, your thinking is penetrating, persistent and very hard to fool.",
    "9": "Your everyday thinking reaches for the bigger picture. A casual chat about the weather turns into a discussion about meaning, politics or how people live elsewhere, and you enjoy it most when it does. You read widely, pick up foreign phrases easily, and connect small facts to large theories. Short journeys feed your mind too, and even a brief change of scene fills you with new ideas. Patience with detail is the weak point: you skim the instructions and trust the general idea. Writing and talking about broad subjects suits you, and people remember your enthusiasm long after they have forgotten the specifics you were so sure about.",
    "10": "Ambition and public life shape how you think. You think strategically, weighing how a conversation will land with the people who matter professionally, and your words carry a certain authority. Communication plays a visible role in your career, through writing, speaking, teaching or being the one trusted to say what everyone else is too nervous to say. You learn most seriously when it leads somewhere. Casual chat can feel harder than presenting formally, and you sometimes sound more guarded than you mean.",
    "11": "Your thinking comes alive in groups. Groups, networks and friends with unusual interests are where your ideas get sharpened and passed around. New and unusual subjects pull you in, from technology to social causes, and you enjoy imagining how things could work differently. Friends are often your teachers, and a single conversation with one of them can change your view for good. You are good at connecting people through information, the one who says 'you two should talk'. Staying with one topic is harder, since a fresh idea always seems to be arriving from somewhere. Your mind works best when it serves a shared vision.",
    "12": "Much of your thinking happens out of sight. You process privately, and your best ideas arrive when your mind drifts or on the edge of sleep. Speaking up in a busy room can feel harder than it should, and you replay what you meant to say long after the moment has passed. Intuition feeds your mind, so you pick up on things before you can explain how you know. Private reflection, solitary reading and quiet study suit you far better than open debate. Once you learn to trust that quiet inner voice, your insight turns out to be strikingly accurate, and people start asking for it."
  },
  "mind:house9": {
    "1": "Higher learning shapes who you are. You carry your ideas openly, and people see you as the student, the reader or the one with an opinion on how the world works. Study is personal: a degree, a course or a subject you taught yourself becomes part of your identity. You share what you have learned readily, sometimes more readily than the room wants, and friends hear about your latest discovery before you have finished exploring it. Confident belief can tip into lecturing when you are excited. Constant intellectual expansion keeps you youthful and bright, and your own story of learning often becomes your best material for teaching others.",
    "2": "You approach big ideas practically. Study appeals most when it has a clear return, and you weigh a course or a qualification partly by what it will earn you. Knowledge feels like property, something you build up steadily and keep, and what you know is an investment you are privately proud of. Your intellectual outlook is shaped by values: what is fair, what is worth the effort, what lasts. Teaching, publishing or advising can become a source of income. Abstract theory without application leaves you restless. Patient learning over many years builds you a store of expertise that others come to trust and pay for.",
    "3": "Big ideas reach you through everyday channels. Serious knowledge reaches you in small daily doses, picked up from conversation, reading and whatever else crosses your path. You are a natural explainer of complex subjects, translating difficult ideas into plain speech for the people around you. Short courses and self-directed reading suit you as well as formal education does. Breadth can outrun depth, leaving you knowing a little about everything and a lot about nothing in particular. Writing, blogging or teaching locally turns your wide curiosity into something useful. Siblings or neighbours often shape your views more than any professor.",
    "4": "Your intellectual life began at home. Family conversations and the ideas you grew up around laid the foundation for how you think about large questions. You study best in comfort, surrounded by your own things, and a space of your own for thinking matters to you. History, ancestry and the way other cultures live at home fascinate you. You may move abroad, or fill your home with foreign influences. Questioning the opinions you were raised with takes effort, but it deepens your thinking considerably.",
    "5": "Learning is a pleasure for you, not a chore. Subjects that spark your imagination win you over, and you study most happily when there is creativity, drama or a touch of romance in it. Teaching children, writing, or sharing your passions with an audience suits you. You fall for ideas the way others fall for people, with a rush of enthusiasm and late nights reading. Dry theory bores you within a chapter. Your big ideas often come out through art, stories or play rather than essays, and your delight in learning is infectious: people want to learn what you love because you make it sound thrilling.",
    "6": "Study, for you, is put to practical work. You learn in order to do something useful, and training, qualifications and professional development shape your daily life. Your intellectual approach is grounded in how things function: you trust evidence and method over grand theory. Teaching, advising or training others often becomes part of the job itself. Detail can crowd out the wider view, and you forget to ask why the work matters at all. Given a meaningful purpose, your study turns into measurable skill, and you are the colleague people seek out when a procedure needs explaining properly, step by careful step.",
    "7": "Relationships are where your big ideas grow. Partners, close friends and even rivals introduce you to new philosophies, countries and fields of study. You learn well in pairs, with a tutor or a study partner, and arguing a point with one sharp person teaches you more than a lecture hall. Partners from different cultures or with strong convictions draw you in, and you have probably picked up a whole subject because someone you loved was passionate about it. Absorbing another person's views wholesale is the pitfall. At its most fruitful, a relationship becomes a shared education, with ideas passed back and forth between you.",
    "8": "Your mind is drawn to the deep end of knowledge. You study what others avoid: psychology, death, power, hidden history, the mechanics of money. Surface explanations dissatisfy you, and you keep reading until you reach the root. Learning often follows a crisis, when you need to understand what has happened to you, and you emerge from a hard year with a whole new understanding. Your intellectual convictions can transform completely after a major life event. You hold ideas intensely and defend them fiercely in argument. Your research is thorough and penetrating, and what you learn tends to change you rather than inform you.",
    "9": "Your higher mind is in its element. Study and big ideas are central themes, and you keep learning long after formal education ends, with a new subject always on the go. Philosophy, law, languages and any field that explains how the world fits together draw you in. You work out your intellectual positions for yourself rather than inheriting them, through reading, argument and experience. Intellectual pride can creep in, along with a habit of assuming your framework covers everything. When it flows, you become a natural teacher, and friends turn to you to explain something complicated because you make it clear and exciting.",
    "10": "Your big ideas shape your career. Higher education, publishing, teaching, law or international work often play a strong role in your professional life. You become known publicly for what you know, and your expertise builds your reputation over years. Study is ambitious for you, a route to authority as much as a source of interest, and you notice which qualifications open which doors. The pressure to be seen as the expert can make it hard to admit what you do not know. As your career develops, your thinking grows more serious and responsible, and people begin to quote you in meetings you did not attend.",
    "11": "Your big ideas develop in community. Friends, networks and societies expose you to new philosophies, and you often study alongside people who share your ideals. Progressive, unusual and humanitarian subjects pull you in, and you are the friend who shares a fascinating idea the moment you find it. Online courses, reading groups and discussion forums suit your way of learning. Your thinking is future facing, concerned with how things could be better for everyone. Loyalty to a group's ideas can make you stubborn in debate. At its finest, your mind helps a whole circle of people see a larger, more hopeful picture.",
    "12": "Your higher mind turns inward. You study privately and often alone, and you are drawn to psychology, mysticism, dreams and knowledge that sits outside the mainstream. Big insights arrive in solitude, in quiet moments or in the half-awake space between sleep and waking. You may learn in hidden places, such as retreats, hospitals or institutions, or keep a subject almost secret from friends. Your intellectual convictions are private and strongly felt, and you rarely argue them in public. Escaping into ideas is the pitfall, reading about life rather than living it. Given time, your learning ripens into gentle, compassionate wisdom."
  },
  "growth:house9": {
    "1": "Your growth is written on you. Every journey, conviction and leap of faith changes how you carry yourself, and people can see when you have been somewhere that mattered. You grow by taking yourself into unfamiliar situations, saying yes before you feel ready and trusting that you will rise to meet them. Faith in your own path is strong, and it gives you a buoyant, forward-leaning presence. Restlessness can make you leave before a place has finished teaching you. Your life feels most meaningful when you are visibly becoming someone larger, and others take courage from watching you do it.",
    "2": "Meaning, for you, has to be tangible. You grow by learning what you value, and a sense of purpose often arrives through how you earn and what you choose to spend on. Travel matters, though you want it to feel worth the money, and you remember how a place felt, tasted and sounded more than its famous sights. Your faith is practical: you believe in what holds up over time. Clinging to comfort can keep you from the leap that would change you. The leap happens when your beliefs and your bank balance point in the same direction.",
    "3": "You grow through the ordinary journeys most people overlook. Everyday experiences carry big lessons for you, and a single remark or a small change of surroundings can stay with you for years. Your sense of meaning is shaped by conversations, and your outlook shifts through what siblings, neighbours and old friends show you. Faith, for you, is something you talk your way into, testing it out loud. You can mistake having an opinion for having found your path. Your life expands most when curiosity leads you just past the edge of what is familiar, one small step at a time.",
    "4": "Your search for meaning starts at home and often leads you far from it. The faith or philosophy of your family shaped your early outlook, and much of your growth is about making that inheritance your own or setting it down. You may settle abroad, or make a home in a culture not your own. You feel most expanded when home itself becomes a place of hope, open to new people and alive with big questions. A home that reflects what you now believe becomes the base from which you keep expanding.",
    "5": "Joy is your road to meaning. You grow through what delights you, and pleasure has a way of turning into experience that changes your whole outlook. Your faith is playful and generous, and you believe life is meant to be enjoyed, not merely endured. Children, art and romance teach you as much as any philosophy, and your happiest memories tend to be your wisest ones too. Chasing thrills can stand in for growth. Purpose deepens when your pleasures carry you somewhere new, and your expansiveness encourages others to take a risk on happiness.",
    "6": "You find meaning in the everyday. Your growth comes through service, skill and the discipline of showing up, and a humble routine can become almost sacred to you. Work sometimes takes you abroad or brings people from other cultures into your daily life. Your faith is practical: you believe in doing things well and helping where you can. Getting lost in tasks can leave you feeling your life lacks a larger shape. Purpose arrives when you see that your daily efforts serve something bigger, and that the care you put into ordinary work is itself a form of belief in action.",
    "7": "Other people are your gateway to a larger life. A partner often opens your world, introducing you to new countries, beliefs or ways of living you would never have found alone. You grow through close relationships, and some of your most important journeys were taken with someone at your side. You are drawn to people whose convictions are strong or whose backgrounds are very different from yours. Borrowing someone else's sense of purpose can stall your own. Meaning deepens when a partnership becomes a shared adventure in which each of you helps the other become larger.",
    "8": "Your growth comes through the deep end. Crises, losses and intense bonds are the forces that change your beliefs, and you often find meaning only after life has taken something away. You are drawn to questions of death, rebirth and what lies beneath appearances, and a single profound experience can transform your whole outlook overnight. Travel for you is rarely casual: you seek places that unsettle and renew you. Clinging to certainty can make you resist the change you most need. Your faith is hard won, and it carries a quiet authority that shallower convictions lack.",
    "9": "Growth is one of the great themes of your life. Travel, faith and the search for meaning come naturally, and you feel most alive on the road, in a new culture or in the middle of a conversation about what life is for. You forge your own convictions rather than inheriting them, and they evolve as you go. Optimism carries you far, sometimes further than practicality allows. Self-righteousness is the pitfall, the belief that your truth is the truth. When your adventures stay open-hearted, you become a living example of how wide a life can be.",
    "10": "Your purpose and your public life are bound together. Career often takes you abroad, into international work or into roles where your beliefs are visible, and you grow most when your work feels like a mission. You want your standing in the world to reflect what you stand for, and a job without meaning leaves you hollow however well it pays. Ambition can swallow your wider search for purpose. Your career becomes yours once your achievements express your convictions.",
    "11": "You grow in company. Friends, causes and communities widen your world, and some of your most important growth has come through experiences shared with people who think as you do. Your faith is social and future looking, bound up with hopes for how people could live together. You are drawn to movements and ideals larger than yourself. Losing yourself in a group's vision can blur your own beliefs. Meaning deepens when your friendships carry you somewhere new and when your hopes are shared by people who push you to become more than you were.",
    "12": "Your search for meaning is largely private. Faith grows slowly in you, through solitude, reflection and quiet time with no purpose but being. Journeys that matter most are often inner ones, and a trip taken alone can feel like a pilgrimage even if it never looked like one. You are drawn to spiritual traditions, sacred places and experiences that dissolve the ordinary self. Escaping into belief can keep you from engaging with the world. Surrender opens the way: trusting what you cannot see and following a quiet inner pull without needing a reason. That quiet, hard-to-explain faith often steadies others more than you realise."
  },
  "spirit:house12": {
    "1": "Your private world sits close to the surface. Moods, hunches and last night's dream show on your face before you have put words to them, and friends ask what is wrong while you are still working out that something is. You need time alone to know who you are, and after too much company you feel strangely absent from yourself until you have had some real quiet. There is a softness in your presence that invites confidences from people you barely know. Soaking up every atmosphere you walk into can leave you unsure which feelings are yours. Withdrawing without apology is what keeps that sensitivity a strength rather than a drain.",
    "2": "Stillness reaches you through the senses. Small sensory comforts can shift you into a deeper, quieter state, and you treat them almost as rituals that bring you back to yourself. Money and possessions carry hidden emotional weight, so an unexpected bill can unsettle you far more than the sum deserves. You give generously and anonymously, sometimes to people who never find out it was you. Reaching for comfort to avoid a feeling is the familiar trap. Simple, physical calm, close to nature and the ground beneath you, leads you most reliably towards peace.",
    "3": "Words are the doorway to your unconscious. Words, written or spoken quietly to yourself, are where buried feelings find a voice, and you often understand what you feel only after putting it into words. Thoughts arrive from somewhere deeper than logic, and you have had the uncanny experience of saying the right thing to a friend without knowing where it came from. A busy mind drowns out the quiet, so silence is precious and you guard it. Unspoken tensions with people from your early life can echo in your head for years. Putting feelings into words settles you in a way nothing else quite does.",
    "4": "The deepest layer of you was laid down at home. Ancestral patterns, unspoken family feelings and memories from very early childhood sit in your unconscious, and they surface in dreams of old houses and in sudden, unexplained tenderness or grief. Home is your sanctuary, the place where you can stop performing and go quiet. A private space of your own, however small, matters more to you than you let on. Sorrows your parents never spoke about can live on in you unrecognised. Making gentle sense of what you inherited, and turning home into a place of peace, feeds your soul.",
    "5": "Creativity is how you pray. Creative work lets you slip into a state where time disappears, and those hours feel closer to meditation than to a pastime. Some of your joys are private: things you make only for yourself, dreams you never share, a love you keep to yourself. Children and the playful part of you open a door to wonder, and you still feel awe at the smallest discoveries. Hidden longings can pull you towards secret romances or escapist pleasures that leave you emptier.",
    "6": "Quiet daily work is your spiritual practice. Simple, repetitive tasks and caring for someone who needs you become a form of devotion, and your mind settles while your hands are busy. You often help behind the scenes, doing the thankless tasks nobody notices until they stop being done. Your body registers unconscious stress, and you know something is wrong inside when your sleep and appetite change. Martyrdom is the danger: working yourself to exhaustion without asking for help, then feeling resentful. Your deepest peace comes once rest and self-care count as part of your service rather than a betrayal of it.",
    "7": "Partners hold up a mirror to your hidden self. Close relationships bring out fears, longings and patterns you never knew you carried, and a single argument can dredge up something from twenty years ago. You can be drawn to someone who seems to need rescuing, or to a love that feels fated and impossible to explain to friends. Even in the happiest partnership you need the right to disappear into your own world without it being taken as rejection. Dissolving into another person is the trap. Love that allows both closeness and space becomes, for you, one of the most profound forms of spiritual education.",
    "8": "Few people live as close to the depths as you do. Death, rebirth, intimacy and the hidden workings of the psyche fascinate you, and you are at ease in conversations others find far too heavy. Crises open spiritual doors, and you often come out of a loss with a sense of meaning you could not have reached any other way. Your intuition about hidden motives is sharp, at times unnervingly so. Old fears and secrets can keep a grip on you long after the event. Letting go, trusting the process of transformation and allowing buried things to surface is how you heal and deepen.",
    "9": "Something in you reaches for the transcendent. The search for ultimate meaning feeds your soul, and you feel most spiritually awake far from the familiar, or near someone who has truly lived what they believe. Solitude, distance and moments when life suddenly feels vast and open can move you to tears. Your beliefs are intensely personal and have a mystical edge you rarely share at work. Soaring ideals can make ordinary days feel flat by comparison. Faith grows solid for you when your inner search shows up as everyday kindness, not only as longing for somewhere else.",
    "10": "A sense of calling runs beneath your public life. You are often drawn to work in healing, care, charities, hospitals or institutions, or bring a quietly spiritual quality to an ordinary job. Behind your professional face there is a private self few colleagues ever meet, and you need time out of the spotlight to recover from being seen. Success can feel oddly hollow when it lacks meaning, and a promotion that should thrill you leaves you strangely flat. Hidden worries about reputation can drain you in the quiet hours. Work that serves something larger than ambition lets your inner values steer your outer life.",
    "11": "Belonging nourishes your soul. Circles of shared purpose and causes that serve people society overlooks draw you, and you feel most connected when you are one quiet pair of hands in a large compassionate effort. Certain friends feel almost fated, as if you recognised them on the first meeting, and some of them become your spiritual guides. Your hopes for the future carry an idealistic, visionary quality that others find moving. Groups that demand too much, or take your devotion for granted, can wear you thin. A community that feeds your inner life rather than using it up is one of your greatest blessings.",
    "12": "Solitude is your native element. With this house's ruler at home in its own territory, dreams, intuition and the unconscious are concentrated themes, and you need regular time alone to stay yourself. You carry a rich private world that even close friends only glimpse, and you process everything slowly, thoroughly and in silence. Retreat, prayer, meditation or simple solitude restore you like nothing else. Symbols, recurring dreams and uncanny coincidences speak loudly to you. Withdrawal can slide into isolation if you stay away too long. Trusted, your inner guidance proves remarkably wise, and people seek out your calm."
  },
};
// aspects, read through the page
window.AstroDeep.areaAspects = {
  "self:sun-moon": {
    "fusion": "What you want and what you need point the same way, and people feel that single-mindedness the moment you walk into a room. There is very little gap between your private mood and your public face: when you are happy everyone around you knows, and when you are not you cannot fake it. You start projects on instinct and throw yourself in completely, often before anyone else has noticed there was a project at all. This gives you a rare wholeness and a strong, self-generated sense of direction. The cost is a kind of blindness to yourself, because it is hard to stand outside a feeling you are made of. Other people's perspectives arrive as a surprise, sometimes years late, and they are the mirror you most need.",
    "flow": "Your head and your heart get on well, and it shows in how easily you settle into your own skin. You can decide to make a big change or end something, and your feelings catch up without a long rebellion. Friends notice that you are the same person in every mood and every setting, and that steadiness makes you easy to trust. Your parents' different ways of being in the world were, in some deep sense, compatible inside you, and you carry that peace around. Because inner conflict rarely forces the issue, you can drift along on comfort and leave ambitions untested. The friction you avoid would sharpen you, and the moments you choose it deliberately are when you grow most.",
    "tension": "Part of you wants to charge ahead while another part wants to stay home under a blanket, and you feel both at full strength. You make a bold plan one day and wake the next with a heavy reluctance you cannot argue away. Relationships and ambitions pull against each other, so choosing one can feel like betraying the other. Often you grew up between two parents who wanted different things, and you learnt to hold both inside. This inner argument is exhausting, yet it also makes you unusually self-aware: you know your moods, your contradictions and your triggers better than most. Once you stop waiting for the war to end and let each side have its turn, the tension becomes drive, and you achieve more because of it than despite it."
  },
  "mind:mercury-moon": {
    "fusion": "Your thoughts and your feelings arrive as one thing, so you rarely know what you think until you have noticed how it makes you feel. You remember conversations by their mood: the exact tone someone used, the room, the weather that afternoon. Words come out warm and personal, and people tell you things, sometimes soon after meeting you, that they have never told anyone. You learn best when a subject touches you emotionally, and dry facts slide off unless they are attached to a story. The difficulty is that a bad mood rewrites your reasoning, and a tired evening can turn a small comment into a verdict on your whole life. Your mind is at its clearest after sleep, food and a moment of quiet.",
    "flow": "Talking about feelings never embarrasses you, and you can put a name to a mood without fuss. You are the friend who says the right thing after a loss, neither too much nor too little. Your memory is excellent for anything that mattered to you, and you can recall the exact words and feelings of moments long past. Learning feels comfortable when your surroundings feel familiar and settled, and you absorb more than you realise. Instinct and logic cooperate, so your gut calls are usually well reasoned. The ease has a cost: pleasant thoughts get your attention, and the unsettling ideas that would stretch you are quietly shelved.",
    "tension": "Your head says one thing and your stomach says another, and you often speak before you have worked out which one is talking. You explain away a feeling with perfect logic, then lie awake because the feeling refuses to be persuaded. In arguments you either become coolly rational at the worst moment or say something hurt and raw you would never have planned. Studying under emotional pressure is hard for you: tension with the people close to you can wipe out days of focus. Yet this friction gives you insight into how people think and feel at odds, and you can write, counsel or teach from that gap with unusual honesty. Your clearest thinking happens in quiet moments on your own, where mind and heart finally meet."
  },
  "mind:mercury-saturn": {
    "fusion": "You think carefully, speak deliberately and distrust anything said too quickly. You often know the answer and still keep it to yourself, because being wrong in front of others feels unbearable. Your mind is built for structure: you make lists, check the facts twice and remember exactly what was promised months ago. People trust your word because you rarely give it lightly. The weight comes from a harsh inner critic that edits every sentence before you say it, and sometimes the silence wins. With age your authority grows, and the carefulness that once felt like slowness becomes the reason people ask you to review their work before anyone else sees it.",
    "flow": "Your mind has natural discipline, and you can sit with a hard problem for hours without losing the thread. You are the one who reads the fine print, finds what everyone else missed and explains it plainly. Learning is a slow build for you rather than a sprint, and what you learn stays: skills, facts and the proper way of doing things. You speak with quiet authority and people instinctively listen. Practical subjects suit you, and you often end up teaching or mentoring because your explanations are so clear. Playful, half-formed ideas get dismissed too quickly by a mind this rigorous, and some of your best thinking happens when you let yourself stay loose and unfinished for a while.",
    "tension": "Somewhere early on you were told, directly or not, that you were not clever enough, and a part of your mind still believes it. You rehearse what you will say before saying it and replay conversations afterwards, wincing at a single clumsy word. Exams, interviews and public speaking bring out a freeze that has nothing to do with what you know. You overprepare to compensate, and often become more knowledgeable than the people you once feared. That hard-won competence holds, and later in life you speak with a depth that quick talkers never reach. Once the internal examiner loosens its grip enough to let a thought out before it is perfect, your cleverness shows most in those unfinished ideas."
  },
  "mind:mercury-jupiter": {
    "fusion": "Your mind thinks big and talks bigger, and ideas arrive in whole systems rather than single thoughts. You are the one who connects today's news to history, philosophy and a half-remembered conversation from years ago, and somehow it all fits. Learning excites you, and you collect knowledge the way others collect possessions. People find you generous with knowledge and inspiring to listen to. The flip side is overpromising: you say yes to five projects, exaggerate a story for effect, or skim the details because the big picture feels more interesting. When you pair your breadth with one subject taken all the way down, you become the kind of teacher people remember for decades.",
    "flow": "Words come easily and optimism runs through how you think, so people leave a conversation with you feeling their problems are solvable. You have a knack for explaining complicated ideas in a way that makes them sound obvious. Travel, reading and conversations with people from other cultures feed your mind, and you often learn more from lived experience than from formal study. Writing, publishing, teaching or anything involving persuasion suits you. Luck follows your communication: the right words reach the right person at the right moment, an offhand comment opens a door. Charm and general knowledge carry you a long way, sometimes further than they should, and deep expertise in one field would take you further still.",
    "tension": "You have more ideas than hours and more opinions than facts to back them, and you know it. You tend to promise your time generously, then realise at the last minute that you also promised three other things. In discussions you argue a big principle and lose patience with people fussing about details, even when the details matter. Your thinking leaps, which makes you exciting to talk to and sometimes careless in writing. The strength here is intellectual appetite: you never stop wanting to understand more. Checking the small print and narrowing your focus gives your vision the credibility it deserves, and then people start funding what you imagine."
  },
  "mind:mercury-uranus": {
    "fusion": "Your mind works in flashes, and the answer often arrives complete before you can explain how you reached it. You finish other people's sentences, jump three steps ahead in any conversation, and are bored by anything taught slowly or by rote. Unusual ideas and new ways of thinking pull you in, and you tend to teach yourself what other people need lessons to learn. People call you brilliant, eccentric or occasionally exhausting. Your nervous system runs fast, so racing thoughts late at night are familiar territory. Conventional schooling rarely suited you, yet given freedom your originality is astonishing, and some of the ideas people laughed at a decade ago are the ones they now quote back to you.",
    "flow": "Original thinking is your default, and you can see a new angle on an old problem without straining. People bring you the stuck problem because you will find the workaround nobody else considered. You pick up new systems and ways of working quickly, and you enjoy explaining them to others. Your conversation is lively and a little unpredictable, full of odd facts and sudden connections. Groups and people with unusual interests sharpen your mind, and a single conversation can redirect a whole year of your thinking. Cleverness scatters easily across dozens of side interests, so the ideas that change something are the ones you stay with long enough to finish.",
    "tension": "You say the unsayable, sometimes on purpose and sometimes before you can stop yourself. In a quiet moment you drop the remark that makes everyone freeze, then wonder why the room has gone cold. Your mind is restless and contrary: tell you a rule and you immediately test it. Concentration comes in bursts, brilliant for three hours and gone for three days, and deadlines are met in a rush of last-minute genius. People find your views stimulating or abrasive, rarely neutral. This friction is also your originality, and you often see flaws in accepted thinking long before others do. The breakthrough comes when you let a disruptive idea arrive in words other people can hear."
  },
  "mind:mercury-neptune": {
    "fusion": "Your thinking is more like dreaming than filing, and images, moods and music reach you before facts do. You can walk into a room and pick up what nobody is saying, then struggle to remember where you left your keys. Imaginative and spiritual ideas speak to you directly, and you often find beautiful words without knowing where they came from. People feel understood talking to you. The difficulty is fog: dates, numbers and instructions blur, and you sometimes agree to things you did not properly hear. Others' opinions can also seep into your mind until you cannot tell which thoughts are yours. Given creative room and a few solid habits, your imagination becomes something other people treasure.",
    "flow": "Imagination and intuition feed your intelligence, and you think in pictures, metaphors and feelings as fluently as in words. You can describe a feeling or a place so that people see it, or explain a loss in a way that comforts. Creative work, and anything that translates the invisible into language, suits your mind. You pick up the emotional subtext of a message instantly and respond to what was meant. Your hunches are often right, even when you cannot justify them. Inspiration arrives so gently that you wait for it instead of chasing it, which is why some of your finest ideas stay private and never reach anyone else.",
    "tension": "Facts and fantasies blur in your mind, and you can talk yourself into believing the kinder version of events. You misread a remark, build a whole story around it, and discover days later it meant nothing. School could feel foggy, with instructions slipping past while you were somewhere else entirely. You are vulnerable to persuasive, charismatic people who promise more than they deliver, and sometimes to your own wishful thinking. Yet this same porous mind is extraordinarily imaginative and compassionate, capable of creative expression that moves others to tears. Clear structures, written notes and a trusted friend who checks your reasoning let your vision stay vivid without costing you the ground under your feet."
  },
  "love:venus-mars": {
    "fusion": "Love and desire arrive together for you: when you like someone you want them, and when you want them you are already half in love. Attraction is immediate and physical, and you often know within minutes of meeting a person whether it will happen. You flirt openly, dress to be noticed and bring heat to relationships. Romance for you is active rather than dreamy; you plan the surprise and initiate the reconciliation. The same intensity makes love volatile, with passion and irritation flaring from one source, and rows that end in bed. A partner who can match your energy and still hold steady when you burn hot is the one who keeps your heart.",
    "flow": "Giving and receiving in love are effortless for you, and your charm carries a warm, easy sexuality. You know how to pursue without pressure and how to be pursued without losing yourself. Dates with you feel relaxed and fun, and people rarely have to guess whether you are interested. You balance affection and desire well, so a long relationship keeps its spark without much effort. Shared pleasures and playful time together are how you keep love lively. Pleasure and habit can carry you into relationships you never quite chose, and the love that satisfies you is one you enter with open eyes.",
    "tension": "What you want and what you find lovely are not always the same person, and that pull shapes your love life. You fall for someone gentle, then find yourself restless for heat, or chase the exciting one who never makes you feel safe. Relationships swing between tenderness and friction, and arguments can become their own kind of intimacy. You are highly magnetic, and there is often a charge in the room when you are interested. Jealousy, competitiveness and sudden coldness come with that charge. Passion and affection can share one relationship, though it takes you a while to believe it, and when they do, the love you create is remarkably alive."
  },
  "love:moon-venus": {
    "fusion": "Tenderness is your native language in love, and you show care by making people comfortable, noticing their small needs and making sure they always feel safe with you. You need affection like other people need air, and a relationship without cuddles, small gifts and gentle words feels cold to you. People find you soft, lovely and easy to be close to. You often recreate the atmosphere of a loving home in every relationship. The risk is keeping the peace at any cost and swallowing your own needs rather than spoil a nice evening. Love that lets you be moody as well as sweet is the kind that nourishes you.",
    "flow": "You feel loved easily and you love comfortably, without fuss or games. Partners describe you as warm, affectionate and easy to live with, the one who notices when they are tired and quietly makes things easier. Your emotional needs and romantic tastes agree, so you are drawn to people who are good for you. Home and romance blend naturally: unhurried time with someone you love is your idea of luxury. You attract kindness and give it freely. Contentment is so available that a pleasant but unstretching relationship can feel like enough. Depth arrives when a partner sees the needier, less agreeable parts of you too.",
    "tension": "What you need emotionally and what you find attractive can point in different directions. You fall for glamorous, exciting or unavailable people, then crave the reliable one who stays in touch and remembers what matters to you. Sometimes you give affection freely while struggling to receive it, or you want comfort but feel restless once you have it. Early love often felt conditional, and pleasing someone came to feel like the price of being cared for. This tension gives you great sensitivity to others' needs and a talent for making people feel special. Once you trust that you deserve care without earning it, your choices in love grow calmer and far kinder to you."
  },
  "love:venus-saturn": {
    "fusion": "Love for you is serious from the start, and you do not give your heart until you have tested the ground. You are the one who waits months before saying the words, then means them for decades. Somewhere early on you learned that affection has to be earned, and you still brace for disappointment even when things are going well. Relationships often come later than for your friends, or with someone older, established or bound by duty. Loyalty is your deepest romantic quality, and people loved by you feel profoundly secure. When you allow yourself pleasure without first proving you deserve it, love softens and becomes the steady, lasting bond you were built for.",
    "flow": "You love with maturity and good sense, and your relationships are built to last. You choose partners carefully and rarely fall for someone who is plainly wrong for you. Commitment feels natural rather than frightening, and you are the partner who remembers anniversaries, keeps promises and turns up in a crisis. Love improves with time for you: the tenth year is often better than the first. People trust your affection because it is consistent. The quieter danger is choosing safety over delight, staying in a comfortable arrangement long after the romance has thinned, and letting yourself be a little foolish in love is where your heart comes most alive.",
    "tension": "Fear of rejection runs deep in your love life, and you can shut down at the very moment someone gets close. You hold back what you feel, pretend not to care, or pick the partner who is safely out of reach. Cold patches appear in relationships where affection dries up for a while, and you are rarely sure whether it was you or them. Love in your early family often felt rationed or came with rules attached. The result is a private conviction that you are hard to love, which is not true. With patience and a partner who stays, you build a love that is mature, loyal and dearly earned, often later than you hoped and stronger for the wait."
  },
  "love:venus-pluto": {
    "fusion": "Love is never casual for you; it is total, magnetic and transforming. When you fall, you fall into someone's history, their secrets and their body all at once, and you want the same depth in return. People feel an intensity from you that is hard to forget, sometimes years later. Attraction can border on obsession: thinking about them constantly, replaying every word, wanting to know everything. Jealousy and control shadow such passion, and a breakup can feel like dying. Yet love also changes you profoundly, and each serious relationship leaves you reborn. A partner who welcomes your depth rather than fearing it becomes someone you will love with astonishing loyalty.",
    "flow": "Your love has depth and staying power, and you are drawn to relationships that change both people for the better. You can talk about sex, money and fear with a partner without flinching, and that honesty builds intimacy. People find you quietly magnetic rather than showy, and attraction to you grows over time rather than fading. You have a knack for helping a partner heal old wounds just by staying present through the hard conversations. Crises deepen your relationships instead of ending them. Lighter love can bore you, yet the silly, playful evenings are what complete the depth you bring.",
    "tension": "Love has been a place of power struggles for you, and you know what it is to want someone more than is comfortable. Relationships swing between fierce closeness and cold withdrawal, and you have watched too closely, or gone silent for days, to feel in control again. Attraction is often strongest towards people who are complicated, unavailable or dangerous in some way. Betrayal, real or feared, hits you at the root. Yet you also have an extraordinary capacity for love that survives the worst and comes back truer. Each hard relationship strips away something false in you. When you let yourself be seen without armour, and choose partners who can hold your intensity, love becomes transformation rather than a battle."
  },
  "career:sun-saturn": {
    "fusion": "Your career is serious business, and you have felt the weight of responsibility since you were young. You are the one who takes the job with the long training and finishes it. Recognition comes slowly, often after years of being overlooked, and your thirties or forties usually mark a turning point. Bosses and authority figures matter enormously to you, and you have probably spent years proving yourself to a demanding parent or manager. Self-doubt pushes you to overwork and undersell yourself. Yet your standing rests on achievement, and what you build lasts. Eventually you become the authority who once intimidated you, and you carry it with quiet dignity.",
    "flow": "You have a natural sense of structure in your working life, and ambition feels steady rather than frantic. Employers notice your reliability quickly: you turn up, deliver on time and handle responsibility without drama. You understand how organisations work and climb within them steadily, often into management or roles requiring trust. Mentors appear at the right moment, and you respect proven expertise. Your sense of who you are grows alongside your work, so the later decades of your career are often your most rewarding. The trap is comfort: safe, respectable work can keep a riskier, more personal ambition waiting on the shelf for years.",
    "tension": "Your career has felt like an uphill climb, with obstacles, bad bosses or slow promotions testing your resolve. You know what it is to work twice as hard as colleagues for half the credit. Authority figures often feel like opponents, and you can clash with managers even when you respect them. Early setbacks shaped you, the kind of disappointment that arrives at the worst possible moment and teaches you to keep going. That friction built extraordinary resilience, and by middle age you are often more accomplished than those who had it easy. Fear of failure is not the same as failure, and the ground you have already won deserves far more credit than you give it."
  },
  "career:saturn-mc": {
    "fusion": "Your public direction carries weight, and you have felt called to a serious vocation for as long as you can remember. People see you as capable and responsible, sometimes even when you are young, and you are handed authority before you feel ready. Career success rarely comes quickly; it is built through years of patient effort, qualifications and proving your worth. You dread public failure, and a single professional embarrassment can haunt you. Yet your reputation, once earned, is remarkably durable. Leadership, law, government or any field requiring discipline suits you, and later in life you often become the steady name everyone in your field trusts.",
    "flow": "You approach your public life with patience and good sense, and professional progress comes steadily. You understand the long game: you take the job that teaches you properly rather than the one that pays most this year. Colleagues and bosses trust you with responsibility because you handle it calmly. Your public image is dependable, respectable and understatedly impressive. Structures that frustrate others, such as hierarchies, qualifications and procedures, work in your favour. Over the years your reputation compounds like interest. Stability suits you so well that you can stay too long in a secure role, and your most satisfying achievements come when you dare to build something of your own.",
    "tension": "Your career path has tested you, and you often feel your public direction is blocked by forces outside your control. Home and work pull against each other: family duties hold back your ambitions, or ambition costs you time with the people you love. Bosses can feel harsh, and a reputation knock early on taught you how quickly standing can be lost. You tend to feel you are running late compared with your peers. Yet this pressure builds tremendous perseverance. By working through each obstacle you gain an authority nobody can take from you, and your career often peaks later, with a lasting achievement that grew out of every setback along the way."
  },
  "career:jupiter-mc": {
    "fusion": "Your public direction is expansive and lucky, and opportunities in your career have a way of finding you. People see you as optimistic, generous and capable of big things, and doors open because of your reputation. You are drawn to work involving teaching, law, travel, publishing, spirituality or anything that widens horizons. Recognition often arrives through mentors, connections across borders or being in the right place at the right time, sometimes through a chance you very nearly let pass. You aim high and usually land somewhere good. Overreach is the catch: taking on too much, promising more than you deliver or assuming success is guaranteed. Your career flourishes when your vision is matched by consistent effort.",
    "flow": "Career growth unfolds with little strain, and you seem to be offered opportunities others have to fight for. Your optimism and generosity make you well liked at work, and colleagues often recommend you for roles you had not even applied for. You do well in fields involving education, travel, international business, publishing or advising others. Your professional reputation grows through goodwill and word of mouth, and people you worked with long ago still send opportunities your way. Mentors appear and help, and in turn you enjoy lifting others up. Luck without a clear aim can leave you drifting between offers, whereas choosing one direction turns general good fortune into a career people remember.",
    "tension": "Your ambitions are enormous, and you sometimes aim at a public role that outstrips your current resources or patience. You jump at big opportunities, then discover the fine print involves years of work. Career choices can feel torn between home and the wider world, or between what your family expected and what excites you. Overconfidence at work leads to overpromising, and a spectacular pitch sometimes lands with a thud. Still, your enthusiasm is infectious, and people back you because you believe so completely. Measuring your stride and building steadily turns your largest dreams into successes, and your reputation grows from vision into accomplishment."
  },
  "home:moon-saturn": {
    "fusion": "Emotional security did not come easily to you, and you learnt early to look after yourself. A parent was often distant, burdened or strict, and you became the sensible child who did not make a fuss. As an adult you create home through order: bills paid on time, the cupboard stocked, routines that keep chaos at bay. Showing vulnerability feels risky, so you comfort others rather than ask for comfort yourself. Loneliness can visit even in a full house. Yet your capacity for loyalty and responsibility is immense, and your family knows you will always be there. With time you soften, and the home you build becomes the safe place you once longed for.",
    "flow": "You bring stability and good sense to home life, and people feel safe in your company. You are the one who remembers birthdays, keeps the family finances straight and holds everything together during a crisis. Emotions feel manageable to you: you process them slowly and steadily rather than being swept away. Traditions, continuity and family history matter to you, and your home has a lived-in solidity. Older relatives and mentors play a supportive role in your life. You can underplay your own feelings for the sake of calm, and a little mess, spontaneity and open emotion bring warmth to the security you build so well.",
    "tension": "Home has been a place of duty and heaviness at times, and you carry a sense of responsibility for your family that feels older than you are. Growing up, you were often the one who noticed when money was short or a parent was struggling, and you tried to make yourself small. Emotionally you fear being a burden, so you go quiet rather than ask for help. Relationships with parents, mothers above all, carry old tensions. The struggle teaches you to build your own security from the ground up, very deliberately. It also means the home you eventually make is solid and yours, and your own family receives the steady care you once had to go without."
  },
  "home:moon-pluto": {
    "fusion": "Your emotional world is deep, intense and utterly private, and home is where you feel most powerfully. Family life carried secrets, strong emotions or a powerful parent whose moods filled the house. You sense undercurrents instantly: the tension behind a smile, the meaning inside a silence. You love fiercely and protect your family with total loyalty, yet fear of losing control or being betrayed makes you guard your heart. Moves, losses and upheavals at home change you profoundly, each one a kind of rebirth. Your home becomes a sanctuary where transformation happens, and the people you let in feel held at a depth few others can offer.",
    "flow": "You feel things intensely yet handle them with remarkable resilience, and your home becomes a place of emotional truth. Family crises that would break others seem to strengthen you. Relatives turn to you in serious trouble, because you do not flinch. You understand the power of emotional bonds and use it to heal rather than control. Moving house or clearing out old belongings feels cathartic, almost like shedding skin. Home does not have to be profound every day, and simple, easy comfort belongs to your security as much as any deep conversation.",
    "tension": "Home has been a battleground at times, and you know how powerful emotions can be when they are turned against you. Growing up, control, manipulation or a parent's overwhelming moods shaped the atmosphere, and you learnt to read danger before it arrived. As an adult you can swing between clinging to loved ones and pushing them away before they can hurt you. Emotional intensity runs high: a small slight at home can reopen an old wound. You are also a survivor with an extraordinary capacity for renewal. Each crisis brings a deeper understanding of yourself, and gradually you build a home where your emotions are safe and your power is your own."
  },
  "home:moon-uranus": {
    "fusion": "Your emotional life runs on its own frequency, and home is wherever you have enough freedom to breathe. Something about your family was unusual: frequent moves, an unconventional parent or sudden changes that kept everyone on edge. You need space even from people you adore, and too much closeness makes you restless. Your home is unconventional too, shared, frequently rearranged or set up in a way few other people would choose. Moods swing fast, and you can feel detached one moment and flooded the next. Your independence protects you, but it can also keep people at a distance. A home that honours freedom and closeness together gives you the security you need.",
    "flow": "Freedom and security coexist more easily in your life than for most, and you can feel at home almost anywhere. You adapt quickly to moves, new people under your roof or unexpected changes in family life. Friends become family, and your home often feels like an open, lively hub for interesting people. You are emotionally open-minded, accepting unconventional arrangements without judgement. Your space tends to have a distinctive, unconventional character that is unmistakably yours. Roots are the one thing you rarely prioritise, and one or two lasting emotional anchors give all that freedom somewhere to return to.",
    "tension": "Home life has been unpredictable, and you learnt early that security could vanish overnight. Sudden moves, a parent leaving or a family that changed shape without warning left you braced for the next shock. You crave closeness yet feel trapped when it arrives, and you have walked out of rooms, or relationships, simply to breathe. Emotions flare and vanish quickly, puzzling those close to you. Your restlessness keeps you moving house or rearranging your life in dramatic ways. The upside of so much upheaval is an adaptable, free-thinking view of what family can be. A home built on trust rather than routine gives you both the independence and the safety you need."
  },
  "growth:sun-jupiter": {
    "fusion": "Belief in yourself and belief in life are bound together, and you radiate a confidence that makes people feel things will turn out well. Opportunities seem to follow you: a chance encounter opens a new path, a single idea changes your whole direction. You are drawn to travel, philosophy, education and anything that expands your world. Generosity is part of your nature, and you share both money and wisdom freely. The flip side is excess: overconfidence, overcommitment or believing your own hype. Your deepest growth comes from turning abundance into purpose, so your natural optimism serves something larger than yourself and inspires others to grow too.",
    "flow": "Growth comes naturally to you, and life keeps offering new horizons. You find meaning easily, and you carry a strong sense that things happen for a reason and that life is on your side. Mentors, teachers and helpful strangers appear at key moments, often saying exactly what you needed to hear at exactly the moment you needed it, and you repay that luck by helping others. You are an encouraging presence, the friend who reminds everyone of the bigger picture when they are stuck in the details. Opportunities arrive steadily rather than dramatically. Blessings arriving this readily are easy to take for granted, and growth turns into wisdom once you choose where to aim it.",
    "tension": "You want more from life than your current circumstances offer, and restlessness drives much of your search for meaning. You chase the next course, the next country or the next belief system, convinced this one will be the answer. Overconfidence leads to risky leaps, and you have probably learnt through big mistakes as much as big wins. Beliefs inherited from family or culture feel too small, and you often rebel against them before finding your own. Out of that friction comes a hard-earned wisdom that is yours. Balanced with patience, your hunger for meaning becomes a lifelong adventure rather than a series of disappointments."
  },
  "growth:jupiter-saturn": {
    "fusion": "Expansion and restraint meet in you, and your growth follows a careful, deliberate rhythm. You dream big but plan precisely, and opportunities are weighed before you take them. Your beliefs are practical: faith must work in daily life, and wisdom is tested through experience. You are often drawn to building institutions, teaching structured knowledge or turning vision into lasting form. Timing matters enormously, and you tend to succeed in cycles, with growth arriving after long periods of preparation, often later than you expected and all the more solid for it. Hope and caution argue constantly inside you, yet together they produce achievements that are ambitious and durable, and wisdom that is earned rather than borrowed.",
    "flow": "You balance optimism and realism naturally, and your growth is steady, sensible and lasting. You know when to take a chance and when to wait, and your decisions about study, travel or belief are well judged. You find meaning in doing things properly: learning earned slowly, commitments seen through, a philosophy practised daily rather than merely admired. Mentors trust you, and you often become a teacher yourself, the person younger colleagues seek out for an honest view. Your faith in life is quiet but solid, and it survives disappointments that shake other people. Moderate success can feel like enough to someone this balanced; one bold leap of faith is what opens a larger horizon.",
    "tension": "Growth for you swings between leaps of hope and hard stops of doubt. You leap towards a new direction, a new plan or a new belief, then pull back when fear or practical limits intrude. Opportunities often seem to arrive at the wrong time, or come with heavy responsibilities attached. You feel caught between wanting more and being told to be realistic, often by a voice inside that sounds like a parent. Slowly, and often painfully, this teaches you to build meaning wisely. Each cycle of expansion and contraction leaves you stronger, and in time your vision and your discipline align into lasting accomplishment."
  },
};
